1868,11785-f19-hw2p2-classification,"# Description

<h1>Face Classification</h1> 
<p>Given a face image as input to your system, you have to predict the ID of the person's face. The true face image ID will be present in the training data and so the network will be doing an N-way classification to get the prediction. You are provided with the development set and can fine-tune the model based on the accuracy you get on the development set.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<h1> Evaluation Metric </h1>
The evaluation metric for this competition is the classification accuracy.

<h1> Submission Form </h1>
<p>You will submit a csv file created form the test_order_classification provided to you. The first column will be the same as the one in the file and the second column will be the class ID you predict for the given test image.</p>","# Dataset Description

<p>As mentioned in the part 2 handout, the <code>score.py</code> utility is:</p>
<pre><code>from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score
import sys
import pandas as pd

def get_auc(y_true, y_score):
    auc = roc_auc_score(y_true, y_score)
    return auc

if __name__ == '__main__':
    args = sys.argv[1:]
    if len(args) < 2:
        print ""python score.py <score_csv> <label_csv>""
        exit()
    score_csv = args[0]
    label_csv = args[1]
    y_score = pd.read_csv(score_csv).score.values
    y_true = pd.read_csv(label_csv).score.values
    auc = get_auc(y_true, y_score)
    print ""AUC: "", auc</code></pre>",True,True
1869,11785-f19-hw2p2-verification,"# Description

<h1>Face Verification</h1>
<p> An input to your system is a trial, that is, a pair of face images that may or may not belong to the same person. Given a trial, your goal is to output a numeric score that quantifies how similar the images of the two people appear to be. On some scale, a higher score will indicate higher confidence that the two images belong to one and the same person in fact. </p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is <a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/learn-forum/53782""> AUC score.</a> </p>
<h1> Submission Format </h1>
You will submit a csv file created form the trials_test provided to you. The first column will be the same as the one in the trials_test and the second column will be the similarity score you compute.","# Dataset Description

<p>You can download the data below. </p>


<p>As mentioned in the part 2 handout, the <code>score.py</code> utility is:</p>
<pre><code>from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score
import sys
import pandas as pd

def get_auc(y_true, y_score):
    auc = roc_auc_score(y_true, y_score)
    return auc

if __name__ == '__main__':
    args = sys.argv[1:]
    if len(args) < 2:
        print ""python score.py <score_csv> <label_csv>""
        exit()
    score_csv = args[0]
    label_csv = args[1]
    y_score = pd.read_csv(score_csv).score.values
    y_true = pd.read_csv(label_csv).score.values
    auc = get_auc(y_true, y_score)
    print ""AUC: "", auc</code></pre>",True,True
