1967,tj-ml-sample-competition,"# Description

<p>For this sample competition, your goal is to take the data and reverse all the 1s into 0s and the 0s into 1s. This is just so you can learn how to use Kaggle!</p>","# Dataset Description

<p>The train.csv file has your training data. In it, the first column corresponds to a some binary value (a feature) and the second value is the label (ground-truth) that you're trying to learn information from. The testing data only has a feature and your goal is to predict the label of these various data points. You should output a file similar to the sampleSubmission.csv file that has correct labels and submit it here into Kaggle. Good luck!</p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>",True,True
