1969,to-loan-or-not-to-loan-4,"# Description

This challenge aims to predict whether a loan will be payed back to the bank or not. To solve this problem, you should carefully analyze the data provided, formulate the problem accordingly to the stated goals and provide solution files to be evaluated.

**All information concerning the problem addressed can be found in the course moodle page.

Information concerning the evaluation measure and the submission files can be found in the evaluation page below.**
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is AUC (Area&nbsp;under the Curve).&nbsp;Further information regarding this metric can be found in this <a href="" https://www.kaggle.com/wiki/AreaUnderCurve"">link</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Submission Format</strong></p>
<p><strong>For every loan in the dataset</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: Id and Predicted. The first column refers to the loan_id and the Predicted value is the status predicted by your model. This status value should be either 1 (loan can be accepted) ou -1 (loan must not be accepted). Both columns are available in the file ""loan_train.csv"".</p>
<p>The submission file with your predictions should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
