1982,tjml1920-decision-trees,"# Description

<p>Your goal in this competition is to create a decision tree that is able to classify tumors as benign or malignant. Don't use any external libraries in Python other than Numpy. </p>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>training.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>testing.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ol>
<li>Clump Thickness 1 - 10</li>
<li>Uniformity of Cell Size 1 - 10</li>
<li>Uniformity of Cell Shape</li>
<li>Marginal Adhesion 1 - 10</li>
<li>Single Epithelial Cell SIze 1 - 10</li>
<li>Bare Nuclei 1 - 10</li>
<li>Bland Chromatin 1 - 10</li>
<li>Normal Nucleoli 1 - 10</li>
<li>Mitoses 1 - 10</li>
<li>Class (0 for benign, 1 for malignant)</li>
</ol>

<h2>More Info</h2>
<p> Your submission should be your predictions of the testing data in order. Each line should have the id (line number, i.e. 1, 2, 3, ...) and the class (0 or 1). Look at the sample submission for clarification. </p>",True,True
1983,ecedeeplearning2019,"# Description

<h1>ECE Paris - Deep Learning Challenge - 2019</h1>

<p>In this challenge you will be building a model that automatically determines logical entailment between two sentences.</p>
<p>You are free to handle the data as you wish, though your final submission file must be reproductible using solely your model.<p>
<p>The size of the dataset is acceptable enough to be processed correctly by your personal computer. That being said, it could be helpful to profit from free cloud computing services, like Kaggle kernels or Google Colab.</p>
<p>Any cheating strategies, like manually labelling the test dataset, would lead to a disqualification and a minimal final grade.</p>
Remember that final evaluation will be based on ranking, quality of code and ideas.
----------------------
# Evaluation

<h2>Goal</h2>
<p>The goal of this InClass competition is to predict the right logical entailment for each sentences couple. Note that the dataset is clearly balanced between all the classes. For every index in the test set, you should predict the correct label, which can only take one of the following three values: contradiction, neutral or entailment.</p>
<h2>Metric</h2>
<p>Since the dataset is balanced, this competition is evaluated on the categorization accuracy of your predictions (the percentage of logical entailments you get correct).</p>
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p>For each index in the test set, you must predict a label.</p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>index,label<br />0,contradiction<br /><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">1,neutral<br />2,entailment<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">3,contradiction<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">etc.</span></pre>","# Dataset Description

<h2>Files descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>dataset_train.csv</strong> - CSV file containing the 392 663 training samples with their labels</li>
<li><strong>dataset_test_no_labels.csv</strong> - CSV file containing the 19 648 test samples</li>
<li><strong>example_submission_test.csv</strong> - a dummy submission test CSV in the correct format as example</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>index</strong> - sample id to be classified</li>
<li><strong>sentence_1</strong> - first sentence of the pair</li>
<li><strong>sentence_2</strong> - second sentence of the pair</li>
<li><strong>label</strong> - category to predict among 3 possible classes</li>
</ul>",True,True
1984,spvfirstdatasciencecompetition,"# Description

Esta ¨¦ a primeira competi??o de Ci¨ºncia de Dados e Machine Learning da comunidade SPV de empreendedores de Minas Gerais.

Como abertura e primeiro contato com este tipo de competi??o, escolhemos uma base simples e bastante utilizada em *papers*: IMDB dataset.

Trata-se de uma base criada pela universidade de Stanford (http://ai.stanford.edu/~amaas/data/sentiment/) contendo 50 mil reviews de filmes realizados por usu¨¢rios do site IMDB. Estas reviews foram organizadas e rotuladas entre positivas e negativas.

O objetivo desta competi??o ¨¦ criar e treinar um modelo com a base de treino para que possa realizar a predi??o de reviews positivas e negativas na base de teste.

Como se pode perceber, ser¨¢ necess¨¢rio a utiliza??o de t¨¦cnicas de NLP (*Natural Language Processing*) para a resolu??o do problema.

O objetivo desta primeira competi??o ¨¦ o aprendizado! A classifica??o ser¨¢ importante para que a habilidade de cada um seja explorada mas o principal foco ¨¦ que todos possam aprender as t¨¦cnicas e, com o tempo, aumentarem sua pontua??o. Logo, n?o deixem de participar do f¨®rum com d¨²vidas e questionamentos ou compartilharem seus *notebooks* com dicas para os colegas.
----------------------
# Evaluation

A m¨¦trica de avalia??o para esta competi??o ¨¦ o <a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/wiki/MeanFScore"">F1-Score M¨¦dio</a>. 

O F1 score, bastante utilizado em recupera??o de informa??o, mede a acur¨¢cia utilizando as estat¨ªsticas precis?o (p) e recall (r). A precis?o ¨¦ a taxa dos verdadeiros positivos (tp) por todos os valores preditos positivamente (tp + fp). Recall ¨¦ a taxa dos verdadeiros positivos por todos os atuais positivos (tp + fn).

O F1 score ¨¦ dado por:
<p>\[ F1 = 2\frac{p \cdot r}{p+r}\ \ \mathrm{onde}\ \ p = \frac{tp}{tp+fp},\ \ r = \frac{tp}{tp+fn} \]</p>

A m¨¦trica F1 balanceia os pesos recall e precis?o igualmente. E um bom algoritmo de recupera??o de informa??o ir¨¢ maximizar precis?o e recall simultaneamente. Assim, uma boa performance em ambos ser¨¢ mais favorecida do que uma excelente performance em um e ruim performance em outro.

Formato de submiss?o:
O arquivo de submiss?o deve conter 2 colunas em formato csv exatamente como mostrado a seguir:

Id,Predicted
0,1
1,1
2,1
3,1
4,1
5,1
6,1
7,1
8,1
9,1
10,1
....
24997,0
24998,0
24999,1","# Dataset Description

Base treino.csv:
base a ser utilizada para treino e valida??o.

- ""id"": id de cada usu¨¢rio que realizou o coment¨¢rio
- ""review"": coment¨¢rio do filme realizado por cada usu¨¢rio
- ""sentiment"": 1 como avalia??o positiva e 0 como avalia??o negativa

Base teste.csv:
base a ser utilizada para teste cujo resultado deve ser submetido.

- ""id"": id de cada usu¨¢rio que realizou o coment¨¢rio
- ""review"": coment¨¢rio do filme realizado por cada usu¨¢rio",True,True
1985,gis-iii-machine-learning-lab-2019,"# Description

Bike sharing systems allows automated bike renting and returning via a network of kiosk located throughout the city. The data generated by these systems is explicitly recorded and could be used for analysis. Bike sharing systems therefore function as a sensor network, which can be used for studying mobility in a city. Now, we have collected the historical usage patterns with weather data and decided to use it for forecasting bike rental demand in the city.
<hr>

###Acknowledgements
The dataset used in this lab was provided by Hadi Fanaee Tork using the data from Capital Bikeshare.
[Fanaee-T, Hadi, and Gama, Joao, Event labeling combining ensemble detectors and background knowledge, Progress in Artificial Intelligence (2013): pp. 1-15, Springer Berlin Heidelberg.].

Icons made by Freepik from www.flaticon.com is licensed by CC 3.0 BY
----------------------
# Evaluation

<h2>Evaluation</h2>
Submissions are evaluated one the Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE). You could find your submission scores in **public leaderboard** (calculated with 40% of the test data) and **private leaderboard** (calculated with 60% of the test data after the deadline of this competition).

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p>Your submission file must have a header and should be structured in the following format:</p>
<pre>datetime,count<br />2011-01-20 00:00:00,0<br /><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">2011-01-20 01:00:00,0<br />2011-01-20 02:00:00,0<br />....<br />....</span></pre>","# Dataset Description

<h3>Data Sources </h3>
-  <b>train.csv</b> : Contains the training data that you need.  
</br>
-  <b>test_withoutLabel.csv </b> : Contains the data that you need to predict. The prediction results need to be submitted for the in-class competition.  
</br>
-  <b>sampleSubmission.csv </b>: A sample of what you should upload for the competition. The sample submission file contains the results from a dummy model.",True,True
