Descripci¨®n de campos
---------------------
- Empleado 0=Desempleado, 1=Empleado actualmente.
- Tiempo_empleado: N¨²mero de a?os que lleva en el empleo actual (si aplica).
- Saldo_cuenta: Saldo en miles de pesos de la cuenta principal con el banco.
- Valor_pr¨¦stamo: Valor actual que adeuda en pr¨¦stamos en el sistema financiero.
- Cuentas_otros: N¨²mero de cuentas que tiene en otros bancos.
- Autocontrol: Mediante una prueba escrita se mide el nivel de autocontrol de la persona, en puntaje de 0 a 100.
- Impulsividad: Mediante una prueba escrita se mide el nivel de impulsividad de la persona, en puntaje de 0 a 100.
- Confianza: Mediante una prueba escrita se mide el nivel de confianza en s¨ª misma de la persona, en puntaje de 0 a 100.
- Incumplimiento: 0=Cumplimiento; 1=Incumplimiento.",True,True
2009,ucfai-dsg-fa19-default,"# Description

Perhaps the most common and popular application of data science is in the financial world. For years, loan providers have had to work on intuition (and perhaps intelligence of underemployed math majors) to determine who should and should not be receiving a loan. But now days, we can use fancy statistics and machine learning to determine who will default on a loan.
----------------------
# Evaluation

This competition will use a ""Receiver Operating Characteristic Area Under Curve (ROC AUC) metric to evaluate your submissions. In plain English, this means that your score is based on the ratio of your true positives vs your false positives.","# Dataset Description

You will be predicting ""GOOD_STANDING"" using the data available from lending tree's loan dataset. A loan in good standing is any loan that has not been charged off, defaulted, or is late. We represent a loan in good standing with a ""1"" and all other loans with a ""0""

There are quite a few features in this dataset, so check out LCDataDictionary for a description of the different features! Note, ""loan_status"" is removed in both the train and test, as this feature was consolidated for the ""GOOD_STANDING"" target.

Good luck!",True,True
