 - Multiple choice single response questions fit into individual columns whereas multiple choice multiple response questions were split into multiple columns. Text responses were encoded to protect user privacy and countries with fewer than 50 respondents were grouped into the category ""other"".",False,False
2022,cs6601ai-fall19-assign4-bonus,"# Description

<p>This is a competition for bonus points on Assignment 4 for the CS 6601 Fall 2019 Artificial Intelligence Class at Georgia Tech.</p>

<p>You need to generate the labels for the test dataset by using the training dataset and by using only classifier(s) composed of Random Forests or Decision trees. The file <strong>generate_kaggle_submission.py</strong> does the task of calling your Challenge Classifier and generating an output file <strong>kaggle_result.csv</strong> to upload to Kaggle for this competition.</p>

<h2>Bonus Points Metric:</h2>
<p>All bonus points will be added to your Assignment 4 grades.</p>
<p>First place: 15 bonus points</p>
<p>Second place: 12 bonus points</p>
<p>Third place: 10 bonus points</p>
<p>Everyone else who achieves an accuracy of more than 90%: 7 bonus points</p>","# Dataset Description

<p>Download the given files in your Assignment 4 folder.</p>

<p>Please download the files as .zip files and the extract the csv files from them.</p>

<ul>
<li>The <strong>kaggle_train_2019_fall.csv</strong> file contains the given instances for training your binary classifier. First column as class, and the rest as features</li>
<li>The <strong>kaggle_test_2019_fall_unlabelled.csv</strong> file contains the test set with no class labels</li>
<li>The <strong>generate_kaggle_submission.py</strong> file needs to be run to train your Challenge classifier on the given training data and generate a <strong>kaggle_result.csv</strong> file to be uploaded to the Kaggle competition.</li>
</ul>",True,True
2023,subscription-of-a-term-depositdav,"# Description

<p>In this competition the idea is to predict if a customer would accept an offer of a term deposit or not. For this purpose, the data set contains demographic, social and financial data and the result of similar offers in the past. 
The competition is about making the best model for the classification problem measure by AUC. 
</p>
<h2>Acknowledgements</h2>
<p>This information is not real and was made for the class.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is <a href=""https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic""> AUC</a>. 
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For every author in the dataset</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: ID and y. 
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>ID,y<br />1,1<br /><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">2,1<br />3,0<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">4,1<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">etc.</span></pre>","# Dataset Description

<p>
This collection of data is about a marketing campaign of term deposit to a random set of customers of a bank. Now we want to know how the new customers would behave to the same offer in order to prioritize them.
</p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
<li><strong>description.txt</strong> - supplemental information about the data</li>
</ul>",True,True
