2088,tjml-2019-20-random-forests,"# Description

<p>Welcome to the (surprise) second competition of the year! Write a random forest to classify the data. More info available <a href=""https://tjmachinelearning.com/competitions/1920"">here.</a></p>
<p> No external libraries allowed other than numpy and pandas. Competition closes at 11:59 PM on 10/29/19. </p>

----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>Submissions evaluated using the <a href=""https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic"">area under the ROC score.</a> </p>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the testing set</li>
<li><strong>sample.csv</strong> - a sample csv file in the correct submission format</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data fields</h2>
<h3>Features</h3>
<ol>
<li>Ticket class: 1=1st, 2=2nd, 3=3rd</li>
<li>Sex: 0=male, 1=female</li>
<li>Age in years</li>
<li># of siblings/spouses aboard the Titanic</li>
<li># of parents/children aboard the Titanic</li>
<li>Passenger fare</li>
<li>Port of Embarkation: 0=Southampton, 1=Cherbourg, 2=Queenstown</li>
</ol>
<h3>Classes</h3>
<ul>
<li>1=survived</li>
<li>0=did not survive</li>
</ul>

<h2>More Info</h2>
