2165,ufcg-cdp-classificacao-20192,"# Description

# Introdu??o

Nesse problema, utilizaremos o Kaggle para avaliar os modelos dos alunos. ¨¦ necess¨¢ria ao menos uma submiss?o.

O problema consiste em elaborar modelos preditivos de classifica??o para a predi??o do resultado de uma partida de futebol de uma rodada dos maiores campeonatos europeus. Nessa competi??o ser¨¢ utilizado o conjunto de dados que cont¨¦m as temporadas 2012-13, 2013-14, 2014-15 e 2015-16 como treino, 2016-17 e 2017-18 como teste.

O Leaderboard p¨²blico ¨¦ computado com uma certa porcentagem dos dados de teste. O ranking final ser¨¢ computado com o restante dos dados, e ser?o mantidos privados at¨¦ o deadline da competi??o. Fique atento, pois o ranking do Leaderboard p¨²blico pode n?o **corresponder ao resultado final**.

# Sobre a submiss?o

A submiss?o deve ser feita de acordo com o exemplo dado no `sample_submission.csv`. A coluna ID representa a coluna ID presente em ambos os conjuntos de dados. A coluna Result representa o resultado da partida.
----------------------
# Evaluation

As predi??es geradas pelos modelos ser?o avaliadas com a m¨¦trica Acur¨¢cia.","# Dataset Description

# Data description

## Teams Identifiers
- ID: Unique identifier for row
- League: League which the match was played (England, Germany, Italy or Spain)
- Date: Date of the match
- HomeTeam: Home team of the match
- AwayTeam: Visitor team of the match

## Teams Stats
- HS: Home team shots
- AS: Visitor team shots
- HST: Home team shots on target
- AST: Visitor team shots on target
- HF: Home team faults
- AF: Visitor team faults
- HC: Home team corners
- AC: Visitor team corners
- HY: Home team yellow cards
- AY: Visitor team yellow cards
- HR: Home team red cards
- AR: Visitor team red cards

## Bet Stats
Each row below describes the probability, according to the bets, of each team winning. Lets look to B365: B365H is the probability for the home team to win, B365D is the probability for a draw, and B365A is the probability for the visitor team to win.

- B365H
- B365D
- B365A
- BWH
- BWD
- BWA
- IWH
- IWD
- IWA
- LBH
- LBD
- LBA
- PSH
- PSD
- PSA
- WHH
- WHD
- WHA
- VCH
- VCD
- VCA

The variables below are also related to bets:

- BbMx>2.5: Betbrain maximum over 2.5 goals
- BbAv>2.5: Betbrain average over 2.5 goals
- BbMx<2.5: Betbrain maximum under 2.5 goals
- BbAv<2.5: Betbrain average over 2.5 goals

## Target variable
- Result: Result of the match, 0 when Visitor team wins, 1 when draw, 2 when Home team wins",True,True
2166,datms,"# Description

<p>This competition is for the 9/23 cohort of the Morgan Stanley Part Time Data Science Course</p>

<h2>Purpose</h2>
<p>You will be using a dataset derived from the Lending Club competition and trying to determine if you can accurately predict if a loan is going to default or not:</p>
<pre>Use any modeling, ensembling , feature engineering and selection techniques to try and maximize your prediction accuracy</pre>
<pre>The target is the Account Loan Status column</pre>
<pre>Work individually or in teams of 2/3, you can make a maximum of 5 submissions a day. Make sure to include the names of the participants in your time. Check the leaderboard to see who is winning</pre>
<p>Note: Make sure that the submission file format is the same as the example provided. Use the Id column as the index</p>
<p>Note: You can make a total of 5 submissions a day </p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation pages describes how submissions will be scored and how students should format their submissions. You don't need a sub-title at the top (the page title appears above). For an example of a high quality evaluation page, see the 2013 KDD Cup page, which we have copied here:</p>
<hr />
<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is <a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/wiki/MeanFScore""> Mean F1-Score</a>. The F1 score, commonly used in information retrieval, measures accuracy using the statistics precision p and recall r. Precision is the ratio of true positives (tp) to all predicted positives (tp + fp). Recall is the ratio of true positives to all actual positives (tp + fn). The F1 score is given by:</p>
<p>\[ F1 = 2\frac{p \cdot r}{p+r}\ \ \mathrm{where}\ \ p = \frac{tp}{tp+fp},\ \ r = \frac{tp}{tp+fn} \]</p>
<p>The F1 metric weights recall and precision equally, and a good retrieval algorithm will maximize both precision and recall simultaneously. Thus, moderately good performance on both will be favored over extremely good performance on one and poor performance on the other.</p>
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For every author in the dataset</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: AuthorId and DuplicateAuthorIds. DuplicateAuthorIds should be a space-delimited list. Every AuthorId counts as his/her own duplicate, and every duplicate should be listed under each of its respective ids.?For example, if you suspect author A, B, and C are the same, you should list (A,A B C), (B,B A C), (C,C A B).</p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>AuthorId,DuplicateAuthorIds<br />1,1<br /><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">8,8<br />9,9 10<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">10,10 9<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">etc.</span></pre>","# Dataset Description

<p>The data below is a subset of the data provided during the Lending Club Competition. 

<p>For convenience, you have been provided both a training and a testing dataset.<p>
<p>The testing dataset does not include the target variable. The columns names should be self explanatory. The purpose of this competition is to accurately predict if a loan will default. <p>

<p>Please review the sample submission file for the format in which your result submissions need to be in. You will be graded on the accuracy of your predictions. .</p>",True,True
