2273,mba2019,"# Description

In this competition, you are provided with historical book sales data. The challenge is to forecast book sales for next month. To make good predictions, you need to create excellent features and models.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated by <a href=""https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root-mean-square_deviation"">root mean square error (RMSE)</a>. True target values are clipped into [0,20] range.
<h3>Submission Format</h3>
For each item_id in the test set, you must predict a total number of sales. The submission file should contain a header and have the following format:
<pre>item_id,item_cnt_month<br />100000,0.5<br /><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">100011,1.5<br />100048,2.5<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">100058,3.5<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">etc.</span></pre>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set. Book sales data from January 2014 to November 2014.</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set. List of books to forecast sales for December 2014.</li>
</ul>",True,True
