2315,ds8-which-whiskey,"# Description

Glasses High!

Can you predict the type of whiskey based on the review? The data is scraped from the Whiskey Advocate.

We will be evaluating submissions on classification accuracy.

### Types of Whiskey
    1    Scotch
    2    Bourbon/Tennessee
    3    Craft Whiskey
    4    Canadian","# Dataset Description

Whisky Advocate Insights from Reviews What makes a great whiskey? It is a smoky flavor? It is peaty? Is it something else?

There isn't a single truth of a great whisky, because tastes vary so much from person to person. However, we can analyze the reviews of experts to see if we can detect patterns in the flavor profiles of 'great' whiskys.

File descriptions 
train.csv  - the training set 
test.csv - the test set 
sample_submission.csv - a sample submission file in the correct format 

Data fields 
description - the text of the whiskey review",True,True
2316,bangla-money-recognition,"# Description

**Online Submission Deadline**
14 December 2019 23:59 PM BD. By this time you can submit multiple times.

<p>Maximum team member is two. Winners' team need to give a presentation about how the work was done.
The presentation will be held on 15 December at ICT Fest, NEUB
</p>

Dataset: [Use this link](https://www.kaggle.com/nsojib/bangla-money)

Test data: There are 333 images of 9 classs [1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 500, 1000 ]

**### [Important] How to load Test data. Read this way to maintain the sequence.**
<pre>
import os
path='E:\Testing'
test_files= [os.path.join(path,f) for f in os.listdir(path) if f.endswith('.jpg')]
print(test_files[:10]) #printing first 10 files.
#Write your code here to load all the test images from filename.

sps=[ im.replace(path+'\\', '')  for im in test_files]
y_actual=array( [  sp[:sp.index('_')] for sp in sps], dtype=int)
print(y_actual[:10])
#Calculate accuracy by compairing with y_actual
</pre>



