</p>

----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>We use accuracy as the metric. </p>
<p>The evaluation metric is \[ accuracy = \frac{\#\text{correctly predicted samples}}{\#\text{all samples}} \]</p>","# Dataset Description

<p>The task is to predict the relationship of two sentence: sent1 and sent2. There are three candidate relations: contradiction, entailment, and neutral. You need to determine the relation between them. </p>
<p>You are given 20000 sentence pairs for training, 5000 sentence pairs for testing.</p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.txt</strong> - format: id \t sent1 \t sent2 \t label \n (Note: splited by \t and the last char is \n)</li>
<li><strong>eval.txt</strong> - format: id \t sent1 \t sent2 \n (Note: splited by \t and the last char is \n)</li>
<li><strong>sample_submission.csv</strong> - format: id \t label. The ids are from the eval.txt.</li>
</ul>

<p>We use accuracy as the metric. </p>
<p>\[ accuracy = \frac{\#\text{correctly predicted samples}}{\#\text{all samples}} \]</p>",True,True
