2358,11-785-winter-2019-hw2p2-classification,"# Description

# Face Classification

Given a face image as input to your system, you have to predict the ID of the person's face. The true face image ID will be present in the training data and so the network will be doing an N-way classification to get the prediction. You are provided with the development set and can fine-tune the model based on the accuracy you get on the development set.
----------------------
# Evaluation

# Evaluation Metric

The evaluation metric for this competition is the classification accuracy.

# Submission Form

You will submit a csv file created form the test_order_classification provided to you. The first column will be the same as the one in the file and the second column will be the class ID you predict for the given test image.","# Dataset Description

# Dataset
The dataset is available at www.kaggle.com/dataset/8a99a96b764d822da11ce50c9ce9d7a69f5064989c4347b382d3217e7897c2f9 and a sample submission is attached below.",True,True
2359,11-785-winter-2019-hw2p2-verification,"# Description

# Face Verification

An input to your system is a trial, that is, a pair of face images that may or may not belong to the same person. Given a trial, your goal is to output a numeric score that quantifies how similar the images of the two people appear to be. On some scale, a higher score will indicate higher confidence that the two images belong to one and the same person in fact.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric is the [AUC score](https://www.kaggle.com/learn-forum/53782).

# Submission Format

You will submit a csv file created form the trials test provided to you. The first column will be the same as the one in the trials test and the second column will be the similarity score you compute.","# Dataset Description

# Dataset
The dataset is available at www.kaggle.com/dataset/8a99a96b764d822da11ce50c9ce9d7a69f5064989c4347b382d3217e7897c2f9 and the sample submission is attached below.",True,True
