2438,mars-traffic-violation-forecast,"# Description

<h2>Traffic Violation Forecast</h2>

<p>Given the history traffic violation data, traffic volume (could be extracted from driving behavior data), and POI data, predict the future traffic violations.</p>
<p>Some feature data have been extracted (see features.zip), you can use these features or create your own feature data.</p>
<p>You can determine a time span yourself. The given features are based on 5 minutes. Since the traffic violation data are sparse, there are many 0 values, so you may choose a longer time span, like 15 minutes or more.</p>
<p>Have fun ^_^</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>Up to you.</p>","# Dataset Description

<p>There are three  traffic violation datasets, turning.db, parking.db and speeding.db, corresponding to three different types of traffic violations, illegal turning, illegal parking and speeding in two cities, Xiamen (2016-09-01 00:00:00 ~ 2016-10-01 00:00:00) and Chengdu (2016-11-01 00:00:00 ~ 2016-12-01 00:00:00). The driving behavior dataset, behavior.db, contains driving behavior information in two cities. </p>

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>parking.db</strong> - the illegal parking behavior dataset</li>
<li><strong>speeding.db</strong> - the speeding behavior dataset</li>
<li><strong>turning.db</strong> - the illegal turning behavior dataset</li>
<li><strong>behavior.db</strong> - the driving behavior dataset</li>
<li><strong>features.zip</strong> - some features extracted from above datasets</li>
</ul>
Please download behavior.db from the following link:
https://pan.baidu.com/s/1exeiXWab6n7DcL-8TpS_pQ
<h2>Table descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<h3>parking.db</h3>
<li><strong>illegal_parking_chengdu/xiamen</strong> - illegal parking behaviors in Chengdu or Xiamen</li>
<li><strong>parking_locations_cd/xm</strong> - the locations of illegal parking behaviors in Chengdu or Xiamen</li>
<h3>speeding.db</h3>
<li><strong>speeding_chengdu/xiamen</strong> - speeding behaviors in Chengdu or Xiamen</li>
<li><strong>speeding_chengdu/xiamen_count</strong> - the number of speeding behaviors on each road in Chengdu or Xiamen</li>
<h3>turning.db</h3>
<li><strong>illegal_turning_chengdu/xiamen</strong> - illegal turning behaviors in Chengdu or Xiamen</li>
<li><strong>illegal_tn_lid_cd/xm</strong> - illegal lid in Chengdu or Xiamen</li>
<h3>behavior.db</h3>
<li><strong>behavior_cd/xm</strong> - driving behaviors in Chengdu or Xiamen</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<h3>illegal_parking_chengdu/xiamen</h3>
<li><strong>npk_id</strong> - the unique id of a no parking area</li>
<li><strong>lat</strong> - the latitude of the parking behavior (wgs84)</li>
<li><strong>lng</strong> - the longitude of the parking behavior (wgs84)</li>
<li><strong>st_ts</strong> - the start time of the parking behavior</li>
<li><strong>ed_ts</strong> - the end time of the parking behavior</li>
<li><strong>confidence</strong> - the confidence of  the parking behavior</li>
<li><strong>road_id</strong> - the road is of the parking behavior</li>
<li><strong>center_ts<strong> - the center time of the parking behavior, center_ts=(st_ts+ed_ts)/2 </li>

<h3>parking_locations_cd/xm</h3>
<li><strong>npk_id</strong> - the unique id of the no parking area</li>
<li><strong>latitude</strong> - the latitude of the center of the no parking area</li>
<li><strong>longitude</strong> - the longitude of the center of the no parking area</li>

<h3>chengdu/xiamen_speeding</h3>
<li><strong>ind</strong> - the unique id of the speeding behavior</li>
<li><strong>speed</strong>- the speed of the speeding behavior</li>
<li><strong>speed_limit1</strong> - the speed limit of the road from data source 1</li>
<li><strong>speed_limit2</strong> - the speed limit of the road from data source 2</li>
<li><strong>road_id</strong> - the road segment id of the speeding behavior</li>
<li><strong>ts_1</strong> - the start time of the speeding behavior</li>
<li><strong>ts_2</strong> - the end time of the speeding behavior</li>
<li><strong>pid1</strong> - the unique id of the start crossing of the speeding behavior</li>
<li><strong>pid2</strong> - the unique id of the end crossing of the speeding behavior</li>
<li><strong>ts_m</strong> - the center time of the speeding behavior, ts_m=(ts_1+ts_2)/2</li>

<h3>chengdu/xiamen_speeding_count</h3>
<li><strong>road_id</strong> - the unique road segment id</li>
<li><strong>pid1</strong> - the unique id of the start crossing of the road segment</li>
<li><strong>pid2</strong> - the unique id of the end crossing of the road segment</li>
<li><strong>lat</strong> - the latitude of the center of the road segment (wgs84)</li>    
<li><strong>lng</strong> - the longitude of the center of the road segment (wgs84)</li>
<li><strong>road_name</strong> - the name of the road</li>

<h3>illegal_turning_chengdu/xiamen</h3>
<li><strong>traj_id</strong> - the unique trajectory id</li>
<li><strong>timestamp</strong> - the time of the illegal turning behavior</li>
<li><strong>longitude</strong> - the longitude of the illegal turning behavior (wgs84)</li>
<li><strong>latitude</strong> - the latitude of the illegal turning behavior (wgs84)</li>
<li><strong>behavior</strong> - the type of the illegal turning behavior</li>
<li><strong>bearing_before</strong> - the direction of the vehicle before the illegal turning behavior</li>
<li><strong>bearing_after</strong> - the direction of the vehicle after the illegal turning behavior</li>
<li><strong>confidence</strong> - the confidence of the illegal turning behavior</li>
<li><strong>lid</strong> - the unique id of the illegal turning behavior</li>
<li><strong>pid</strong> - the unique id of the crossing where the illegal turning behavior happened</li>

<h3>illegal_tn_lid_cd/xm</h3>
<li><strong>lid</strong> - the unique id of the illegal turning behavior</li>
<li><strong>pid</strong> - the unique id of the crossing where the illegal turning behavior happened</li>
<li><strong>longitude</strong> - the longitude of the illegal turning behavior (wgs84)</li>
<li><strong>latitude</strong> - the latitude of the illegal turning behavior (wgs84)</li>
<li><strong>behavior</strong> - the type of the illegal turning behavior</li>
<li><strong>num</strong> - the number of the illegal turning behavior corresponding to lid</li>
<li><strong>sign_conf</strong> - the confidence of the corresponding traffic sign</li>
<li><strong>lon_bd</strong> - the longitude of the turning behavior (bd09)</li>
<li><strong>lat_bd</strong> - the latitude of the turning behavior (bd09)</li>

<h3>behavior_cd/xm</h3>
<li><strong>traj_id</strong> - the unique trajectory id</li>
<li><strong>timestamp</strong> - the time of the driving behavior</li>
<li><strong>longitude</strong> - the longitude of the driving behavior (wgs84)</li>
<li><strong>latitude</strong> - the latitude of the driving behavior (wgs84)</li>
<li><strong>behavior</strong> - the type of the driving behavior</li>
<li><strong>bearing_before</strong> - the direction of the vehicle before the behavior</li>
<li><strong>bearing_after</strong> - the direction of the vehicle after the behavior</behavior</li>
<li><strong>confidence</strong> - the confidence of the driving behavior</li>
<li><strong>pid</strong> - the unique id of the location where the driving behavior happened</li>
<li><strong>lid</strong> - the unique id of the driving behavior</li>
<li><strong>road_id</strong> - the unique id of the road where the driving behavior happened</li>
</ul>

<h2>feature.zip</h2>
same for xiamen and chengdu
<h3>speeding</h3> 
<ul>
<li><strong>poi</strong> - indexed by road_id (filename), a 1*5 vector for each road_id (['business','accommodation','entertainment','infrastructure','tourism']), each value represents the number of the corresponding POIs within 200m from the center of the road segment (extracted from chengdu/xiamen_poi.db ).
<li><strong>traffic_volume</strong> - indexed by road_id (filename), a 1*8641 vector for each road_id, sum(confidence) of behaviors on two crossing of this road segment (pid1, pid2) every 5 minutes (extracted from behavior.db).
<li><strong>traffic_violation</strong> - indexed by road_id (filename), a 1*8641 vector for each road_id, the number of speeding on this road segment every  5 minutes (extracted from speeding.db).
</ul>
<h3>parking</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>poi</strong> - indexed by npk_id (filename), a 1*5 vector for each npk_id (['business','accommodation','entertainment','infrastructure','tourism']), each value represents the number of the corresponding POIs within 200m from the center of the no parking area (extracted from chengdu/xiamen_poi.db ).
<li><strong>traffic_volume</strong> - indexed by npk_id (filename), a 1*8641 vector for each npk_id, sum(confidence) of behaviors on this road segment (road_id) every 5 minutes (extracted from behavior.db).
<li><strong>traffic_violation</strong> - indexed by npk_id (filename), a 1*8641 vector for each npk_id, sum(confidence) of  illegal parking behaviors on this no parking area segment every  5 minutes (extracted from parking.db).
</ul>
<h3>turning</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>poi</strong> - indexed by lid (filename), a 1*5 vector for each lid (['business','accommodation','entertainment','infrastructure','tourism']), each value represents the number of the corresponding POIs within 200m from the location of the lid (extracted from chengdu/xiamen_poi.db ).
<li><strong>traffic_volume</strong> - indexed by lid (filename), a 1*8641 vector for each lid, sum(confidence) of behaviors in this crossing (pid) every 5 minutes.
<li><strong>traffic_violation</strong> - indexed by lid (filename), a 1*8641 vector for each lid,  sum(confidence) of this type of  illegal turning behavior in this crossing (lid) every  5 minutes (here only consider the confidence of behaviors, you can add the confidence of corresponding traffic sign as well).
</ul>",True,True
