2470,data-science-nigeria-instagram-marketing-ad,"# Description

### CORAY GROUP AD CONVERSION RATE PREDICTION

<p>Coray Inc. is a registered beverage seller that wants to run a new Instagram marketing campaign. They have done multiple campaigns in the past and wants you to build a machine learning model to help them predict total conversions. Features about the ad and the user, plus the duration of the campaign is provided.</p>

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
<li><strong>data_desc.csv</strong> - supplemental information about the data</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>id:</strong> ""Unique identifier for the nstances""</li>
    <li><strong>ad_start:</strong> ""The start date of the advert campaign""</li>
    <li><strong>ad_end:</strong>  ""The end date of the advert campaign""</li>
    <li><strong>campaign_id:</strong>  ""The unique campaign identifier""</li>
     <li><strong>ig_campaign_id:</strong>  ""Unique ID assigned by Instagram""</li>
     <li><strong>age:</strong> ""The age range of the target users""</li>
     <li><strong>sex: </strong> ""The gender of the target user""</li>
     <li><strong>interest1:</strong>  ""Anonymized interest1 of the target user""</li>
     <li><strong>interest2:</strong>  ""Anonymized interest2 of the target user""</li>
     <li><strong>interest3:</strong>  ""Anonymized interest3 of the target user""</li>
     <li><strong>impressions:</strong> ""impressions are the total number of times your content could have been seen""</li>
     <li><strong>no_clicks: </strong> ""Number of times the post was clicked""</li>
     <li><strong>money_spent:</strong>  ""Amount of money in USD spent on the advert""</li>
     <li><strong>total_conversion (Target feature):</strong>  ""The conversion rate is the percentage of people who took an action such as filling out a lead form, making a purchase.""</li>
</ul>
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is the [Mean Absolute Error](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_absolute_error). The Mean Absolute Error, commonly used in information retrieval, measures the error rate between the predicted class and the true/ground class. 

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For every ad in the dataset</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: ad_id and total_conversion.</p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>ad_id,total_conversion<br />779608,2<br /><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">779634,8<br />536526,6<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">452467,10<br /></span></pre>","# Dataset Description

