The teams mentioned above must fill this [form](https://forms.gle/ARtwLRShpf1zuzWd7)","# Dataset Description

<p>You are provided with a training set and a test set of images. The dataset comprises of 7 classes. There are 7,696 training images and 3,675 test images. The goal of the competition is to create a classifier capable of determining the class of the image from a photo. </p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>data_images.zip</strong> - contains two folders: train (which contains the training images) and test (which contains the test images). </li>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - A csv file containing two fields: <b>image</b>, which corresponding to name of the image (which is present in the train folder) and <b>label</b> which corresponds to the class to which the image belongs to.</li>
<li><strong>sample_submission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
<li><strong>mnist_train_56x56_grayscale.csv</strong> - The images in the train folder are resized to 56*56 (then flattened) and the pixel values are stored in this csv file. The first column corresponds to name of the image followed by 3136 columns containing the pixel value of the corresponding images. For the label of the image refer to train.csv</li>
<li><strong>mnist_test_56x56_grayscale.csv</strong> - The images in the test folder are resized to 56*56 (then flattened) and the pixel values are stored in this csv file. The first column corresponds to name of the image followed by 3136 columns containing the pixel value of the corresponding images.</li>
</ul>",True,True
