2552,different-anomalies-in-ecgs,"# Description

<h2>Introduction</h2>

<p>Electrocardiogram (ECG) can be reliably used as a measure to monitor the functionality of the cardiovascular system. Recently, there has been a great attention towards accurate categorization of heartbeats. While there are many commonalities between different ECG conditions, the focus of most studies has been classifying a set of conditions on a dataset annotated for that task rather than learning and employing a transferable knowledge between different tasks. </p>
<p> The aim of this competition is to develop a method based on deep recurrent neural networks for the classification of heartbeats which is able to accurately classify five different arrhythmias in accordance with the AAMI EC57 standard. </p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

Evaluation is based on the mean F1-score over the different labels.","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set, the last column represents the labels </li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>",True,True
2553,predict22x22,"# Description

§¯§Ñ§Õ§à §á§à §à§Õ§ß§à§Þ§å §ã§à§ã§ä§à§ñ§ß§Ú§ð §Ü§Ý§Ö§ä§à§é§ß§à§Ô§à §Ñ§Ó§ä§à§Þ§Ñ§ä§Ñ §á§â§Ö§Õ§ã§Ü§Ñ§Ù§Ñ§ä§î §Õ§â§å§Ô§à§Ö.
§°§Ò§å§é§Ñ§ð§ë§Ú§Û §æ§Ñ§Û§Ý §á§à§Ý§å§é§Ö§ß §ä§Ñ§Ü§Ú§Þ §Ü§à§Õ§à§Þ:
```
n = 22
n_lines = 50000
np.random.seed(10)
tmp = []
for t in tqdm_notebook(range(n_lines)):
    k = np.random.randint(1, 6)
    X0 = init_pole(n)
    X1 = makeksteps(X0.copy(), k=k)
    tmp.append( np.r_[[t], [k], X1.ravel(), X0.ravel()] )
    
data = pd.DataFrame(np.array(tmp), columns = ['id', 'steps'] + ['x_' + str(t) for t in range(n*n)] + ['y_' + str(t) for t in range(n*n)])

data.to_csv('gtrain.csv', index=False)
```

§³§Ñ§Þ§í§Ö §Ó§Ñ§Ø§ß§í§Ö §æ§å§ß§Ü§è§Ú§Ú §Ù§Õ§Ö§ã§î:
```
def make_step(X):
    from scipy.signal import convolve2d
    nbrs_count = convolve2d(X, np.ones((3, 3)), mode='same', boundary='wrap') - X
    return (nbrs_count == 3) | (X & (nbrs_count == 2))
    
def makeksteps(X, k=3):
    for i in range(k):
        X = make_step(X)
    return (X)
```

