2609,uva-image-challenge-2020,"# Description

<p> Using analytics to better understand and monetize data via process augmentation and AI-enabled product innovation is an important opportunity for many established companies and start-ups. You will use the ¡°Deep Learning CNN Playbook¡± starter code to develop a predictive model that can predict an important health outcome. Predictive analytics is about predicting future or unknown outcomes. In this class competition, you will build a machine learning predictive model to best predict a particular outcome that may have significant societal and monetary value. You will leverage the starter code provided to you in class. This is a team-level competition.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The performance of each model will be evaluated using the area under the curve (AUC) metric computed on the receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve on the test data.</p>
<hr>

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For each instance in the dataset</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: Id and Prediction</p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>Id,Prediction<br>1,0.6746433<br></pre>","# Dataset Description

<p>The data details will be discussed in class.</p>",True,True
2610,20-ades,"# Description

The intrusion detector learning task is to build a predictive model (i.e. a classifier) capable of distinguishing between ""bad"" connections, called intrusions or attacks, and ""good"" normal connections.
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is AUC.</p>
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p>Submission files should contain two columns: Id and class. Class can be one of {0,1} but it can also be a score in the domain [0,1].</p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>Id,class<br />1,1<br /><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">8,8<br />9,9 10<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">10,10 9<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">etc.</span></pre>","# Dataset Description

**Two files are provided:**
- dev.csv: data to develop the models
- compete.csv: data to generate predictions for submission in kaggle

**Data dictionary**",True,True
