2619,jacoubet-atlas-of-paris-where-are-the-numbers,"# Description

The goal of this competition is to **detect the street numbers** in sheets of the *Jacoubet Atlas of Paris*. For each sheet, you have to find the numbers. In order to do that, you could, for instance, detect the bounding boxes and run an OCR on them.
 ![sample number bounding boxes](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F4537231%2F57427a6de3f4515483092aa8e77bd55d%2Fnumbers.png?generation=1583933730291531&alt=media)

Due to the current limitations of kaggle inClass competitions, we will evaluate an aggregation of your results based on a tiling of the input images. This is done by tiling each image with tiles of 100 pixels by 100 pixels as seen in the following figure.
![Tiling example](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F4537231%2F55759d4ac6bbfbaaa15b9112bc479009%2Fgrille.png?generation=1583935162415742&alt=media)
Each resulting tile has an ID using the minimum X and Y values of the tile in the form ""X\_Y"". The tiles being 100 pixels, the tiles are then 0\_0, 0\_100, 0\_200, ..., 100\_0, 100\_100, etc.

You are given, as a start, 5 images from the Jacoubet Atlas. In order to produce the final solution which will be evaluated, you have to add to the tile ID, the name of the file (without extension). For instance, you will have IDs:
Atlas\_de\_Jacoubet\_-\_11.\_Hospice\_Beaujon\_et\_ses\_environs\_-\_BHVP\_0\_0
Atlas\_de\_Jacoubet\_-\_11.\_Hospice\_Beaujon\_et\_ses\_environs\_-\_BHVP\_0\_100
Atlas\_de\_Jacoubet\_-\_11.\_Hospice\_Beaujon\_et\_ses\_environs\_-\_BHVP\_0\_200
Atlas\_de\_Jacoubet\_-\_11.\_Hospice\_Beaujon\_et\_ses\_environs\_-\_BHVP\_0\_300

For each final ID (image\_tile), you will have to aggregate the **sorted** numbers you have found. Hence, you might obtain:
| ID | number |
| --- | --- |
| Atlas\_de\_Jacoubet\_-\_11.\_Hospice\_Beaujon\_et\_ses\_environs\_-\_BHVP\_0\_0 | 10 |
| Atlas\_de\_Jacoubet\_-\_11.\_Hospice\_Beaujon\_et\_ses\_environs\_-\_BHVP\_0\_100 | 2 4 6 |
| Atlas\_de\_Jacoubet\_-\_11.\_Hospice\_Beaujon\_et\_ses\_environs\_-\_BHVP\_0\_200 | |

Meaning that we found number **10** in tile *0\_0* of image *Atlas_de_Jacoubet_-_11._Hospice_Beaujon_et_ses_environs_-_BHVP*, numbers 2, 4 and 6 in tile *0\_100* of the same image and, no number in tile *0\_200*.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The submissions are evaluated using the [Mean Levenshtein distance](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levenshtein_distance).

The submission format is CSV with columns (see description for the content description):
ID, numero","# Dataset Description

This first data source (more might be coming) contains 5 sheets of the Jacoubet Atlas of Paris, all containing street numbers.",True,True
