2704,homealone2020v2,"# Description

<p>HomeAlone 2020 is a mini-hackathon organized by the Students' Union of Faculty of Information Technology, University of Moratuwa. This is not like a traditional hackathon, but a more interesting and creative competition to all IT enthusiasts. This contest is open for anyone in Sri Lanka, who is willing to take their IT knowledge and creativeness to the next level!</p>
<p>Some tasks of this contest are published here in the Kaggle platform. Visit the evaluation page under this for more info about the competition.</P> 

----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>Please go through the below guidelines thoroughly before attempting the competition. </p>
<li>The evaluation metric for this competition is <ahref=""https://www.kaggle.com/wiki/MeanFScore""> Mean F1-Score</a>. </li>
<li><strong>You can only make 2 submissions per day.</strong></li>
<li>You have to make your submissions using your team name.(team_name.csv)</li>
<li>You can use any programming language that you are comfortable with to solve this problem.</li> 
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>Your submission file should contain</strong> two columns: NAME and  WINNER. It should contain the list of candidates that <strong>we have provided in the test set</strong> and the prediction whether the candidate won the election or not.</p>
<p> We have provided the 100% of your Public leaderboard score</P>

----------------------
# Problem Statement

You are given a training and testing dataset of a previous elections. Please download the 2 datasets and study them. Use the datasets to train a model.

Your task is to predict whether a given Election Candidate will win an election in the future or not. Using 1 or 0 to indicate the prediction about winning or losing is sufficient.

Please submit your answer according to the given submission format.
----------------------
# Clarification About Leaderboards

The public leaderboard is updated dynamically when the teams add their submissions.
But the public leaderboard display the team's score only by considering model along with 50% of the dataset. Therefore the score in the Public leaderboard can be changed after the whole dataset is finished evaluating.

The private leaderboard is visible only after the competition ends. Therefore the actual score you earned will be displayed here with various other details. This shows the final mark you obtained after evaluating your model according to the whole dataset.","# Dataset Description

<h2>Data files</h2>
<li>Train set - Training data set</li>
<li>Test set -  Test data set for submission</li>

<h2>Data Description</h2>
<li>Category - Scheduled Caste (SCs), Scheduled Tribes (STs) and General quota.</li>

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>Your submission file should contain</strong>two columns: NAME and  WINNER. It should contain the list of candidates that <strong>we have provided in the test set</strong> and the prediction whether the candidate won the election or not.</p>",True,True
