2707,dsc-house-price-prediction,"# Description

COVID-19 has caused so many damages to the world¡¯s economy. Analyst have reported that the major sectors to be impacted by this pandemic are:
?	Tourism & Leisure
?	Aviation & Maritime
?	Automotives
?	Construction & Real Estate
?	Manufacturing (non-essentials)
?	Financial Services
?	Education and Oil & Gas
Clearly, we can justify why these sectors will be affected. In Nigeria, liquidity will be the first challenge. People will sell properties including land just to be liquid even at ridiculously low prices.
Businesses will fold up and their buildings will be unoccupied for a long period of time, non-essential workers will lose their job and there would be low purchasing power.
With all these and other explicit effect of recessed economy, house prices will drop significantly.
As a data scientist, before you make moves to propose a solution, you need to understand the problem. This month¡¯s challenge will focus on the following tasks:
1.	Perform in-depth descriptive analysis and present your findings in a PowerPoint presentation file. Ensure your report includes the following:
a.	What the task is
b.	The approach
c.	Findings
d.	Proposed machine learning solution
2.	Execute your proposed Machine Learning solution by predicting house prices and submit your result on Kaggle competition page.
The question I would personally love to get answered is ¡°Is this the best time to buy properties? if Yes, what part of the country is the most optimal?¡±

Learning Rewards
1.	Knowledge
2.	Gift vouchers for grab
3.	Participation in A.I. acceleration training from Ernst & Young Team
Let the doers rejoice","# Dataset Description

## Variable Description
Suburb: Suburb  
HouseID: unique number for houses in the database  
Rooms: Number of rooms  
Price: Price in dollars  
### Method:  
S - property sold;  
SP - property sold prior;  
PI - property passed in;  
PN - sold prior not disclosed;  
SN - sold not disclosed;  
NB - no bid;  
VB - vendor bid;  
W - withdrawn prior to auction;  
SA - sold after auction;  
SS - sold after auction price not disclosed.  
N/A - price or highest bid not available.  
### Type:  
br - bedroom(s);  
h - house,cottage,villa, semi,terrace;  
u - unit, duplex;  
t - townhouse;  
RealEstate_Agent: Real Estate Agent  
Date: Date sold  
Distance: Distance from Town central in Kilometres  
Regionname: General Region (West, North West, North, North east ¡­etc)  
Propertycount: Number of properties that exist in the suburb.  
Bedroom2 : Scraped # of Bedrooms (from different source)  
Bathroom: Number of Bathrooms  
Car: Number of carspots  
Landsize: Land Size in Metres  
BuildingArea: Building Size in Metres  
YearBuilt: Year the house was built",True,True
2708,whoisafriend,"# Description

# Predict Friends or Not.

In this machine learning challenge you are to *predict whether two persons are friends or not.*

You are given a data of recorded events from a group of people and using the given data you have to predict whether they are friends or not. 

The personal information have been masked for obvious reasons.

### **Safe Coding!**
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Goal

It is your job to predict if two persons are friends or not.
For each in the test set, you must predict a 0 (Not a Friend) or 1 (Are Friends) value for the variable.

## Metric

Your score is the percentage of friends you correctly predict. This is known as accuracy.


## Submission File Format

You should submit a csv file with as given in the sample_submission.csv. Your submission will show an error if you have extra columns (beyond ID and Friends) or rows.

The file should have exactly 2 columns:
    
- ID
- Friends (contains your binary predictions: 1 for friends, 0 for not friends)

You can download an example submission file (sample_submission.csv) on the Data page.
----------------------
# Timeline

### The competition ends on **7 April 2020.**

### Timings : 

- **1 PM (UTC)**
- **6:30 PM (IST)**
----------------------
# Prizes

# Prizes

As this competition is a part of the CODE-DOWN, you will get points added in the leaderboard after you've won the competition.
 
**NOTE : The points to be given are in discussion and will be declared on the Slack Channel and Facebook Page**

1st Position : TBD

2nd Position : TBD
 

**NOTE : You will also get points for your public kernels based on combination of *number of stars* + *number of forks* + originality of the content.**","# Dataset Description

## Overview

The data has been split into two groups:

- training set (train.csv)
- test set (test.csv)


The training set should be used to build your machine learning models. For the training set, we provide the outcome (also known as the ¡°ground truth¡±) for each meeting. Your model will be based on ¡°features¡± like Interaction Duration, Interaction Type, etc You can also use feature engineering to create new features.

The test set should be used to see how well your model performs on unseen data. For the test set, we do not provide the ground truth for each meeting. It is your job to predict these outcomes. For each record in the test set, use the model you trained to predict whether or not they are Friends.

We also include sample_submission.csv, a set of predictions that assume nobody is a friend, as an example of what a submission file should look like.

## Data Dictionary

- Person A : Name of Person A
- Person B : Name of Person B
- Years of Knowing : Years of Person A knowing Person B
- Interaction Type : The type of interaction they had
- Interaction Duration : The duration of interaction they had (in minutes)
- Moon Phase During Interaction : The Moon Phase during their interaction",True,True
