2823,cs4670spring2020pa3,"# Description

<h1>Welcome to the CS 4670 Kaggle Competition!</h1>

On his adventures travelling the world, Bharath (and his crew of dedicated TAs) collected hundreds of photographs of different animals. Unfortunately, there's been a mix-up, and the pictures have all been shuffled together! Your mission - if you choose to accept it - is to classify all the animal photographs into the appropriate categories.

<h2>Competition Rules</h2>
- Open Source libraries such as cv2, numpy, scipy, skimage are allowed, although they must be cited in the writeup. Use of pre-trained models such as ResNet, Vgg, etc. is not allowed.
- There is a computational budget of 5MB for the maximum size of the model weights - work within these limits.
- Sharing personal code between teams or acquiring labels for the test dataset (by hand labeling/other means) is expressly forbidden, and will be considered a violation of academic integrity. To check consistency, we will run your model with your training script uploaded to CMS.
- Have fun, and be creative!

<h2>Acknowledgements</h2>
Training/Validation Datasets obtained from the tiny image","# Dataset Description

<h2>Welcome to The Data Page!</h2>
Here you will find the test data for generating the submission csv file using Kaggle_Submission.ipynb. You find more details on how to integrate this dataset with your current code in the About this file section below.

<h2>/test_labeled</h2>
This folder contains 16 subfolders corresponding to each of the 16 classes. Try exploring the folder by clicking on the down arrow next to the folder name below. You will see that each ""class folder"" has 25 images. We have included them because **the distribution that these images come from is not the same distribution as the training images**. You may find it helpful to perform validation on this data to get an idea of how well your model generalizes. You may also train on these images along with the provided training data. **Note**: this distribution is similar to the one being used by Kaggle for both public and private rankings.

<h2>/test_unlabeled</h2>
This folder contains 1984 images on which you will perform class prediction. Make sure this folder is place inside /data so Kaggle_Submission.ipynb can locate it. Note: The distribution is similar to the labeled data in */test_labeled*. You **may not** hand-label the images as this is a **violation of Academic Integrity**. See **Rules** for more information.

Now get cracking. Bharath needs your help sorting the animals.",True,True
