# Evaluation

<h3>Evaluation metric: R2Score</h3>

----------------------
# Timeline

<p>Date: 9 May - 23 May 2020, 2359</p>
<p>Submission Deadline: 05/23/2020 11:59 PM SGT</p>
----------------------
# Prizes

## ?? WIN ATTRACTIVE PRIZES! ?? 
1st prize: $200 CapitaVoucher 
2nd prize: $100 CapitaVoucher
3rd prize: $50 CapitaVoucher
Consolation: $40 x 10 CapitaVouchers
Winners will be contacted via DM through email!
----------------------
# Kernels Requirements

Tested under Python 3.8, scikit-learn 0.22.2, numpy 1.18.1, pandas 1.0.3, matplotlib 3.1.3, seaborn 0.10.1.","# Dataset Description

<h3>Please refer to ""submission_sample.csv"" for your submission.</h3>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>submission_sample.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>
<h2> Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>id</strong> - row that represent id of the diamond</li>
<li><strong>price</strong> - known price of diamonds</li>
<li><strong>carat</strong> - weight of the diamond </li>
<li><strong>cut</strong> - quality of the cut (Fair, Good, Very Good, Premium, Ideal)</li>
<li><strong>color</strong> - diamond colour, from D (best) to J (worst)</li>
<li><strong>clarity</strong> - a measurement of how clear the diamond is (I1 (worst), SI2, SI1, VS2, VS1, VVS2, VVS1, IF (best))</li>
<li><strong>x</strong> - length in mm</li>
<li><strong>y</strong> - width in mm</li>
<li><strong>z</strong> - depth in mm</li>
<li><strong>depth</strong> - total depth percentage = z / mean(x, y) = 2 * z / (x + y)</li>
<li><strong>table</strong> - width of top of diamond relative to widest point</li>
</ul>",True,True
