3001,cv2020-classification-challenge,"# Description

<h2>Classification Competition</h2>

<p>Image classification is a classic task in the Computer Vision domain. In this classification competition, you need to train your model based on a total of 120 species of dogs, and predict the type of images in the test set to get as much accuracy as possible.</p><p>

</p><p>NOTE: You are allowed to use ImageNet pretrained weights to initialize your model and NOT allowed to use ANY OTHER dataset for training.</p><p></p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>We adopt the Categorization Accuracy metric for evaluation.</p>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>

</p>Training set: kaggle_cv_train.zip</p>
</p>Test set: kaggle_cv_train.zip</p>
</p>File that you need to upload: sample_submission.csv</p>

</p> Note: There is no .txt file, you need to write your own data_loader to process the data.</p>",True,True
