3015,aml-week-4,"# Description

You goal is to use h2o to create a logistic regression model.  The target variable is called ""target"".  Features are anonymised but you will see that there are numeric, categorical and hccv features.  You are expected to deal sensibly with missings in train or test data, with numeric, categorical and hccv features.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric is AUC.","# Dataset Description

Data for this competition is anonymised, however the feature names make clear what type of feature it is.  hccvs have not been named differently but they should be obvious to you.",True,True
3016,30-days-of-ml-2,"# Description

# DAY 14-16 
## HELPING THE MERRY MEN

Nollywood is selling tickets to their newly released movie   
**MERRY MEN** starring your friendly neighbourhood Babalawo **GeekTutor**  
   
Advertisements are placed on all social media platforms along with  link to buy tickets to the movie. Different users view the ads. Some buy the tickets, some don't.   

The data of 320 users that viewed the ad are stored.   
  
You are a Machine Learning Engineer working at Nollywood you are to create a model using this data to predict if a user will or will not buy the ticket so they can tailor the adverts to the right user. 

###Goodluck
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Data  
Check the data section. Each document has been described.  
    
## Submission
You will submit a csv file with two columns **User Id** and **Purchased** an each row will correspond to that of the test data.
<pre>User Id,Purchased
15657163,0
15577514,1
15807909,0
15646091,1
15730688,0
</pre>

Just as described above this is what your submission should look like. You can refer to **sample.csv** in the data section.   

You have a maximum of 20 submissions per day.    
   
### Submissions close on 24/06/2020 by 5:00am

## Evaluation Metric   
You will be scored based on **Categorization Accuracy**   
Your score will vary from 0.0000 to 1.0000.","# Dataset Description


<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>training.csv</strong> - the training set. Use this to train your classification model</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set. You will input these values into your trained model to make a prediction</li>
<li><strong>sample.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>

</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>User Id</strong> - A number unique to every customer. No two customers have the same User Id</li>
<li><strong>Gender</strong> - Male or Female</li>
<li><strong>Age</strong> - Age of the user</li>
<li><strong>EstimatedSalary</strong> - Estimated salary of the user </li> 
<li><strong>Purchased</strong> - Whether or not the user purchased the ticket. 1 if the user purchased it and 0 otherwise.</li> 
</ul>",True,True
