3037,fare-classification-2020,"# Description

<p>Training dataset consists of a sample tuk rides completed. Nearly 10% of the fares are incorrect. The aim should be to train a model based on the given dataset and predict whether the fare of a new set of trips is correct or not.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>Submissions will be evaluated based on their <a href=""https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F1_score""> macro F1 score </a> </p>
<p>For each tripId in the test set, you must predict whether the fare is correct (1) or incorrect(0)<p>
<p> The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>tripid,prediction<span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;""><br/>189123628,1 <br\><br />189125358,1<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">189125719,1<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">etc.</span></pre>","# Dataset Description

<p>Use <strong>train.csv</strong> file  to train the model and test it. You can split the data to test/train as required for model building. Then you are expected to classify <strong>test.csv</strong> trips. Your submission should be in the format of <strong>sample_submission.csv</strong> as described</p>",True,True
