3042,sysu-dmml-b,"# Description

Please use ""train"" data set to train your model. The objective is to predict the ""Playoffs"".

Each student should complete this assignment independently. Please edit your team name as ""name_student id"". All algorithms, tools and packages you obtained from Internet can be used.
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is Accuracy. </p>
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For every author in the dataset</strong>, submission files in CSV should contain two columns: Id and Playoffs. The Id should be as same as the Id in Test data set, and the Playoffs should be your predictions. </p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>Id,Playoffs<br />1,1<br />2,0 <br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">3,0<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">etc.</span></pre>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>Test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>Sample Submission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Id</strong> - an anonymous id</li>
<li><strong>RS</strong> - number of runs scored</li>
<li><strong>RA</strong> -number of runs allowed</li>
<li><strong>W</strong> - number of wins</li>
<li><strong>OBP</strong> - on-base percentage </li>
<li><strong>SLG</strong> - slugging percentage</li>
<li><strong>BA</strong> - batting average</li>
<li><strong>Playoffs</strong> - in palyoffs or not</li>
<li><strong>RankSeason</strong> - rank in season</li>
<li><strong>RankPlayoffs</strong> - rank in playoffs</li>
<li><strong>G</strong> - number of games</li>
<li><strong>OOBP</strong> - opponents on-base percentage </li>
<li><strong>OSLG</strong> - opponents slugging percentage</li>

</ul>",True,True
