3049,hcirs-ctf,"# Description

<h1> Fraudulent Transactions </h1>
<p>Baba's Shopping Company has been having a problem with fraudulent transactions. Can you train a model to predict whether a transaction is fraudulent? <br>
Baba's Shopping Company has given you anonymised transaction data to work with - train.csv. Using this data, predict whether the transactions in test.csv are fraudulent.  </p><p>
</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<h2>Evaluation Metric</h2>
<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is <a href=""https://towardsdatascience.com/understanding-auc-roc-curve-68b2303cc9c5""> AUC ROC Curve</a>. It is basically the weighted average of true positives and true negatives</p>

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For every author in the dataset</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: id and Class. Class is the predicted label from the test set, 0 or 1. </p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>id,Class<br>0,0<br>0,0<br>0,0<br>.<br>.<br>.<br>56118,0<br>56119,1<br>56120,0</pre>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
<li>etc...</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>V1-V40</strong> - Anonymised Datapoints</li>
<li><strong>Amount</strong> - Amount transaction</li>
<li><strong>Class</strong> - Fraudulent Transaction?</li>
<li>etc...</li>
</ul>",True,True
