3125,sperm-morphological-quality,"# Description

<h2>Context</h2>
<p>The task is to assess the morphological quality of sperm cells. The dataset consists of two distinct image qualities and the images of each quality fall into two categories, namely good and bad morphological quality sperm.</p>
<h2>Dataset details</h2>
<p>The dataset contains images of two distinct qualities. They differ based on the imaging systems used to capture the images.</p>
<p>The high-quality set comprises 4142 annotated sperm images, imaged using an industry grade 100X microscope. The images are annotated as good and bad sperm based on its morphological quality.</p>
<p>The low-quality set comprises 10 unannotated smeared and stained slides of human sperm samples imaged using a 3D-printed portable imaging system.</p>
<p>Note: Morphological quality depicts the two different classes of sperm cells. Image quality refers to the two different sub-datasets. Each sub-dataset contains images of good and bad morphological quality.</p>
<h2>Task</h2>
<p>The aim is to use the high-quality annotated data to obtain optimal performance on low-quality unannotated data.</p>
<h2>Submission details</h2>
<p>Your submission should include the following ¨C </p>
<p>1. ReadMe file outlining the approach used with the architecture and other relevant details</p>
<p>2. All scripts used for training and testing</p>
<p>3. Best model used to evaluate the low-quality set</p>
<p>4. Slide-wise morphological quality scores of the low-quality set in a .csv file with the following format ¨C </p>
<pre>Slide Number (1-10), Quality Score</pre>
<p>Note : Quality Score can be calculated as - </p>
<p>\[ q = \frac {n_{good}}{n_{total}}\]</p>
<p> where,\[{n_{good}}\] indicates the number of good sperm cells in the slide and \[{n_{total}}\] indicates the total number of sperm cells in the slide.</p>
<p>10 quality score values should be provided corresponding to the 10 slides in the low quality set.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<h2>Evaluation</h2>
<p>Your Quality Score file will be evaluated using the Root Mean Square Error metric : </p>
<p>\[rmse = \sqrt{(\frac{1}{10})\sum_{i=1}^{10}(y_{i} - t_{i})^{2}}\]</p>
<p>where \[y_{i}\] denotes your quality score for slide <b>i</b> and \[t_{i}\] denotes the gold standard quality score for slide <b>i</b>.</p>","# Dataset Description

<h2>Data description</h2>
<p>The master directory is labelled <b>Sperm-Data</b> and contains 2 sub-directories - </p>
<ul>
<li><b>High Quality Sperm - Labeled</b></li>
<li><b>Low Quality Sperm - Unlabeled</b></li>
</ul>
<p>The directory named as <b>High Quality Sperm - Labeled</b> totally contains 4142 images. It contains 2 sub-directories - </p>
<ul>
<li><b>Bad Sperm</b> which contains 3656 images</li>
<li><b>Good Sperm</b> which contains 486 images</li>
</ul>
<p>The directory named as <b>Low Quality Sperm - Unlabeled</b> totally contains 4716 images. It contains 10 sub-directories (slides)- </p>
<ul>
<li><b>D926</b> which contains 135 images</li>
<li><b>E883</b> which contains 222 images</li>
<li><b>E902</b> which contains 229 images</li>
<li><b>E914</b> which contains 307 images</li>
<li><b>E919</b> which contains 1014 images</li>
<li><b>E950</b> which contains 315 images</li>
<li><b>E952</b> which contains 809 images</li>
<li><b>E979</b> which contains 529 images</li>
<li><b>E986</b> which contains 311 images</li>
<li><b>E998</b> which contains 845 images</li>
</ul>",True,True
