3153,ml-with-python-course-project,"# Description

<h2>Welcome</h2>
<p>Good day</p>
<p>This is a limited edition Kaggle competition in evaluation of a paid short course on machine learning. The course titled **Machine Learning with Python** hosetd by QuantumAI. (Write something about the course, time, syllabus. ) The course contained regression, classification and clustering. </p>

<h2>About QuantumAI</h2>
<p>This organization has the purpose of gathering all the Data Science, Big Data, Machine Learning, and Deep learning enthusiast and professionals in BD.</p>

<h2>Before joining</h2>
<p>Please complete the survey feedback form before joining the competition.</p>
  Click [here](https://forms.gle/eF5b7S32cm6FkPSU8).

<h2>Questions</h2>
1. Play with the data conducting all statistical tests like mean, mode, median and other description using pandas.
2. Build a prediction model using SVM, Logistic R, Naive Bayes, Decision tree. Compare the model accuracy and find the best model. If possible, please explain why your model is the best?
3. Make a prediction of the following factors: 
&lt;...&gt;","# Dataset Description

<h2>Data files</h2>
<p>This page shows the data files. Here you find the format and content of each file. There is no single format for this page that is appropriate for all competitions, but you should strive to describe as much as you can here. A little time spent describing the data here can save a lot of time answering questions later. Participants should be able to answer the questions listed in the overview tab description. 

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
