3162,girlsgoit-competition-2020,"# Description

<h1> Prezicerea popularit??ii cantecelor de pe Spotify</h1>
<p> ?n aceast? competi?ie va trebui s? prezice?i popularitatea unui cantec de pe Spotify analizand datele din baza de date propus?. Pe baza a ceea ce a?i ?nv??at la GirlsGoIT summer camp, va trebui s? crea?i un model de clasificare/regresie care s? prezic? pentru fiecare cantec popularitatea - de la 1 la 10</p>


<h1>Reguli:</h1>
<ul>
 <li>Competi?ia se adreseaz? doar participantelor la tab?ra de var? GirlsGoIT 2020</li>
<li> Codul trebuie s? fie scris ?n **Python**, alte limbaje de programare nu se accept?!!! </li>
<li> Se vor utiliza doar modelele ?nv??ate la tab?ra de var? GirlsGoIT!</li>
 <li> Nu copia?i ideile altor echipe, s-ar putea ca ideea voastr? s? fie mai bun?!</li>
 <li> Ve?i ?nc?rca doar fi?ierul cu predic?ii predictions.csv, iar prezent?rile le ve?i trimite separat trainerilor GirlsGoIT!</li>
</ul>

<h2>Evaluarea finala</h2>
<p>Evaluarea finala va consta ?n rezultatul ob?inut la aceast? competi?ie pe kaggle ?i evaluarea prezent?rii powerpoint, ?n care ve?i include descrierea proiectului, grafice, etc.</p>

----------------------
# Evaluation

<h2> Modalitatea de evaluare</h2>
<p> Pentru evaluarea rezultatelor, ve?i trimite de fiecare data <b> un singur fi?ier .csv</b>, in formatul de mai jos. Pe durata competi?iei, ve?i putea trimite <b>maxim cate 2 solu?ii zilnic</b></p>

<p>?n leaderboard, ve?i vedea clasamentul bazat pe 40% din setul de date final de evaluare. Celelalte 60% din setul de date vor fi ascunse ?i solu?ia vostr? va fi testat? doar dup? ce se va ?ncheia competit?ia. </p>

<p> La final ve?i putea alege 2 solu?ii care s? fie evaluate pe setul de date final</p>

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
Pentru fiecare cantec din dataset, fi?ierul pe care ?l trimite?i (submission file) trebuie s? con?in? **2 coloane: SongId ?i Popularity**.

Fi?ierul ?nc?rcat (submission file) trebuie s? fie salvat cu extensia **.csv**, ?n urm?torul format:

<pre>SongID, Popularity
1,3
2,1
3,2</pre>


<h2> Metrici de evaluare </h2>
<p> Pentru evaliarea acestei competitii, se va folosi metrica <a href=""https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accuracy_and_precision"">""Classification accuracy""</a></p>
<p>Aceasta e definita ca numarul de exemple clasificate corect impartit la numarul total de exemple din setul de date.
</p><p>\[ Accuracy = \frac{nrDeExempleClasificateCorect}{nrTotalDeExemple} \]</p>


<h2>Evaluarea finala</h2>
<p>Evaluarea finala va consta ?n rezultatul ob?inut la aceast? competi?ie pe kaggle ?i evaluarea prezent?rii powerpoint, ?n care ve?i include descrierea proiectului, grafice, etc.</p>","# Dataset Description

<p> Aceast? pagin? con?ine fi?ierele cu date necesare pentru competi?ie</p>
<p> Mai jos g?si?i descrierea fi?ierelor ?i a coloanelor din seturile de date</p>

<h2>Descrierea fi?ierelor</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - setul de date de antrenare </li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - setul de date de testare</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> -un exemplu de fisier solutie in formatul corect</li>
</ul>
<h2>Coloane ?n seturile de date</h2>

<h5>Primary:</h5>
<ul>
<li><strong>ID </strong>(Id of track generated by Spotify)</li>
</ul>
<h5>Numerical:</h5>
<ul>
<li><strong>acousticness </strong>(Ranges from 0 to 1)</li>
<li><strong>danceability </strong>(Ranges from 0 to 1)</li>
<li><strong>energy</strong> (Ranges from 0 to 1)</li>
<li><strong>duration_ms </strong>(Integer typically ranging from 200k to 300k)</li>
<li><strong>instrumentalness </strong>(Ranges from 0 to 1)</li>
<li><strong>valence</strong> (Ranges from 0 to 1)</li>
<li><strong>popularity </strong>(Ranges from 0 to 100)</li>
<li><strong>tempo </strong>(Float typically ranging from 50 to 150)</li>
<li><strong>liveness </strong>(Ranges from 0 to 1)</li>
<li><strong> loudness </strong>(Float typically ranging from -60 to 0)</li>
<li><strong> speechiness </strong>(Ranges from 0 to 1)</li>
<li><strong> year </strong>(Ranges from 1921 to 2020)</li>
</ul>

<h5>Dummy:</h5>
<ul>
<li><strong>mode (0 = Minor, 1 = Major)</li>
<li><strong>explicit (0 = No explicit content, 1 = Explicit content)</li>
</ul>

<h5>Categorical:</h5>
<ul>
<li><strong>key</strong> (All keys on octave encoded as values ranging from 0 to 11, starting on C as 0, C# as 1 and so on¡­)</li>
<li><strong> artists</strong> (List of artists mentioned)</li>
<li><strong>release_date </strong>(Date of release mostly in yyyy-mm-dd format, however precision of date may vary)</li>
<li><strong>name </strong>(Name of the song)</li>

<li><strong>popularity</strong>(Popularity of the song to be predicted) - integer in range from 0 to 10</li>

</ul>

<br>
<p>More on Spotify audio features, click <a href=""https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-api/reference/tracks/get-audio-features"">here</a></p>
<p>More on other Spotify track features, click <a href=""https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-api/reference/tracks/get-track"">here</a></p>

<h2>Acknowledgements</h2>
<p>Thank you for providing the initial Spotify dataset here: <a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/yamaerenay/spotify-dataset-19212020-160k-tracks?select=data.csv""> 
https://www.kaggle.com/yamaerenay/spotify-dataset-19212020-160k-tracks?select=data.csv
</a>
</p>",True,True
