3191,nmlo-contest-2,"# Description

##Description
In this competition, you have to predict the type of clothing based on an image. You must code your neural network from scratch (only using libraries like numpy and pandas). You may not use libraries like scikit-learn, tensorflow, pytorch, etc.

The clothing labels are: t-shirt/top (0), trouser (1), pullover (2), dress (3), coat (4), sandal (5), shirt (6), sneaker (7), bag (8), ankle boot (9).

Data was taken from zalandoresearch.


##Learning Resources
- [Introduction to numpy](https://www.w3schools.com/python/numpy_intro.asp#:~:text=NumPy%20Introduction&text=NumPy%20is%20a%20python%20library,you%20can%20use%20it%20freely.) 
- [Overview of neural network](https://towardsdatascience.com/first-neural-network-for-beginners-explained-with-code-4cfd37e06eaf)
- [Perceptron](https://tjmachinelearning.com/lectures/1920/nn/Neural_Networks_1.pdf)
- [Neuron and forward propagation](https://tjmachinelearning.com/lectures/1920/nn/Neural_Networks_2.pdf)
- [Backpropagation](https://tjmachinelearning.com/lectures/1920/nn/Neural_Networks_3.pdf) 
- [Hyperparameter optimization](https://tjmachinelearning.com/lectures/1920/nn/Hyperparameter_Optimizations.pdf)
- [Coding neural network from scratch](https://towardsdatascience.com/how-to-build-your-own-neural-network-from-scratch-in-python-68998a08e4f6)
----------------------
# Evaluation

Categorization Accuracy is used to score submissions.","# Dataset Description

