3211,xyz10test2,"# Description

<p> <a href=""https://aka.ms/location20"">Indoor Location Competition 2.0</a> is a continuation of Microsoft Indoor Location Competition. Competition this year will be completely virtual and evaluated on large-scale real indoor location datasets. The dataset to be released consists of dense indoor signatures of WiFi, geomagnetic field, iBeacons etc., as well as ground truth collected from hundreds of buildings in Chinese cities.</p>
<h2>History</h2>
- 2014 Microsoft Indoor Localization Competition
- ¡­
- 2018
- 2020 Indoor Location Competition 2.0
<h2>What¡¯s New This Year?</h2>
- Completely Virtual
 - Easy setup
 - Flexible schedule
 - Online ranking
- Real-world Dataset
 - Structured data with large coverage
 - Standardized evaluation
 - Research beyond competition
<h2>Timeline</h2>
- April: announcement
- July: sample data &amp; code release
- August: complete data release &amp; competition launch 
- November: workshop &amp; award ceremony
<h2>Competition Logistics</h2>
- Kaggle
- Evaluation metric
 - Euclidean distance between the ground truth coordinates and the estimated by the system under test coordinates.
 - The average Euclidean distance across all evaluation points will be the overall score of each team.
- Awards
 - Top 3 teams will be awarded prizes.
 - Top teams will be invited to present at ACM SenSys¡¯20.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Outline:
<h2>Goal</h2>
<p>It is your job to predict the coordinates for the items listed in the first column of  <a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/c/xyz10test2/data"">sample_solution_of_test_data.csv</a>.</p>

<h2>Metric</h2>
<p>Your score is average of square error between your answers and the standard answers. 
The smaller the result, the better.</p>



<h2>Submission File Format</h2>
<p>You should submit a csv file as <a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/c/xyz10test2/data"">sample_solution_of_test_data.csv</a>. The only you can change is the second column.</p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
 - WaypointId (sorted in any order)
 - Coordinate
<pre>WaypointId,Coordinate<br>site3_B1_5dda14979191710006b5720e_1574572522291_X,123.45<br>site3_B1_5dda14979191710006b5720e_1574572522291_Y,10.3<br>site3_B1_5dda14979191710006b5720e_1574572525431_X,123<br>site3_B1_5dda14979191710006b5720e_1574572525431_Y,37.5<br>Etc.<br></pre>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test</strong> - the testing set</li>
<li><strong>sample_solution_of_test_data</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
<li><strong>waypoints_in_train_data.csv</strong> - the waypoints extracted from train set</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
See  <a href=""https://github.com/location-competition/indoor-location-competition-20/blob/master/README.md"">README.md</a> on GitHub project  <a href=""https://github.com/location-competition/indoor-location-competition-20"">indoor-location-competition-20</a>.",True,True
