3226,chords-prediction,"# Description

# ##  **Competition Brief**
Hey there!
In this competition, you have to build a model to predict chords that were played in a Bach piece given pitch, bass, and meter. You can use any multiclass classifier for prediction.

# ## **Hosts**
This competition is being hosted by the Society for Data Science, Birla Institute of Technology Mesra. You can check us out [here](https://sdsbitmesra.in/)

----------------------
# Instructions

## **EVALUATION Metric**
The Scoring Metric for this competition is categorization accuracy.

**## Submission**
The submission format is given in the data. There should be two columns in the CSV file titled 'choral_ID' and chord_label as given in the sample submission file.
----------------------
# Data Description


# **Description**
Pitch classes information has been extracted from MIDI sources downloaded from (JSB Chorales). Meter information has been computed through the Meter program which is part of the Melisma music analyser (Melisma: http://www.link.cs.cmu.edu/music-analysis/). Chord labels have been manually annotated by a human expert.


**# # LICENSE**
UCI Machine Learning Repository

D. P. Radicioni and R. Esposito. Advances in Music Information Retrieval, chapter BREVE: an HMPerceptron-Based Chord Recognition System. Studies in Computational Intelligence, Zbigniew W. Ras, and Alicja Wieczorkowska (Editors), Springer, 2010.

****# Dataset Attributes****
**## Identifiers**
Id - choral_ID	string	Corresponding to the file names from Bach Central: http://www.bachcentral.com/

**## Other Columns**
Name	Type	Description
event_number	integer	Index (starting from 1) of the event inside the chorale.
pitch_1	string	C: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
pitch_2	string	C#/Db: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
pitch_3	string	D: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
pitch_4	string	D#/Eb: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
pitch_5	string	E: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
pitch_6	string	F: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
pitch_7	string	F#/Gb: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
pitch_8	string	G: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
pitch_9	string	G#/Ab: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
pitch_10	string	A: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
pitch_11	string	A#/Bb: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
pitch_12	string	B: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
chord_label	string	Predictor Class: Chord resonating during the given event.","# Dataset Description


-Name	Type	Description
-choral_ID	string	Corresponding to the file names
-event_number	integer	Index (starting from 1) of the event inside the chorale.
-pitch_1	string	C: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
-pitch_2	string	C#/Db: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
-pitch_3	string	D: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
-pitch_4	string	D#/Eb: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
-pitch_5	string	E: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
-pitch_6	string	F: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
-pitch_7	string	F#/Gb: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
-pitch_8	string	G: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
-pitch_9	string	G#/Ab: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
-pitch_10	string	A: YES/NO depending on whether pitch is present.
