3247,BYUMovieRatings,"# Description

<p>We are using a train-test split of the IMDB 5000 movie database to begin building models for predicting movie ratings. The dataset contains information of 5000 different movies along with the IMDB score.  The IMDB score is from 1 to 10 with 10 suggesting a very well received movie. 
 Your goal is to use any available information to predict the IMDB score.  </p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>Prediction scores will be calculated based on the root mean square error criteria:</p>
<p>\[ RMSE = \sqrt{\frac{1}{n_{test}} \sum_{i=1}^{n_{test}}(\hat{y}_i - y_i)^2} \]</p>
<p>where ""y"" is the actual movie rating and ""y-hat"" is the predicted movie rating. </p>
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p>Submission files should contain two columns: movie_title and imdb_score.  The csv file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>movie_title,imdb_score<br>Movie Title, 7.0<br></pre>","# Dataset Description

