3388,stat946,"# Description

In this data challenge, we will practise how to use neural networks for the task of image classification. For this purpose, you will do the CIFAR-10 classification task. CIFAR-10  is an established computer-vision dataset consist of 60,000 32x32 colour images (50,000 train samples and 10,000 test samples) containing one of the 10 known objects: airplane, automobile, bird, cat, deer, dog, frog, horse, ship, and truck <a href=""https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html"">[1]</a>.  You can find some examples of this dataset below:
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F262611%2Ffd05ee6cb5b7d35fafe373c92e874d04%2Fcifar10.PNG?generation=1601079925214299&amp;alt=media)

<h2>Task </h2>
1- Download all parts of the dataset from the data section.
2- Design a neural network that gets the images from the input and predicts the labels of the images in the output.
3- Train your neural network using the train dataset.
4- Predict the correct labels of test data and submit your prediction file. You can find a sample submission file and its format in the data section (Note that later you also need to submit your codes in the learn and your submission file must be reproducible by your code)
5- The deadline for this competition is Oct 9, 11:59 pm EST= Oct 10, 3:59 am UTC (Kaggle time)
6- You have a submission limitation of 5/day for this challenge.
7- Team is not allowed for this competition
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on classification accuracy (the percent of labels that are predicted correctly).

Submission Format
For each image in the test set, predict a label for the given id. Your labels must match the label ids exactly {'plane'=0, 'car'=1, 'bird'=2, 'cat'=3, 'deer'=4, 'dog'=5, 'frog'=6, 'horse'=7, 'ship'=8, 'truck'=9}. Your submission should have a header.

<pre>&lt;p&gt;id,label
0,1
1,1
2,3
3,0
...&lt;/p&gt;</pre>","# Dataset Description

<p>Here you can find the dataset. To download the data you can either select each part and download them separately or you can download them all.</p>

<h2>Data description</h2>
<b>1- tran: </b>Contains the train set images. This directory consists of 50,000 jpg files. Each image has a unique id between 0-49,999 which indicates the sample ids. <br /><br />
 <b>2- test: </b>Contains the test set images. This directory consists of 10,000 jpg files. Each image has a unique id between 0-9,999 which indicates the sample ids. <br /><br />
<b>3- train_labels.csv</b> Is a CSV file with two columns. The first column indicates the samples id and the second column indicates the label of the samples. The labels are between 0 and 9. Here you can find how they are mapped. <br />
'plane' -> 0 <br />
'car' -> 1 <br />
'bird' -> 2 <br />
'cat' -> 3 <br />
'deer' -> 4 <br />
'dog' ->5 <br />
'frog' -> 6 <br />
'horse' -> 7 <br />
'ship' -> 8 <br />
'truck' -> 9
<br /><br />
<b>4- sample_submission.csv: </b> Is the sample submission file which your submitted results must be similar to this file. Like the train_labels.csv file, this file also have two columns where the first column of it indicates the ids of the test samples and the second column indicates the predicted labels of your model. After training your model, you should create a file similar to this file and submit it here in this competition.",True,True
