3392,11-785-fall-20-homework-2-part-2,"# Description

<p>In this assignment, you will use Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) to design an end-to-end system for face verification. Your system will be given two images as input and will output a score that quantifies the similarity between the faces in these images. This helps us decide whether the faces from the two images are of the same person or not.</p>


----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The Receiver Operating Characteristic (ROC) curve is created by plotting the True Positive Rate (TPR) against the False Positive Rate (FPR) at various threshold settings. The Area Under the Curve (AUC) for the ROC curve is equal to the probability that a classifier will rank a randomly chosen similar pair (images of same people) higher than a randomly chosen dissimilar one (images from two different people) (assuming 'similar' ranks higher than 'dissimilar' in terms of similarity scores). 
</p>","# Dataset Description

<p>The structure of the dataset folder is as follows:</p>

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>classification_data</strong></li>
<li><strong>verification_data</strong></li>
<li><strong>verification_pairs_val.txt</strong></li>
<li><strong>verification_pairs_test.txt</strong></li>
<li><strong>hw2p2_sample_submission</strong></li>
</ul>",True,True
3393,Imagenette-comp,"# Description

# Imagenette Competition
Hi! It's the Imagenette competition, based on [imagenette](https://github.com/fastai/imagenette) dataset. This dataset is one of the main benchmark dataset for the image classification task, within ImageNet and CIFAR. Your goal here is creating and training a neural network model, that will identify an object on a photo.
## Data Description
Dataset splits into train and test part. The training part consist of 10 folders with photos for each class. The test part has only photos without any distribution.
## Baseline
In [github link](https://github.com/catalyst-team/dl-course/tree/master/homework-2/classification) you can find baseline notebook which will help you start your work.
