3432,ece4110-mini-project-1,"# Description

Consider the file **step_noisy0.wav**, available under the Data tab. This is an audio recording of Neil Armstrong¡¯s famous phrase ¡°That¡¯s one small step for [a] man; one giant leap for mankind,¡± which has been corrupted by additive noise. Use techniques discussed in class to remove as much of the noise from this recording as you can. Specifically, produce a second recording, say **step.wav**, that is as close as possible in mean square sense to the original, uncorrupted recording (which is not available to you).
----------------------
# Data Description

The data are .wav audio files.","# Dataset Description

The target audio file is here. Use any program/language you like to parse it and try to eliminate the noise. For example, if you are using MATLAB, you can use $$\mathsf{[Y,Fs] = audioread('step\_noisy.wav');}$$ and $$\mathsf{audiowrite('step\_filtered.wav',Y,Fs);}$$ to load and save **.wav** files.",True,True
