3478,tau-ethiopic-digit-recognition,"# Description

<p>Character recognition is one of the first fields where machine learning was used. Among the first extensive experiments was the MNIST dataset, handwritten digits 0...9 collected from US postal envelopes. Since this classic benchmark collection, a number of MNIST-like datasets have been collected; for example the Fashion MNIST dataset consisting of pictures of 10 different clothing classes. </p>

<p>Recently, the list of MNIST's was extended by <i>Afro-MNIST</i>, a synthetic MNIST-style dataset for four orthographies used in Afro-Asiatic and Niger-Congo languages. This competition hosts a modified version of the Ge`ez (Ethiopic) dataset published in the paper [1].</p>

<p>The competition is part of Tampere University (TAU) course DATA.ML.200 <i>Pattern Recognition and Machine Learning</i> in the Fall semester 2020.</p>

<p>[1] Daniel J Wu, Andrew C Yang, Vinay U Prabhu, ""Afro-MNIST: Synthetic generation of MNIST-style datasets for low-resource languages,"" in <i>ICLR 2020 Practical Machine Learning for Developing Countries workshop.</i>
</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is classification accuracy (the proportion of correctly predicted samples).</p>
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For every digit in the test set</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: <b>Id</b> and <b>Category</b>.</p>
<p>An example of a valid submission would be</p>
<pre>Id,Category<br>00000,6<br>00001,9<br>00002,10<br>.<br>.<br>.<br>09999,1</pre>","# Dataset Description

<p>The data consists of two files: <code>train.zip</code> and <code>test.zip</code>. The former file, <code>train.zip</code>, contains 60000 bitmaps of size 28x28, and is organized into folders <code>1</code>, <code>2</code>, ... <code>10</code>, each containing 6000 examples of the respective symbol. The folders are indeed <code>1</code>, <code>2</code>, ... <code>10</code> as Ethiopic does not have the digit <code>0</code>.</p>
<p>The second zip file, <code>test.zip</code> contains 10000 test digits, for which you should predict the respective classes. Each filename in the test.zip refers to the column <code>Id</code> in the submission csv file, i.e., from the file <code>00000.jpg</code> you should generate a row like <code>00000,6</code> into the submission file.</p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.zip</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sample_submission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>
The sample submission was created with following 4 lines of code.
<pre>
with open(""sample_submission.csv"", ""w"") as fp: 
    fp.write(""Id,Category\n"") 
    for idx in range(10000): 
        fp.write(f""{idx:05},{random.randint(1,10)}\n"") 
</pre>",True,True
3479,recunoasterea-scris-de-mana,"# Description

<p>?n Republica Moldova, alegerile implic? completarea par?ial manual? a diferitor formulare ?i hartii care sunt ulterior procesate. Calculele manuale sau semi-automate necesit? mult timp ?i sunt sensibile la eroarea uman?. </p>
<p>Concursul acesta amical propune ca set de date dreptunghiurile completate manual cu cifre din procesele verbale de la alegerile locale din 2019 din Republica Moldova. Scopul concursului este de a identifica corect numerele reprezentate ?i a le transforma ?n format electronic.</p>
<p> Algoritmul cel mai eficient ar putea face parte dintr-un produs final care ar u?ura prelucrarea proceselor verbale per total ?n viitor. </p>
<p>Exemplu process verbal de la alegeri</p>
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F4546354%2F2189be840b6a7f16a4ac1b944323eacb%2Fimg.png?generation=1604588919661097&amp;alt=media)

<p> Fii parte din schimbare! </p>
<p> Concurs organizat de grupul <a href=""https://www.facebook.com/groups/aiinactiune/""> Inteligen?a Artificial? ?n Ac?iune </a>
</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>Metoda de evaluare pentru aceast? competi?ie este <strong>Media Levenshtein (Levenshtain Mean)</strong>. Distan?a Levenshtein(sau distanta de editare) reprezint? num?rul de caractere care trebuie schimbate pentru a ajunge la rezultatul corect. Levenshtein Mean e media distan?elor Levenshtain pentru fiecare rezultat.</p>
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F4546354%2F3ae584039c5e043d47cb8e7d3eb70739%2Fdownload.png?generation=1604589269562976&alt=media)

<h2>Formatul fi?ierelor depuse</h2>
<p>Fi?ierul final e un .csv cu o coloan? ?image¡± care reprezint? denumirea imaginii (extensia inclus?) ?i o coloan? ?label¡± care reprezint? num?rul din dreptunghi.</p>
<p>Fi?ierele cu prezicerile trebuie s? aib? urm?torul header</p>
<pre>image, Expected</pre>","# Dataset Description

<p>Pentru a u?ura sarcina, din procesele verbale au fost deja extrase dreptunghiurile care con?in c?su?ele cu cifre. Scopul concursului e de a identificare num?rul din dreptunghiuri, ?inand cont de faptul c? unele c?su?e ar putea fi goale.</p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train</strong> - setul de antrenament (imaginile cu un dreptunghi cu c?su?e goale sau cu numere) </li>
<li><strong>test</strong> - setul de test (imaginile cu un dreptunghi cu c?su?e goale sau cu numere)</li>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - etichetele pentru setul de antrenament </li>
<li><strong>samplesubmission.csv</strong> - exemplu cum trebuie sa arate predictiile pentru imaginile de testare</li>
</ul>",True,True
