3488,fit3181-5215,"# Description

<p>This is the home page of the competition. The competition is organized for FIT3181 and 5215: Deep Learning unit at Monash University. The students who are interested in can join in this competition.
</p><p>If you are in the top 10, you will be awarded 5 points in your assignment 2, while if you are in the top 3, you will be awarded 10 points in your assignment 2.
</p><p>Regarding the competition task, you can utilize any ML and DL techniques to train your model with the aim to obtain as highest as possible performance on a testing dataset. Below are some recommendations:
</p><li> You can use the training and valid sets provided in assignment 2 to train and fine-tune your models. </li>
- You can take advantage of pre-trained Word2Vec, Bert, and so on to boost up the performance.
- You can apply boosting or ensembling techniques to improve performance.
-  We do not restrict the techniques you apply. Be flexible and creative to propose your own way to train your models.
<p></p><p>Please note that for those who join in this competition, in conjunction with your main assignment jupyter notebook file, you need to submit your trained model and a pdf document that describes how you train your model.
</p><p>Hope that you enjoy this competition. Have funs!</p>
