3532,umich-si650-ir-based-chat-bot,"# Description

You will build and evaluate a chatbot using the ground truth dataset of conversations you have created.

You will be provided with a list of message ids for remaining annotated queries and you will upload your top 10 most relevant responses with their response id for each message id.

You are free to use any form of relevance scoring, including using off-the-shelf IR libraries to compute relevance. However, you cannot use any existing chatbot library. 

<img src=""https://blog-assets.freshworks.com/freshdesk/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/17172638/chatbot.png"" alt=""Markdown Monster icon"" style=""float: left; margin-right: 10px"">
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation pages describes how submissions will be scored and how students should format their submissions.</p>
<hr>
<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is 
<a href=""https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discounted_cumulative_gain#Normalized_DCG"">NDCG</a> (Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain) @ k, where k = 10. The <code>nDCG</code> value, commonly used in evaluating Web search, measures  the effectiveness of the search engine algorithms. The <code>nDCG</code> is given by:</p>
<p>\[nDCG_{k} = \frac{DCG_{k}}{IDCG_{k}}\ \]</p>
<p>\[ IDCG_{k} = \sum_{i=1}^{|rel_{k}|} \frac{2^{rel_{i}}-1}{log_{2}(i+1)}\]</p>
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p>The submission should be a list of <code>queryid-docid</code> ranked from top to bottom according to their relevance (i.e., the top docid is the most relevant document for a the specified query). Each line should be a single <code>queryid-docid</code>. The columns are as follows: <code>queryid</code> is the query number (1..50), <code>docid</code> is the id of the document retrieved.</p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>queryid,docid<br>1,1<br></pre>","# Dataset Description

In this challenge, you are given a list of message ids for remaining annotated queries. The goal is to upload your top 10 most relevant responses (with their response id) for each message id.

##File descriptions
* aggregated-hw3-rating.test.csv - message id and response id
  * message_id - the id of the query
  * response_id - the id of several responses",True,True
