3556,itml-dev,"# Description

The below dataset consists of a few thousands of commercial flights, where for each one of them is described by a set of features (e.g. departure and destination airports etc) . Each flight is also characterized by a variable related to the number of passengers. Each variable value denotes a specific range of the number of passengers. For some flights, this variable value is known, for each it's not. The goal of this test is to predict the variable values for the flights where this information is unknown.
----------------------
# Evaluation

*Solution Submission:*
After you've designed and ran your algorithm and you've predicted the passenger category for each flight of the test set, you must submit your proposed solution to the Kaggle platform so it can be evaluated. Specifically, there is a *Submit Predictions* option in the main screen where you can upload your predictions. Your predictions must be included in a file where each line corresponds to the flight in the respective line of the test set. Please check the submission sample to get an idea of what your submission should look like.

*Evaluation Score:*
The evaluation of your predictions will be calculated based on mean F-score. Mean F1-score takes values between 0 and 1. The higher the score, the better the classifier that predicted these values is.",# Dataset Description,True,True
