<p>The file should contain a scan index and localization result like below:</p>
<pre>id, x, y, z, yaw, pitch, row<br>1,0,0,1,0,0,1<br>2, ...<br>3, ...<br>.<br>.<br>.<br></pre>","# Dataset Description

<p>We only provide the sample submission for you to understand the format you need to follow. To get the rosbag and other data, please download them from the slide.</p>
<p>For this case, you need to submit your result with <strong>389 rows</strong> data.</p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>id</strong> - the id of the LiDAR scan sequence</li>
<li><strong>x</strong> - translation transformation</li>
<li><strong>y</strong> - translation transformation</li>
<li><strong>z</strong> - translation transformation</li>
<li><strong>yaw</strong> - rotation transformation</li>
<li><strong>pitch</strong> - rotation transformation</li>
<li><strong>roll</strong> - rotation transformation</li>
</ul>",True,True
3596,nyc-airbnb-rental-price,"# Description

<p>This competition is an in-class competition for the course ""Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning (Fall 2020)"" in Renmin University of China.</p>
<p>The competition is to predict the rental prices for listed rooms or appartments in New York City on the Inside Airbnb site.</p>
<h2>Acknowledgements</h2>
<p>The data was adapted from the dataset <a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/dgomonov/new-york-city-airbnb-open-data""> New York City Airbnb Open Data</a>, which was originally from the <a href=""http://insideairbnb.com/"">Inside Airbnb site</a>.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is <a href=""https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root-mean-square_deviation""> Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)</a>.</p>
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p>For <strong>every listing</strong> in the test dataset, submission files should contain two columns: <strong><i>id</i></strong> and <strong><i>price</i></strong>, i.e. the id and the predicted price for the listing.</p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>id,price<br>13055,110<br>2970,80<br>27364,60<br>......</pre>","# Dataset Description

<p>Since 2008, guests and hosts have used Airbnb to expand on traveling possibilities and present more unique, personalized way of experiencing the world. This data set contains summary information and metrics for listings in New York City on the Inside Airbnb site in 2019. It is good for exploration, visualizations and predictions. The goal is to predict the rental price for each listed room or appartment using all kinds of its information.</p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>NYC_Airbnb_train.csv</strong> - the training dataset</li>
<li><strong>NYC_Airbnb_test.csv</strong> - the test dataset</li>
<li><strong>NYC_Airbnb_baseline.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<p>There are 16 variables:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>id</strong> - listing ID</li>
<li><strong>name</strong> - name of the listing</li>
<li><strong>host_id</strong> - host ID</li>
<li><strong>host_name</strong> - name of the host</li>
<li><strong>neighbourhood_group</strong> - location</li>
<li><strong>neighbourhood</strong> - area</li>
<li><strong>latitude</strong> - latitude coordinates</li>
<li><strong>longitude</strong> - longitude coordinates</li>
<li><strong>room_type</strong> - listing space type</li>
<li><strong>minimum_nights</strong> - amount of nights minimum</li>
<li><strong>number_of_reviews</strong> - number of reviews</li>
<li><strong>last_review</strong> - latest review</li>
<li><strong>reviews_per_month</strong> - number of reviews per month</li>
<li><strong>calculated_host_listings_count</strong> - amount of listing per host</li>
<li><strong>availability_365</strong> - number of days when listing is available for booking</li>
<li><strong>price</strong> - price in dollars</li>
</ul>",True,True
3597,iplml2020,"# Description

Bienvenue dans le projet Machine Learning IPL 2020!
