3610,statlearning-sjtu-2020,"# Description

<p>The aim of this project is to classify the electrocardiogram(ECG) data. You are provided with labeled ECG traininig data and need to use several machine learning methods to predict the labels on ECG test data.</p>

<h2>A-T-T-E-N-T-I-O-N:</h2>
<h4>Deadline for submitting your predictions on Kaggle: 2020/1/3 11:59PM.</h4>

<h4>Deadline for uploading your report and code via our course website: 2021/1/6 11:59PM.</h4>


<h3>Before submitting your predictions:</h3>
Please update your name with ""STUDENTID_NAME"" before submitting your predictions. You can update your name in the ""Team"" tab.


<h3>About the leaderboard and submissions:</h3>
Any extra training data or the code can not reproduce the score is regarded as CHEATING. We will check the results and the submissions after the deadline, PLEASE DO NOT CHEAT.

There are two submissions allowed for each person every day. Please carefully arrange the schedule of your submissions.

Since the ECG test data is limited (70 test case in total, 21 test cases in Public Board and 49 test caes in Private Board) , there may exist bias between the score in Public Board and Private Board. A suggestion is to split the ECG train data into traininig set and validation set to verify your model in private. 

Don't be too nervous about your rank on the leaderboard and we jus use it as a reference. The scores are just the proof that your work is valid and sound. We will judge your project **mainly** by the project report. 


<h3>Requirements for the project report:</h3>
You have to try at least three different methods(we highly recommend the methods which are mentioned in the class), and explain the details about your methods. Please select the submissions from the valid submissions and put the screenshot of the selected submissions in your project report. You can find all your submissions in ""My Submissions"" tab. Your results that mentioned in your reports should be the results on private leaderboard, instead of your results on public leaderboard.

The length of the project report has no hard limitations. The project report can be written in Chinese or English. A recommended length is 10 pages for one column if you write your report in latex with 10pt font size in English.

The codes for your submissions are required for the project. Please also provide the scripts or instructions to run your codes in a readme.txt.

Requirements for uploading:
You need to zip and upload the following files before deadline:
¢Ùyour report ¢Úyour codes(without pretrain model) ¢Ûa readme.txt, which includes the scripts or instructions to run your codes.
The final zip file should be uploaded via our course website.


Deadline of this project:
Deadline for submitting your predictions on Kaggle: 2020/1/3 11:59PM
Deadline for uploading your report and code via our course website: 2021/1/6 11:59PM

----------------------
# Evaluation

<h2>Metric</h2>
<p>This competition is evaluated on the categorization accuracy of your predictions (the percentage of images you get correct).</p>

<h2>Submission File </h2>
<p>For every id, submission files should contain two columns: id and categories.
The id for data is its filename.
The categories should be an integer representing the predicted label for id.</p>

<pre>Id mapping:
832076.mat: 832076
833856.mat: 833856
834869.mat: 834869
</pre>
<pre>Category mapping:
