3664,stat441datachallenge2,"# Description

<p>How good can a machine classify a set of images? In this Data Challenge 2, you are given the values of pixels from a large set of fashion images. Your task is to develop a model that can accurately predict the type of the fashion object that each image depicts.</p>

<h2>Dataset</h2>
<p>Our fashion image dataset contains the following variables:</p>
<p>?	Label: the true class of each image (class of the fashion object).</p>
<p>?	ID :  the ID of each fashion image.</p>
<p>?	pixel 1- 784: the pixels from each fashion image.</p>

<p> The image below shows how the label and the true images are related: </p>
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F1364433%2F5d27f6cf8e1b237cf95f3dfa1a0a35f7%2FDataset-Images-with-Labels-and-Description-II-LITERATURE-REVIEW-In-image.jpg?generation=1606005399230374&alt=media)





<h2>Submission Details</h2>
<p> Unlike the last time, the evaluation criteria for this data challenge is the accuracy rate on the test image. Your submission csv file should include 2 columns, where the first column is the variable `ID` (ID of the test images), and the second column is the variable `label` which indicates the predicted class for each image. </p>

<p> The submission csv file should look like the following:</p>
<pre>ID, label<br>1473,3<br>6306,3</pre>

