3690,ifest-20-misig,"# Description

Art lights up the monotonous continuity of our lives, especially in current times. Songs, movies, books, podcasts, and much more, which are some of the many examples of artistic works, were a boon to everyone stuck at home in this pandemic.

Today, your task as an ML expert, is to predict the monetary returns (recovered) made by such works. The returns can be based on several factors, but, here we primarily consider, the following factors:-
- Estd. Amount Invested
- Language
- Public Opinion Index
- Length
- Ratings (Mean)
- Number of Surveyees
- Amount Recovered

So, go ahead and create the most accurate models.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The Evaluation Metric for this contest is RMSE (Root Mean Square Error). 

For submission format, please refer to the sample.csv file available under the Data tab. Your submission should also be in the same format.","# Dataset Description

The data description for the contest is as given below:- 

Files provided:- 

- train.csv: The Training set 
- test.csv: The Testing set 
- sample.csv: Your submission should be in this format 

Columns List (in order):- 

- train.csv: Item_Index, Estd. Amount Invested, Language, Public Opinion Index, Length, Ratings (Mean), Number of Surveyees, Amount Recovered (to be predicted) 

- test.csv: Item_Index, Estd. Amount Invested, Language, Public Opinion Index, Length, Ratings (Mean), Number of Surveyees 

- sample.csv: Item_Index, Amount Recovered (your submission should also have the same columns in same order)",True,True
