3692,predict-marks-this-is-a-test-competition,"# Description

<p>This data approach student achievement in secondary education of two Portuguese schools. The data attributes include student grades, demographic, social and school-related features and it was collected by using school reports and questionnaires. Datasets are provided regarding the performance in Portuguese language (por). In [Cortez and Silva, 2008], the dateset was modelled under binary/five-level classification and regression tasks. Important note: the target attribute G3 has a strong correlation with attributes G2 and G1. This occurs because G3 is the final year grade (issued at the 3rd period), while G1 and G2 correspond to the 1st and 2nd period grades. It is more difficult to predict G3 without G2 and G1, but such prediction is much more useful.</p>

<hr>

<h2>Content</h2>
<p>The data set is from the UCL Machine Learning Repository.</p>
(https://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/datasets/Student+Performance)

<p>This is a test competition.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<h2>Goal</h2>
<p>It is your job to predict the marks a student will earn in the exam.For each case in test set you should predict a value between 0 and 20 for the variable.</p>
<hr>
<h2>Metric</h2>
<p>Submissions are evaluated on Mean Absolute Error(MAE) between the predicted value and the observed marks.</p><p>

</p><p>Read more about MAE...</p>(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_squared_error)
<hr>
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>

Id, G3
461, 16
462, 18.2
463, 17.5
etc.

<h3>Important</h3>
**<p>In your submission file the Id attribute should start from 519 (similar as the Id attribute given in the test dateset).</p>**

<hr>
<p><b>Competitors should work on their local machines and submit only the submission(.csv) file.(Do not work on Kaggle kernels. ??)</b></p>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>id</strong> - an anonymous id unique to a given students</li>
<li><strong>school</strong> - student's school (binary: ""GP"" - Gabriel Pereira or ""MS"" - Mousinho da Silveira) </li>
<li><strong>sex</strong> - student's sex (binary: ""F"" - female or ""M"" - male)</li>
<li><strong>age</strong> - student's age (numeric: from 15 to 22)</li>
<li><strong>address</strong> - student's home address type (binary: ""U"" - urban or ""R"" - rural)</li>
<li><strong>famsize</strong> - family size (binary: ""LE3"" - less or equal to 3 or ""GT3"" - greater than 3) </li>
<li><strong>Pstatus</strong> - parent's cohabitation status (binary: ""T"" - living together or ""A"" - apart)</li>
<li><strong>Medu</strong> - mother's education (numeric: 0 - none,  1 - primary education (4th grade), 2 ¨C 5th to 9th grade, 3 ¨C secondary education or 4 ¨C higher education)</li>
<li><strong>Fedu</strong> - father's education (numeric: 0 - none,  1 - primary education (4th grade), 2 ¨C 5th to 9th grade, 3 ¨C secondary education or 4 ¨C higher education)) </li>
<li><strong>Mjob</strong> -mother's job (nominal: ""teacher"", ""health"" care related, civil ""services"" (e.g. administrative or police), ""at_home"" or ""other"")</li>
<li><strong>Fjob </strong> - father's job (nominal: ""teacher"", ""health"" care related, civil ""services"" (e.g. administrative or police), ""at_home"" or ""other"")</li>
<li><strong>reason</strong> - reason to choose this school (nominal: close to ""home"", school ""reputation"", ""course"" preference or ""other"")</li>
<li><strong>guardian</strong> -student's guardian (nominal: ""mother"", ""father"" or ""other"") </li>
<li><strong>traveltime</strong> - home to school travel time (numeric: 1 - <15 min., 2 - 15 to 30 min., 3 - 30 min. to 1 hour, or 4 - >1 hour)</li>
<li><strong>studytime</strong> - weekly study time (numeric: 1 - <2 hours, 2 - 2 to 5 hours, 3 - 5 to 10 hours, or 4 - >10 hours)</li>
<li><strong>failures</strong> - number of past class failures (numeric: n if 1<=n<3, else 4)</li>
<li><strong>schoolsup</strong> - extra educational support (binary: yes or no)</li>
<li><strong>famsup</strong> - family educational support (binary: yes or no)</li>
<li><strong>paid</strong> - extra paid classes within the course subject (Portuguese) (binary: yes or no)</li>
<li><strong>activities</strong> - extra-curricular activities (binary: yes or no)</li>
<li><strong>nursery</strong> - attended nursery school (binary: yes or no)</li>
<li><strong>higher</strong> - wants to take higher education (binary: yes or no</li>
<li><strong>internet</strong> -  Internet access at home (binary: yes or no)</li>
<li><strong>romantic</strong> -with a romantic relationship (binary: yes or no)</li>
<li><strong>famrel</strong> - quality of family relationships (numeric: from 1 - very bad to 5 - excellent)</li>
<li><strong>freetime </strong> - free time after school (numeric: from 1 - very low to 5 - very high)</li>
<li><strong>goout</strong> - going out with friends (numeric: from 1 - very low to 5 - very high)</li>
<li><strong>Dalc</strong> - workday alcohol consumption (numeric: from 1 - very low to 5 - very high)</li>
<li><strong> Walc</strong> - weekend alcohol consumption (numeric: from 1 - very low to 5 - very high)</li>
<li><strong>health</strong> - current health status (numeric: from 1 - very bad to 5 - very good)</li>
<li><strong>absences</strong> - number of school absences (numeric: from 0 to 93)</li>
</ul>

<p>These grades are related with the course subject, Portuguese:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>G1</strong> - first period grade (numeric: from 0 to 20)</li>
<li><strong>G2</strong> - second period grade (numeric: from 0 to 20)</li>
<li><strong>G3</strong> - third period grade (numeric: from 0 to 20)</li>
</ul>",True,True
3693,mlds-comp-2020,"# Description

Hi! Welcome to the 2021 MLDS semester competition! This year¡¯s competition asks students to combine knowledge in image recognition, sequence methods, and encryption. 

Read more about the competition and how the dataset was generated here: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mOcsUur3j7XK1M0MokYw9_KbPWxV6hIV/view

The competition will be hosted on Kaggle and finalists will be chosen to present to the club.

Participants will be evaluated on:

- Kaggle Leader Board Placement
- A report detailing model/methodology
- Presentation

Competition Timeline:
-  Currently we¡¯re looking to end the competition in the first few weeks of the Spring semester, we¡¯ll let you know when we settle on a concrete date!


Prizes:

In scholarship or tech items of equivalent value!

1st place - $500
2nd place - $300
3rd place - $200

----------------------
# Timeline

UPDATED 2/20/2021 - Kaggle Contest will end on 2/28/2021 instead of 2/21/2021
----------------------
# Prizes

In scholarship or tech items of equivalent value!

1st place - $500
2nd place - $300
3rd place - $200","# Dataset Description

The training data file provides you information with which you can train your model. It provides values for each of the pixels as well as the gold label for the value. 

The predictions data file provides only values for each pixels for which you must generate predictions for and submit.",True,True
