3701,salestimeseriesforecasting-afcs2020,"# Description

Forecasting predicts the number of sales in the future. Having the right amount of products in stock is a core challenge in retail. A good forecast makes sure there are enough of your favorite products in stock, even if you come to the store late in the evening.

In this competition, you will use a subset of M5 Forecasting - Accuracy hierarchical sales data from Walmart at one store, CA3 in the State of California, the world¡¯s largest company by revenue, to forecast daily sales for the next 28 days. The data include item level, department, product categories, and store details. In addition, it has explanatory variables such as price, promotions, day of the week, and special events. Together, this robust dataset can be used to improve forecasting accuracy.

<h2>Acknowledgements</h2>
<p>We thank Professor Spyros Makridiakis and Evangelos Spigliotis, Ph.D. for providing this dataset.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<hr>
<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is <a href=""https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root-mean-square_deviation""> RMSE-Score</a>. The RMSE score, is commonly used as a measure of accuracy, to compare forecasting errors of different models for a particular dataset and not between datasets, as it is scale-dependent. </p>
Submissions are evaluated using Root Mean Squared Error(RMSE). For each row and id, you must submit your HOBBIES_ 2_ X_ CA_ 3 predictions. 

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For every Group in the dataset</strong>, each row contains an id that is a concatenation of an item_id and a store_id, which is either validation (corresponding to the Public leaderboard), or evaluation (corresponding to the Private leaderboard). You are predicting 28 forecast days (F1-F28) of items sold for each row. For the validation rows, this corresponds to d_1914 - d_1941, and for the evaluation rows, this corresponds to d_1942 - d_1969. 

</p><p>The files must have a header and should look like the following:</p><p>

</p><p>id,F1,...F28</p><p>
</p><p>HOBBIES_2_001_CA_3_validation,0,...,2</p><p>
</p><p>HOBBIES_2_002_CA_3_validation,2,...,11</p><p>
</p>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
The historical data range from 2011-01-29 to 2016-06-19. Thus, the Hobbies products have a (maximum) selling history of 1,9412 days / 5.4 years (test data of h=28 days not included).

<li><strong>calendar_afcs2020.csv</strong> - Contains information about the dates on which the products are sold.</li>
<li><strong>sales_train_validation_afcs2020.csv</strong> - Contains the historical daily unit sales data per product and store [d_1 - d_1913]</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission_afcs2020.csv</strong> - The correct format for submissions. Reference the Evaluation tab for more info</li>
<li><strong>sell_prices_afcs2020.csv</strong> - Contains information about the price of the products sold per store and date</li>
<li><strong>sales_train_evaluation_afcs2020.csv</strong> - supplemental information about the data</li>",True,True
