3732,online-advertising-challenge-fall-2020,"# Description

<h3><strong>Advertising Challenge</strong></h3>
<p>Display advertising is a billion dollar effort and one of the central uses of machine learning on the Internet. However, its data and methods are usually kept under lock and key. In this research competition, Mail.Ru is sharing a week¡¯s worth of data for you to develop models predicting ad click-through rate (CTR). Given a user and the page he is visiting, what is the probability that he will click on a given ad?</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>Submissions are evaluated using the <a href=""http://wiki.fast.ai/index.php/Log_Loss"">Logarithmic Loss</a> (smaller is better).</p>
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">Id,Click<br />1,0.1<br />2,0.9<br />3,0.4<br />4,0.3<br />5,0.8<br />6,0.2<br />7,0.4<br />etc.<br /></span></pre>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train_adv.tar.gz</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test_adv.tar.gz</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>sample_adv.txt</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>timestamp</strong> - timestamp</li>
<li><strong>label</strong> - click or not click</li>
<li><strong>C1-12 </strong>- categorial features</li>
<li><strong>l1-2 </strong>- counters</li>
<li><strong>CG1-3 </strong>- groups of categorial features</li>
</ul>",True,True
