<pre>id,fres_am<br>1,si<br></pre>",# Dataset Description,True,True
3765,creditriskinbankingxgboost,"# Description

<p>Financial institutions usually use statistical models to estimate credibility of applicants for a loan. Applicant with the higest risk are declined, those who are appoved can be assigned different available product parameters based on their score.</p>

<p>Using provided data set, create an extreme gradient boosting model, that will serve for assessment of applicants creditbility. Quality of the model will be measured by its separation power - Gini coefficient.</p>

<p>To pass the competition sucessfully, competitiors should reach Gini higher than 48.5 Gini (equivalent to AUC 0.7425) on the public leaderboard.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>
Performance of the logistic regression model will be measure by its power to separate good and bad clients - Gini coefficient.
</p>
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p>
For every out of sample application ID (SK_ID_CURR), submission files should contain two columns: SK_ID_CURR and estimated probability of default or its logit transformation (score).
</p>
<p>The file should contain a header, be in cvs file with comma as a separator. First column is named SK_ID_CURR and the second one SCORE.</p>
<pre>SK_ID_CURR,SCORE<br>1111111,0.1<br></pre>","# Dataset Description

<p>Data file data_devsample.csv holds data to be used for development of the model. Binary variable describing, if the client repaid his or her obligations succesfully is in column TARGET.<\p>

<p>Data file data_to_score.csv contains data sample to be scored by the model.<\p>",True,True
