3776,unstructuredl0,"# Description

<p>The given text data contains open source reviews of a product. There are 2 problem statements:
</p><h3>I. Topic Modelling</h3>
<p>Categorize the reviews into the following topics:</p>
1. Value for Money 
2. Delivery Service
3. Absorbency
4. Comfort and Softness
<p></p><h3>II. Sentiment Analysis</h3>
Classify the polarity of each review into positive and negative

<h3>Steps to Follow</h3>
1. Obtain data for the 2 problem statements by splitting data.csv using column 'problem\_flag' into SentimentAnalysis and TopicModelling
2. Solve separately for both problems and tag the output into column 'predicted'
3. Append both scored datasets to obtain the same format as step 1 with the additional column 'predicted' (You may refer to SampleSubmission.csv file for reference)
4. Submit!

NOTE:  Upload your Assessment Notebook with  FileName YourName\_Submission (In case using multiple files, upload a zip file)
https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScgrm_WTEA7TQQMpdi79FQ-jGLIKdTNEi_MZ1WSuXf2zs689Q/viewform?usp=sf_link
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is Mean F1-Score. The F1 score, commonly used in information retrieval, measures accuracy using the statistics precision p and recall r. Precision is the ratio of true positives (tp) to all predicted positives (tp + fp). Recall is the ratio of true positives to all actual positives (tp + fn). The F1 score is given by:


$$F1 =2\frac{p.r}{p+r}$$  

where  $$p=\frac{tp}{tp+fp}$$,  $$r=\frac{tp}{tp+fn}$$ 

Submission Format
For every review in the test set, submission files should contain two columns: id and predicted.

The submission file should contain the column headers: id, predicted

Example:
id, predicted
sent\_tm\_1, value\_for\_money
sent\_sa\_1, positive","# Dataset Description

**What files do I need?**

You'll need data.csv which contains the input data, Use same data for predictions, you can refer to SampleSubmission.csv to understand the output format

**What is the data format?**

Each row contains 'id', 'review', 'problem_flag'
 
(id: unique Id for the text, review: the text, problem_flag: type of problem)

**What am I predicting?**

You will be predicting the label (topics) for the given corpus of reviews, and Sentiment label (polarity). Make sure you submit your predictions with correct label names referenced in the description.

**For example:**

id, predicted

sent_tm_1, value_for_money

sent_tm_2, comfort_and_softness

sent_tm_3, value_for_money

sent_tm_4, absorbency

sent_sa_1, positive

sent_sa_2, negative",True,True
