3796,vislab-grapeleaf-competition,"# Description

<p>The miller lab has taken pictures of thousands of different grapeleaves taken at different period of growth. These leaves come from four different types of rootstocks (Own, 3309C, 1103P, and SO4). There are no clear visual differences between the leaves.</p>

<p>You task is to try to train a program that is able to accurately classify a leaf to one of the four possible rootstocks. The training data set has 1138 leaves in each class along with 568 leaves in the testing set. This means that random chance is exactly 25%</p><p></p>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>training_images</strong> - the training set containing four subfiles with for each of the rootstock classifications</li>
<li><strong>testing_images</strong> - the testing set containing four subfiles for each of the rootstock classifications</li>

</ul>",True,True
3797,computationalintelligencesc2020,"# Description

<h1> Introduction </h1>
Welcome to the competition. This competition is dedicated to fo SC Students in the Computational Intelligence course at FCIS. The goal of the competition is to build deep learning models that can recognize 7 categories of natural images.
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>You have to submit a file in CSV format named as 'submit.csv'.</p>
<hr>
<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is the overall accuracy </p><p> 

</p><h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong> The file contains 2 column, the first column is the name of the test image, while the second column is your predicted label for this image </strong> </p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>Image,Label<br>1020.jpg,0<br></pre>","# Dataset Description

<h1> Dataset description </h1>
<p>
This dataset contains natural images of size 150x150 for 6 categories (buildings, forest, glacier, mountain, sea, and street). The training set contains 6 folders, around 2300 for each category. The testing set contains 3050 images. The goal is to build a model that can recognize the category of each image in the testing set.
<h2>Files description</h2>
<ul>
<li> Scenes training set.rar</strong> - contains the training set</li>
<li> Google drive link (for Colab users) </strong> <p> [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1Jff904-zKuWeL45jbtb6Jsxg7-_ePkzk?usp=sharing] </li>
<li><strong>Scenes testing test.rar</strong> - contains the testing set</li>
<li> Google drive link (for Colab users) </strong> <p> [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1_5lhlTGmZcA5HZ_03dGskwvRutSl893e?usp=sharing] </li>
<li><strong>submit.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
<li><strong>names.csv</strong> this file contains the IDs of the six categories</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Image</strong> - the name of image</li>
<li><strong>Label</strong> - the predicted label</li>
</ul>",True,True
