3800,intro-to-ml-assignment-2,"# Description

<p>This assignment requires you to design your own face recognizer using any technique taught in the classes. You can use the python packages such as sklearn, TensorFlow, OpenCV, NumPy, ..., and so on. However, you are not allowed to copy the source code of the recognizer from any other person.</p>
### Stuff you should hand in
Besides submitting your answer file here for accuracy evaluation, you should also submit the following stuff to the –|ÈAeŒWÔ·£º
1. The **source code** of your face recognizer with clear comments
2. A brief **report **(written with Markdown markup language on HackMD) which describes your method, results, problems solved during development, and a summary about what you have learned from the assignment.
3. If you can design a simple **GUI program** that allows a user to load an image file (from the file manager) and output the recognized person, then you'll get a bonus of ?? **15 points** ??  in the final grade evaluation.
4. It is recommended to prepare a **movie file** demonstrating how your program works on testing the test files (showing how the output, with your student ID, is generated from your program). You will get a bonus of ?? **5 points**??  if such a movie file is provided.

### Important: If you do not use your student ID as the username on Kaggle, you MUST clearly note in the report what your username is on Kaggle in your REPORT when submitting the stuff to the –|ÈAeŒWÔ·. Otherwise, you will get zero point if CCC cannot find your student ID on the Kaggle leaderboard.
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is the recognition accuracy </p>","# Dataset Description

<p>The data is a zip file containing a zipped directory `train`. Please get the zip file from the course page on the Google classroom.</p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train_label.csv</strong> - the training set with both image filenames and the corresponding labels for your model training,</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set with only image filenames for testing the image files in the specified sequence,</li>
<li><strong>sample_submission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>file_id</strong> - the id number contained in the image filename,</li>
<li><strong>label</strong> - the label of the corresponding image file</li>
</ul>",True,True
