3817,applai-global-contest-a2,"# Description

<p style=""margin: 0px 0px 10.5px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-numeric: inherit; font-variant-east-asian: inherit; font-weight: 400; font-stretch: inherit; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: Inter, sans-serif; vertical-align: baseline; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7); letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"">Features are computed from a digitized image of a fine needle aspirate (FNA) of a breast mass. They describe the characteristics of the cell nuclei present in the image.<br>n the 3-dimensional space is that described in: [K. P. Bennett and O. L. Mangasarian: &quot;Robust Linear Programming Discrimination of Two Linearly Inseparable Sets&quot;, Optimization Methods and Software 1, 1992, 23-34].</p>
<p style=""margin: 10.5px 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-numeric: inherit; font-variant-east-asian: inherit; font-weight: 400; font-stretch: inherit; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: Inter, sans-serif; vertical-align: baseline; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7); letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;""><br></p>
<p style=""margin: 10.5px 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-numeric: inherit; font-variant-east-asian: inherit; font-weight: 400; font-stretch: inherit; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: Inter, sans-serif; vertical-align: baseline; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7); letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"">Attribute Information:</p>
<p style=""margin: 10.5px 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-numeric: inherit; font-variant-east-asian: inherit; font-weight: 400; font-stretch: inherit; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: Inter, sans-serif; vertical-align: baseline; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7); letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"">1) ID number<br>2) Diagnosis (M = malignant, B = benign)<br>3-32)</p>
<p style=""margin: 10.5px 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-numeric: inherit; font-variant-east-asian: inherit; font-weight: 400; font-stretch: inherit; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: Inter, sans-serif; vertical-align: baseline; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7); letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"">Ten real-valued features are computed for each cell nucleus:</p>
<p style=""margin: 10.5px 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-numeric: inherit; font-variant-east-asian: inherit; font-weight: 400; font-stretch: inherit; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: Inter, sans-serif; vertical-align: baseline; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7); letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"">a) radius (mean of distances from the center to points on the perimeter)<br>b) texture (standard deviation of gray-scale values)<br>c) perimeter<br>d) area<br>e) smoothness (local variation in radius lengths)<br>f) compactness (perimeter^2 / area - 1.0)<br>g) concavity (severity of concave portions of the contour)<br>h) concave points (number of concave portions of the contour)<br>i) symmetry<br>j) fractal dimension (&quot;coastline approximation&quot; - 1)</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p> submission files should contain two columns: id and diagnosis.</p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>id,diagnosis<br>1,1<br></pre>","# Dataset Description

<p style=""margin: 0px 0px 10.5px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-variant-numeric: inherit; font-variant-east-asian: inherit; font-weight: 400; font-stretch: inherit; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: Inter, sans-serif; vertical-align: baseline; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7); letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"">Features are computed from a digitized image of a fine needle aspirate (FNA) of a breast mass. They describe the characteristics of the cell nuclei present in the image.<br>n the 3-dimensional space is that described in: [K. P. Bennett and O. L. Mangasarian: &quot;Robust Linear Programming Discrimination of Two Linearly Inseparable Sets&quot;, Optimization Methods and Software 1, 1992, 23-34].</p>
