3840,shopee-case-study-seller-ltv-ads-jan21,"# Description

# **Background**
Paid advertising is a key source of revenue for Shopee. Hence, it is important to identify important seller groups, which allow us to improve seller engagement in growing, retaining and acquiring these sellers.

# **Model Output**
As we are keen to know each seller's monthly ads expenditure for the next 3 months, the model should include ***three predicted Y labels***, one label for each forward month (FXM). For example, if the current date is 1 August 2020, the ***predicted Y labels*** are as follow:

- Y label F1M: Predicted ads expenditure for the month of August 2020
- Y label F2M: Predicted ads expenditure for the month of September 2020
- Y label F3M: Predicted ads expenditure for the month of October 2020

# **Data Definition**

## Settings 
The training and test data sets included in this study are named xx and yy respectively. These data are extracted based on the settings depicted in this chart.
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F5897968%2F699d504caa33db1cd099358881284d49%2Fregression%20settings.jpg?generation=1602577603351979&amp;alt=media)

This setting was designed to use the predicted Y value of the previous month as part of the feature set for the next month's model. For example, for Train Y 2M model, the predicted Y value of the 1m model (PRD Y 1M) is included as part of its feature set. You may follow this setting or design your own.

## Features
There are 525 columns in the data set and the data dictionary for each column is as follows:

- shop_id: This is the unique identifier for each seller
- shop_profile_x: There are 27 shop profile related features. Examples of these features include shop type (i.e. cross border, official, preferred), main item category, ratings, followers, date of registration.
- shop_behavior_x: There are 51 shop behavior related features. Examples of these features include the type of promotion tools used (i.e. product discounts, vouchers), number of logins, number of product listings. These features are extracted across different time periods (i.e. 1 week ago, 1 month ago).
- shop_performance_x: There are 73 shop performance related features. Examples of these features include number of orders, gross merchandise value (GMV), product impressions, product clicks and product views. These features are extracted across different time periods.
- organic_performance_x: There are 24 organic performance related features. Organic performance, also known as non-advertised performance, is a subset of total shop performance. Examples of these features are similar to shop_performance_x features.
- ads_performance_x: There are 171 ads performance related features. Ads performance is shop performance that result from a paid ad, and is a subset of total shop performance. Examples of these features are similar to shop_performance_x features.
- ads_behavior_x: There are 60 ads behavior related features. Examples of these features include number of active ads, number of edits (i.e. adjusting keyword, bid price) and date of ads account creation date. Some of these features are extracted across different time periods.
- ads_topup_x: There are 115 ads topup related features. Examples of these features include topup method, topup amount, date of last topup and remaining credit balance.
- ads_expense_future_1m: Actual Y Value for first forward month
- ads_expense_future_2m: Actual Y Value for second forward month
- ads_expense_future_3m: Actual Y Value for third forward month

----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this study is [Mean Absolute Error (MAE)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_absolute_error). MAE measures the absolute error between the model's predicted value and the actual value. 

As this study have three Y values, there should be a MAE score for each Y value. Your goal is to reduce the absolute error for all three Y values.

## Submission Format
Your submission should include 4 columns 
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F5897968%2Fef4a8d512701dc3a2841b896f4420d7c%2Fsample_output.JPG?generation=1602749130332046&amp;alt=media)","# Dataset Description

Train set: 201014_train_set.csv, Test set: 201015_test_set.csv",True,True
