# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is <a href=""https://towardsdatascience.com/understanding-auc-roc-curve-68b2303cc9c5""> AUC Score</a>. The ROC curve is created by plotting the true positive rate (TPR) against the false positive rate (FPR) at various threshold settings. The true-positive rate is also known as sensitivity, recall or probability of detection[7] in machine learning. The false-positive rate is also known as probability of false alarm[7] and can be calculated as (1 ? specificity). It can also be thought of as a plot of the power as a function of the Type I Error of the decision rule (when the performance is calculated from just a sample of the population, it can be thought of as estimators of these quantities). <a href=""https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic""> WIKI</a></p>

