3894,ipl-2020-player-performance,"# Description

<h2>Summary</h2>
<p>Fantasy sports in this age of technology has been a closely connected part of every particular sport community. This time we are trying to predict the player performance index of each player who participated in IPL 2020 using the delivery-by-delivery data of each ball bowled since IPL 2008 till IPL 2019</p>
<h2>Data</h2>
<ul>
<li>""Training.csv"" : File Containing various performance stats of a player in a match</li>
<li>""Matches IPL 2020.csv"" : Schedule of matches that occrued in IPL 2020</li>
<li>""IPL 2020 Squads.csv"" : Squads of each participating club/team in IPL 2020</li>
<li>""Matches IPL 2008-2019.csv"" : Schedule of matches that occrued in IPL 2020</li>
<li>""sample_submission.csv"" : Sample file. The submission file should be in this format and structure only with the values changed with those predicted ones. Please note that the player names in this file are lexographically order and this order has to be maintained in the submission file also.</li>
</ul>
<b>The Column ""Id"" in the training and submission file is of the format ""MatchID_PlayerName"" where the MatchID is a column named ""match_id"" in ""Matches IPL 2020.csv"" and ""Matches IPL 2008-2019.csv""</b>
<h2>Calculation</h2>
<p> The calculation involves evaluating the bowling points and batting points of a player in a match as per the formula : </p>
- Batting Points = Runs scored by batsman in the match + Number of boundaries + 2 * Number of sixes + 8 {if the player scores a fifty} + 16 {if player scores a hundred} - 2 {if player gets dismissed without scoring a run}
- Bowling Points = 25 * Number of wickets taken by the bowler + 8 {if player did a 4 wicket haul} + 16 {if player did 5 wicket haul} + 8 * Number of maiden overs bowled
- Total Points = Bowling Points + Batting Points
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation process is quite simple and straight-forward:

Given the predicted values in the ""Total Score"" column which represents the performance index of a player in IPL 2020 in the submission file. Let this value be ""pi_p"". And the corresponding expected value - ""pi_l""

Then the root mean square error is calculated as  : 
```math
RMSE = \sqrt{\frac{1}{n}\Sigma_{i=1}^{n}{\Big({pi_l - pi_p}\Big)^2}}
```

where 'n' is the number of players participating in IPL 2020
