3945,iowa-engr2995-2021spring-calories,"# Description


<p>You joined this challenge to work with the Calories and Exercise dataset. Your goal now will be to take the training data and use it to train a KNN and Naive Bayes regressors. After training, you need make predictions and then format your results similar to what is in the example solution file, and submit them. The final submission you make will be counted as your submission for this portion of the assignment.</p>

<p>Test and training data can be read in using the code below. Similar to your in-class assignments, make sure the data files are in the same folder as your notebook file.</p>
```
data_train_df = pd.read_csv(""TrainingFileName.csv"") 
data_train_ft = data_train_df.drop('Target', axis=1)
data_train_tgt = data_train_df[""Target""]
```

To format your solution correctly you can use the function below. It will take your prediction data and write it to CSV file, which you can then submit as your solution.

```
import csv

def writeSubmission(predictions):
    i=1
    submissionList = []
    for prediction in predictions:
        submissionList.append([str(i), str(prediction)])
        i+=1
    with open('submission.csv', 'w', newline='') as submission:
        writer = csv.writer(submission)
        writer.writerow(['id', 'Target'])
        for row in submissionList:
            writer.writerow(row)
```


<h2>Acknowledgements</h2>
<p>None right now.</p>


----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation pages describes how submissions will be scored and how students should format their submissions. You don't need a sub-title at the top (the page title appears above). For an example of a high quality evaluation page, see the 2013 KDD Cup page, which we have copied here:</p>
