3946,mds-macventures-classification-task2,"# Description

<h2> THIS COMPETITION IS ONLY MEANT FOR 2MDS STUDENTS OF CHRIST</h2>
<p>Provided you have y2_test_task2 as np.array variable, you can use following code to create submission.csv for upload (it will be created in your current working directory.</p>

<h2>Creating Submission File</h2>
<p>pd.DataFrame({""Id"": np.arange(len(y_test_task1)), ""Category"": y2_test_task2}).astype(int).to_csv(
    ""solution.csv"", index=False
)</p>

<p>In general, two columns are needed: ""Id"" (zero-numbered) and ""Category"" containing your predictions. Single best submission will be taken at the end and scored against private dataset (or you can choose one manually, it might perform better!)</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is  F1-Score. The F1 score, commonly used in information retrieval, measures accuracy using the statistics precision p and recall r. Precision is the ratio of true positives (tp) to all predicted positives (tp + fp). Recall is the ratio of true positives to all actual positives (tp + fn). The F1 score is given by:</p>
<h2> <b>2*( (precision * recall)/(precision + recall))</b></h2>
<p>The F1 metric weights recall and precision equally, and a good retrieval algorithm will maximize both precision and recall simultaneously. Thus, moderately good performance on both will be favored over extremely good performance on one and poor performance on the other.</p>","# Dataset Description

<h2>Data</h2>
<p>
Dataset is secret, you may try to find it's origins and improve your score, but this might be really hard! We have provided 3 datasets saved as np.arrays (see np.load in order to read in the data):</p>

<ul>

<li>X2_train_task2.npy - training features, shape: (199364, 28)</li>
<li>y2_train_task2.npy - training labels, shape: (199364,)</li>
<li>X2_test_task2.npy - training features, shape: (85443, 28)</li>

</ul>
 <p><b>You have to submit prediction on the features X2_test_task2 as described in Overview.</b></p>",True,True
