4015,d2l-house-price,"# Description

The task is to predict house sale prices based on the house information, such as # of bedrooms, living areas, locations, near-by schools, and the seller summary. The training dataset consists of 40K houses sold in the [bay area](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco_Bay_Area) before 05/01/2020.  The test dataset has 23K houses sold after, which is divided into two parts for the public leaderboard and private leaderboard, respectively. The private leaderboard houses were sold after the ones in the public leaderboard.
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Metric

Submissions are evaluated on [Root-Mean-Squared-Error (RMSE)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root-mean-square_deviation) between the logarithm of the predicted value and the logarithm of the observed sales price. (Taking logs means that errors in predicting expensive houses and cheap houses will affect the result equally.)

## Submission File Format

The file should contain a header and have the following format:

```
Id,Sold Price
2076037805,223500.0
153558840,835000.0
19511211,1155000.0
69302785,705000.0
82955526,1005000.0
```","# Dataset Description

## File descriptions

- `train.csv` - the training set
- `test.csv` - the test set
