4033,criots-iot-challenge,"# Description

<p>Welcome to the final question  of Criot's IoT Challenge hosted as a part of SciTech Week 2021 at IIT Hyderabad </p>

<p>In this question Criot requires you to put in your data science knowledge and help them detect outliers in the time-series data recorded from 4 types of sensors on Criot-hardware.
</p>

<p>FYI, this is an unsupervised problem statement. Hence you are expected to analyze data carefully and flag the outlier data points and turn in your submissions.</p>

<p>An outlier is defined as in when majority of the sensors show bizarre values when compared to the datapoints in its time-vicinity.<\p>
<p>Make sure you join the contest's Whatsapp group (sent in the mail) for further hints/clarifications <\p>

<p>Top performing teams must share their notebook at the end of the competition whose results should exactly match with the submitted results.<\p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p> Evaluation will be done based on both public and private leaderboard </p>

<p> AUC (Area under ROC curve) is used as an evaluation metric </p>","# Dataset Description


<p>The file 'sensor_data.csv' consists of  (randomly shuffled) time-series  readings of the sensors embedded on  criot-hardware which is installed somewhere in a room.</p>

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>sensor_data.csv</strong> - the time series data </li>
<li><strong>sample_submission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>'Id' </strong>: Unique Id for each time series data point </li>
<li><strong>'time_stamp' </strong>: HH:MM  ; H: hour , M : minutes</li>
<li><strong>'sensor_i' </strong>: Readings of raw data observed from i-th sensor (You should have known about the  sensor type through previous questions !! )</li>
<li> <strong>'flag' </strong>: 1 --> If datapoint is an outlier ; 0--> else
</ul>",True,True
