4079,spring-2021-dl-assignment-2,"# Description

<p>In this assignment you are going to develop a program that would be able to guess age (in years) of a person given his/her photo.</p>
<p>Roughly speaking, utilize your  favorite deep learning knowledge to solve this regression problem given images.</p>

----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is [RMSE](""https://www.statisticshowto.datasciencecentral.com/rmse/), Root Mean Square Error. 

RMSE is defined as : 
![RMSE = \sqrt{MSE} = \sqrt{\dfrac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^m\left(y_i-h_w(x_i)\right)^2}](https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1a1YhMSdz5TlB6CShdIWT2nHhlxluThF5&sz=w700-h130)

where, there are m samples, yi is the true/known target label for the ith sample, and hw(xi) is the predicted target for the input sample xi.
<hr />

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For every author in the dataset</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: ID and age </p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>ID,age<br />1,38.8<br /><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">2,25<br /></span><span style=""font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4em;"">etc.</span></pre>","# Dataset Description

<p>This page shows up underneath the data files. </p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>wiki_labeled</strong> - the labeled dataset, and should be used to train and test the model. The wiki_labeled/ directory will contains 60327 facial images kept in 100 folders, naming 00-99. Dimension of each image is 100 pixels by 100 pixels. </li>
<li><strong>wiki_labele.csv</strong> file, containing meta information of each of the 60327 images. It contains the following information about each of the 60327 images:</li>
<ul>
    <li> ID: identification number of the subject (starting from 2002)</li>
    <li> dob: the date of birth of the subject. (It is Matlab¡¯s datenum value calculated based on total number of days since January 0, 0000.)</li>
    <li>dob_str: the DD-MMM-YYYY format dob value.</li>
    <li> photo_taken: when the photo was taken (only the year  value)</li>
    <li> full_path: directory path, including filename of the image</li>
    <li> gender: Gender of the subject (0: female, 1: male, NaN if unknown)</li>
    <li> name: name of the subject</li>
    <li> face_location: location of the face.</li>
    <li> face_score: detector score (the higher the better). Inf implies that no face was found in the image, and the face_location then just returns the entire image.</li>
    <li> second_face_score: detector score of the face with the second highest score. This is useful to ignore images with more than one face. second_face_score is NaN (not a number) if no second face was detected.</li>
    <li> age: age of the person (in years), and was calculated based on the ¡°dob¡± value and the ¡°photo_taken¡± values.</li>
</ul>
<li><strong>wiki_judge_images</strong> containing **1409** facial images (1.png, etc.) of resolution 100x100. This is the judge/test dataset for you based on what you are going to apply your learned model to predict ages of the **1409** subjects.</li>
<li><strong>wiki_judge.csv</strong> contains some meta information about the **1409** images. For instance,  ID, full_path, gender, face_score, second_face_score. However, the information does not include ¡°age¡± field.</li>

<li><strong>sample_submission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format. Please disregard the values in the age field. They are all made up values.</li>
</ul>",True,True
4080,recognizance-2,"# Description

<h1>About Recognizance</h1>
<p>Recognizance is a Machine Learning event organised by the Department of Electrical Engineering IIT BHU, Varanasi. It has 2 Rounds. Round 2 of the competition would be from 19-20th March , 2021.</p>

<h1> Problem Statement</h1>
<p>Image-based power line detection is highly important for threat avoidance when the aerial vehicles fly in low altitude. However, it is very challenging for the requirements of high detection rates, low false alarms and real-time application.</p>
<p>Given two set of images one containing powerlines and the other not containing the power lines. Your task is to detect and classify the images as containing powerlines or not.</p>
<h1>About the Dataset</h1>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> -  the train set . Contains two columns the <b>image file</b> and the target label <b>powerline</b>.</li>
<li><strong>Train Folder</strong> - Contains powerline and No_powerline folder. Powerline folder has 5417 images containing power lines. No_powerline folder has 4583 images NOT containing the power lines.</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format. The target label is <b>powerline</b>. Solution must be submitted in this format only.  Output to be predicted as ""YES"" or ""NO""</li>
<li><strong>test folder</strong> - contains 6078 images. These images are to be classified as containing power lines or not.</li>
</ul>

<h2> Some General Guidelines </h2>

1. There will be a public leader board and a private leader board.
2. After the competition the top performers will be asked to submit the code of their machine learning algorithm. Final standing will be evaluated only after the code evaluation.
3. No external data is allowed
4. <b>No pretrained models are allowed.</b>

<h2> Time Duration </h2>

Competition will begin on 19th March 10:00 AM to 20th March 11:59 PM
----------------------
# Evaluation

The metric used for this challenge is Categorization Accuracy.","# Dataset Description


<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the train set . Contains two columns the <b>image file</b> and the target label <b>powerline</b></li>
<li><strong>Train Folder</strong> - Contains powerline and No_powerline folder. Powerline folder has 5417 images containing power lines. No_powerline folder has 4583 images NOT containing the power lines.</li>
<li><strong>sampleSubmission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format. The target label is <b>powerline</b>. Solution must be submitted in this format only.</li>
<li><strong>test folder</strong> - contains 6078 images. These images are to be classified as containing power lines or not.</li>
</ul>",True,True
