4094,spotify-popularity-prediction,"# Description

Nesta tarefa construiremos modelos preditivos de regress?o para a predi??o de popularidade de m¨²sicas. Os dados a serem utilizados foram extra¨ªdos do Spotify e est?o dispon¨ªveis aqui no Kaggle. Voc¨º pode ver os atributos dos dados na aba ""Data"" aqui no Challenge, onde tamb¨¦m ¨¦ poss¨ªvel baixar os dados, ou na descri??o da atividade no Canvas. 


----------------------
# Avalia??o

Para submeter um envio, voc¨º deve adicionar um arquivo `.csv` que siga o mesmo padr?o do arquivo `sample_submission.csv`: uma coluna contendo a ID da m¨²sica, e outra coluna contendo a popularidade predita pelo seu modelo. Voc¨º pode baixar o arquivo `sample_submission.csv` na aba `Data`, aqui no Kaggle.

Neste desafio, como estamos lidando com um problema de regress?o, utilizaremos a Raiz do Erro Quadr¨¢tico M¨¦dio, ou RMSE, como m¨¦trica de avalia??o. O RMSE pode ser entendido da seguinte forma:

$$\text{RMSE} = \sqrt{
\dfrac{1}{N} * \sum\_{1}^{N} \left( Y\_i - \hat{Y}\_i \right)^2
}$$

De modo que:
* \\(Y\_i\\) ¨¦ o valor da popularidade da m¨²sica
* \\(\hat{Y}\_i\\) ¨¦ o valor da popularidade da m¨²sica predito pelo modelo
* \\(N\\) ¨¦ o n¨²mero de m¨²sicas","# Dataset Description

Os dados possuem os seguintes atributos:

* id: Identificador da m¨²sica na base do spotify
* artists: Nomes dos artistas
* name: Nome da m¨²sica
* year: Ano de lan?amento
* release_date: Data de lan?amento da m¨²sica, codificada em Ano-M¨ºs-Dia. Entretanto, nem todas as m¨²sicas possuem a informa??o completa, ent?o ¨¦ poss¨ªvel que apenas s¨® contenha o ano, por exemplo.
* acousticness: Entre 0 e 1, quanto a m¨²sica ¨¦ ac¨²stica.
* danceability: Entre 0 e 1, quanto a m¨²sica ¨¦ dan?¨¢vel.
* duration_ms: Dura??o em mil¨¦simos de segundos.
* energy: Entre 0 e 1, quanto a m¨²sica ¨¦ energ¨¦tica.
* explicit: 1 se a m¨²sica cont¨¦m letra com conte¨²do expl¨ªcito, 0 caso contr¨¢rio.
* instrumentalness: Entre 0 e 1, qu?o instrumental ¨¦ a m¨²sica.
* key: Tom da m¨²sica, mapeado aqui.
* liveness: Entre 0 e 1, qu?o ¡°Ao vivo¡± ¨¦ a m¨²sica
* loudness: O quanto a m¨²sica ¨¦ volumosa. O valor usualmente varia entre -60 e 0, representando a quantidade de decib¨¦is da m¨²sica.
* mode: 1 se a m¨²sica ¨¦ em tom maior, 0 se em tom menor. Popularmente, as m¨²sicas em tom maior s?o consideradas m¨²sicas felizes, enquanto as em tom menor s?o consideradas mais tristes.
* speechiness: Entre 0 e 1, quanto a m¨²sica ¨¦ vocalizada/falada.
* tempo: Tempo da m¨²sica em quantidades de Batidas por Minuto (BPM)
* valence: Entre 0 e 1, descreve a positividade da m¨²sica, com valores altos para m¨²sicas positivas (felizes, alegres, euf¨®ricas, etc) e valores baixos para m¨²sicas negativas (tristes, com raiva, etc)
* popularity: Entre 0 e 100, popularidade da m¨²sica. Neste conjunto, esta ¨¦ a vari¨¢vel alvo.",True,True
4095,saas-2021-spring-cx-kaggle-compeition,"# Description

<p>Welcome fellow data enthusiasts! I am sure you have learned so much from the past CX lectures and are eager to get your hands dirty. This competition is aimed to help solidify the concepts you have learned this semester and hope you enjoy this competition! </p>

<h2>Happy Kaggling :)</h2>
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Metric
Submissions are evaluated on Mean Absolute Error(MAE). 
## $$ MAE = \frac{\textstyle Number \ of \ Mistakes}{\textstyle Total \ Number \ of \ Predictions } $$

## Submission File Format
See the submission file (sample_submission.csv) on the Data page.","# Dataset Description

##File descriptions

train_features.csv - the features of training set <br />
test_features.csv - the features of test set <br />
train_targets.csv - the targets of training set <br />
sample_submission.csv - follow the format of sample_submission.csv for submitting your final results",True,True
4096,california-house-prices,"# Description

The task is to predict house sale prices based on the house information, such as # of bedrooms, living areas, locations, near-by schools, and the seller summary. The data consist of houses sold in California on 2020, with houses in the test dataset sold after the ones in the training dataset. Also the private leaderboard houses were sold after the ones in the public leaderboard.
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Metric

Submissions are evaluated on [Root-Mean-Squared-Error (RMSE)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root-mean-square_deviation) between the logarithm of the predicted value and the logarithm of the observed sales price. (Taking logs means that errors in predicting expensive houses and cheap houses will affect the result equally.)

## Submission File Format

The file should contain a header and have the following format:

```
Id,Sold Price
0,223500.0
1,835000.0
2,1155000.0
```","# Dataset Description

## File descriptions

- `train.csv` - the training set
- `test.csv` - the test set
- `sample_submission.csv` - a sample submission file in the correct format


## Data fields

- Id - the house ID
- Sold Price - the price this house was sold 
- Summary - seller summary about this house
- ...",True,True
4097,gt-cse6250-spring-2021-hw5,"# Description

<p>A gatech.edu email address is required to participate.</p>
<p>Follow the sign-up direction using your GT email address, or if you already have an account, change the email on your existing account via your profile settings so that you can participate. Make sure your display name (not necessarily your username) matches your GT account username so that your Kaggle submission can be linked to the grading system.

In the homework5.pdf, we ask you to improve the performance of your RNN model with variable-length sequences on mortality prediction. In this challenge, you will submit your my_predictions.csv to compete with your classmates.

You will be required to submit the predicted labels for the test patients. After you submit, your accuracy on 50% of the test dataset will be visible to the class on the public leaderboard. You can use this accuracy as a sanity check to make sure your classifier is performing as intended and improve your model.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:<br>
<br>
SUBJECT_ID, MORTALITY<br>
1, 0.5432<br>
8, 0.9123<br>
9, 0.1251<br>
10, 0.3253<br>
etc.</p>","# Dataset Description

<p>Use the data files provided in our Homework 5. Below gives a sample submission file.</p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>kaggle_sample_solution.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>SUBJECT_ID</strong> - an anonymous id unique to a given patient</li>
<li><strong>MORTALITY</strong> - a predicted probability of mortality</li>
</ul>",True,True
