4110,applications-of-deep-learning-wustl-spring-2021b,"# Description

You can find a video of the winning solution [here](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OlMG_8NqrdU).

This semester you will get a chance to try your hand at detecting fake images from real images.  I trained a [model](https://github.com/jeffheaton/pretrained-gan-minecraft) on images that I collected from the [Minecraft video game](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minecraft).  From the provided link, you have access to my trained model, and can generate more fake data, if you like.  However, if you would like additional real data, you will need to capture it from Minecraft yourself.

The following is a real image from Minecraft:
![Real Minecraft](https://github.com/jeffheaton/jheaton_images/blob/main/kaggle/spring-2021/mc-34.jpg?raw=true)

This Minecraft image is obviously fake:

![alt](https://github.com/jeffheaton/jheaton_images/blob/main/kaggle/spring-2021/mc-202.jpg?raw=true)

Some images are not as easily guessed, such as this fake image:

![alt](https://github.com/jeffheaton/jheaton_images/blob/main/kaggle/spring-2021/mc-493.jpg?raw=true)

You will also have to contend with multiple times of the day.  Darker images will be more difficult for your model.

![alt](https://github.com/jeffheaton/jheaton_images/blob/main/kaggle/spring-2021/mc-477.jpg?raw=true)


----------------------
# Evaluation

Your submission will be evaluated using the log loss.","# Dataset Description

All images are 1024x1024 JPEG images stored with a low compression quality.  Because there are over 40K images, the file size would be very large if lossless PNG files were used.  You will likely need to decrease the image size before feeding into a neural network.  The zip down load contains the JPEG images with names such as mc-1.jpg.  There are also three CSV files

* train.csv - Labeled training data.
* test.csv - The file you should score and submit.
* sample.csv - A sample submission file.

The label for this training set is a true (1)/false (0) value that indicates if the image is fake.",True,True
4111,khatam-nlp-assignment-2-squad,"# Description

**Question Answering (QA)** is the task of answering a question(source:nlpprogress :D  )! Most current QA datasets frame the task as reading comprehension where the question is about a paragraph or document and the answer often is a span in the document.

The **Stanford Question Answering Dataset (SQuAD)** is a reading comprehension dataset, consisting of questions posed by crowdworkers on a set of Wikipedia articles. The answer to every question is a segment of text (a span) from the corresponding reading passage. 

To make it easier, we just use the questions with single word answers in this assignment. Take a look at [here](https://rajpurkar.github.io/SQuAD-explorer/explore/1.1/dev/) for more information on SQuAD. You can also read [this paper](https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/K17-1028/) to get a clue on how to tackle the problem wihtout RNNs. 

----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is **Categorical Accuracy**.
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>id,label<br>0,1<br>1,63<br>2,24<br>...</pre>","# Dataset Description

This is a dummy data file. Use squad 1.1 dev from torchtext.",True,True
