4122,wm2021-vector-space-model,"# Description

# Overview
We will give you a bunch of Chinese news articles and several queries in NTCIR format, and your task is to find the relevant documents among these articles according to the given queries.

You should implement the retrieval system by **Vector Space Model (VSM)** with **Rocchio Relevance Feedback (pseudo version)**.
----------------------
# Evaluation

# Evaluation Metric
We will use the **Mean Average Precision (MAP@100)** value to evaluate your ranking list.

We provide an answer ranking list for query-train.xml, which can be used to check your system's performance.

You need to produce a ranking list of query-test.xml and submit to Kaggle. You can see your performance ranking on the leaderboard.

## Submission Format

For every query topic in the dataset, submission files should contain two columns: *queryid* and *retrieveddocs.* retrieved_docs should be a **space-delimited** list. For each query topic, you can retrieve up to **100** documents.

The file should contain a header and have the following format:
```
query_id,retrieved_docs
011,doc_1 doc_3 doc_5
012,doc_2 doc_4 doc_6
013,doc_3 doc_6 doc_9
014,doc_4 doc_8 doc_12
...
```","# Dataset Description

<h1>**File descriptions**

   * CIRB010.tar.gz - NTCIR Document Set
   * model.zip
       * vocab.all - contains all vocabularies in NTCIR documents.
       * file-list - a list of all NTCIR documents.
       * inverted-file - vocab_id and file_id referred from vocab.all and file-list.
   * script.zip - shell script templates, we will use these 2 scripts to compile and run your code.
   * sample_submission.csv - a sample submission file in the correct format
   * queries.zip
       * query-train.xml - queries for you to validate your system
       * query-test.xml - queries for competition
       * ans-train.csv - ground truth for query-train.xml
   * user_agreement_form_for_ntcir.pdf - you MUST sign and hand in it first, or you will get NO POINT",True,True
