4141,usp-pj01,"# Description

# **Project 01 - Iris Dataset**

## **Building Your First Intelligence Algorithm - Classification Task**

## **Task**

Use the dataset **Iris (train and test)** to build a classification model for iris species (plants). 

**Important:** A machine learning project has a number of well known steps:

    - Problem definition ¡ú Create a classification model for iris species (plants). 
    - Data preparation.
    - Algorithm evaluation.
    - Improvement of results.
    - Presentation/Visualization of final results.


For this challenge, use Holdout or any data splitting strategy (e.g., Cross-Validation, Leave-One-Out, Bootstrap, ... ) to assess which of the chosen classifiers (at least two) has the best results on the data, some examples of classification algorithms are:  

  - SVM Linear
  - SVM RBF
  - KNN
  - Decision Tree
  - Bayes

Also:
 
- Decide what data standardization/normalization strategy (if any) will be applied to the data for each algorithm.
- Report at least three performance metrics for each classifier.

**Doubts** - see Supplementary Material - https://classroom.google.com/u/5/c/MzEwODc0NzQzMDEy

## Dataset

""The Iris dataset was used in R.A. Fisher's classic 1936 paper, The Use of Multiple Measurements in Taxonomic Problems, and can also be found on the UCI Machine Learning Repository. It includes three iris species with 50 samples each as well as some properties about each flower. One flower species is linearly separable from the other two, but the other two are not linearly separable from each other."" (**description made in** https://www.kaggle.com/uciml/iris).

Train - Labeled samples 
Test - Unlabeled samples 

## Supplementary Links

1 - https://towardsdatascience.com/step-by-step-guide-to-building-your-own-neural-network-from-scratch-df64b1c5ab6e

2 - https://towardsdatascience.com/writing-your-first-ai-machine-learning-program-92a590df86de



