4188,ukrainian-news-classification,"# Description

<h2>Competition Description</h2>
<p>
Participants of this competition are provided with texts from real articles published in Ukrainian and international media. The task of the competition is to determine the source of news by the content.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is <a href=""https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.f1_score.html""> Macro-averaged F1-Score</a>. The F1 score, commonly used in information retrieval, measures accuracy using the statistics precision p and recall r. Precision is the ratio of true positives (tp) to all predicted positives (tp + fp). Recall is the ratio of true positives to all actual positives (tp + fn). The F1 score is given by:</p>
![f1 score](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/9c94f59b68f5ae0dc92185906c7ec4214fd04e1e)
<p>The F1 metric weights recall and precision equally, and a good retrieval algorithm will maximize both precision and recall simultaneously. Thus, moderately good performance on both will be favored over extremely good performance on one and poor performance on the other.</p>

<p>You can take f1-score implementation from <a href=""https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.f1_score.html"">sklearn library</a>. Be sure to set <i>average</i> parameter to <i>macro</i>. </p>

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For every text in the dataset</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: Id and Predicted.</p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>Id,Predicted<br>1,1<br></pre>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train_small.csv</strong> - small subsample of training set.</li>
<li><strong>train_large.csv</strong> - larger subsample of training set. Combine it with train_small to get the full training set.</li>
<li><strong>test_without_target.csv</strong> - the test set.</li>
<li><strong>sample_submission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>title</strong> - short article title</li>
<li><strong>text</strong> - article text</li>
<li><strong>source</strong> - source of the article (this column is the target variable you need to predict)</li>
</ul>",True,True
