4216,2021-iml-hackathon,"# Description

<p><b>Cars4U,</b> is an on-demand car aggregator and rental service operating in New York. Under its purview, the company has cars which are either owned by the company itself or is listed on the platform by other car owners (Airbnb for Cars). The company has recently raised a $ 10 million Series A funding and is looking to expand its services. In order to do so the company looking to strategically position its cars in various parts of the city by predicting the demand.
<br>
<br>
<b>Cars4U</b> is looking for talented data scientists such as you to help them with predicting the demand for their cars. The company has provided a dataset detailing their historical trends and is now looking for help to predict the demand.
</p>
![](https://i.ibb.co/S3KWV2Y/car-rental.jpg)
----------------------
# Evaluation

# Evaluation Metric

The evaluation metric for this competition is root-mean-square error (RMSE). The RMSE score, is a frequently used measure of the differences between values (sample or population values) predicted by a model or an estimator and the values observed. The RMSE score is given by:

![](https://i.ibb.co/G7tqcWY/rmse-1.jpg)

# Submission Format

For every unique 'Date' and 'Time' combination in the dataset, submission files should contain two columns: Id and Demand.

The file should have the following format:
```
Id,Demand
1,23
```","# Dataset Description

 'Demand' is the dependent variable that has to be predicted using the remainder of the independent varibales provided in the dataset.

# File descriptions
* <b> train.csv </b>- The training dataset.
* <b> test.csv </b> - The test dataset.
* <b> sample_submission.csv </b>- A sample submission file in the correct format. This is the format in which you are expected to submit your solution.

# Data fields

* <b> Id </b> - Unique Identifier
* <b> Date </b> - Date
* <b> Time </b> - Time
* <b> Season </b> - spring, summer, fall, winter
* <b> IsHoliday </b> - Is the given 'date' a holiday
* <b> IsWorkingDay </b> - Is the given 'date' a working day i.e. neither a holiday nor weekend
* <b> Weather </b> - Clear, Cloudy, Light Rain, Heavy Rain
* <b> Temperature </b> - Acutal temperature recorded (in Celcius)
* <b> AdoptedTemperature </b> - Adopted or feels like temperature (in Celcius)
* <b> Humidity </b> - Humidity
* <b> WindSpeed </b> - WindSpeed
* <b> Demand </b> - Number of cars at the service location",True,True
