4238,ieeespawc21localization,"# Introduction

Positioning systems are the key ingredient for the success of Industry 4.0, whereas it is envisioned that the factory functions almost automatically. Thus, a large amount of effort is pointed towards enabling positioning in a robust and versatile way using multiple techniques, ranging from Camera-based to ultra-wideband (UWB). In the end there will be no clear winner, but a subset of techniques will form a symbiosis for enabling localization in a deploy-able fashion (e.g. inertial measurement unit (IMU) joining UWB). Although it is apparent that fusion is the key to success, it is unclear which sets are favorable, thus this challenge has the goal to foster a deeper understanding into these techniques.

----------------------
# Description

![Measurement Setup](https://i.ibb.co/TWws3km/Spawc2021-3.png)
Fig 1. Shows the measurement platform (left) the measurement schematic (middle) and the measurement scenario (right), where multiple sensors are measured to give a fair comparison. From the scenario it becomes directly apparent that not all regions get the same amount of coverage, and thus the solution needs to rely on only the sensors available, e.g. in cases where the signal is blocked or interfered the IMU can take over, due to its environment independency. To make this challenge more interesting, we will distribute a dataset which is measured at the morning and the performance will be evaluated on a dataset measured in the evening, demonstrating which method shows the best generalizability.
----------------------
# Challenge

The challenge will be to find the best subset of raw data and find the best algorithm to do positioning with points being:
-  localization on the same-dataset
- localization on a slightly different dataset 
demonstrating the capability of finding the best generalized solution.

The challenge will have the following datasets:
 - You will receive 90% of the dataset from the morning measurements 
-  You will receive ~6000 points of the dataset from the evening measurements

The challenge will consist of the performance on the first dataset in combination with the performance of the evening measurements.  In general saying:
- Find a suitable sensor fusion approach
- Try to use the limited dataset from the evening to make your system generalize
- Demonstrate the best overall performance

On the witheld ground truth we will calculate the MSE.
----------------------
# Additional Reference

Additional information is provided in the paper arxiv 

https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.05438

If you use this dataset for your research please site the given reference.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.05438
If you have questions please contact:
maximilian.arnold@nokia-bell-labs.com","# Dataset Description

# Dataset properties

![Dataset properties](https://i.ibb.co/ZNDS5GX/Spawc2021-4.png)

The table shows the properties of the measurement campaigns. For more information read the arxiv paper given in additional references.

The dataset contains to each position a time stamp and all the available sensor information.

Be careful the datasets are huge. The Dataset1 contains 90% of the original dataset and the Dataset2 small contains ~6000 points with ground truth. The Dataset 2 test is without ground truth to predict on.

## How to read the data
import joblib
data_dir = './Dataset1.dat'

Data_Dict = joblib.load(data_dir)

Positions = Data_Dict['pos']

time =  Data_Dict['time']

RSSI = 10**(Data_Dict['RSSI']/20)

CSI = Data_Dict['CSI']) // Careful Complex value!

IMU = Data_Dict['IMU']

UWB =  Data_Dict['UWB']",True,True
4239,prediction-challenge-3-ta-test-2021,"# Description

<p>
Predict Earnings. Use any learning package from recitation (or any other). You can also use linear regression and as I mentioned, rpart - which works nicely for numerical variables.  Remember that knowing your data before just blindly trying different ML methods is always a good idea. Often some transformation of data (new attributes etc) will lead to better or much better results!</p>

<p>
IMPORTANT: Before you apply ML methods - tell us more about the data using plots. What variables matter in determining earnings?    Think about creating a new attribute that can be more predictive?   Like multiplying the number of connections by GPA?  Be creative.  You can significantly  improve the ML results with a bit of ""human intervention""</p>

<p>
Submit PPT and R code as always. Plus KAGGLE submission - rules same as previous weeks
</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>Evaluations would be based on MSE for this competition.</p>",# Dataset Description,True,True
4240,music-genre-prediction,"# Description

Nesta tarefa construiremos modelos preditivos de regress?o para a predi??o de popularidade de m¨²sicas. Os dados a serem utilizados foram extra¨ªdos do Spotify e est?o dispon¨ªveis aqui no Kaggle. Voc¨º pode ver os atributos dos dados na aba `Data` aqui no Challenge, onde tamb¨¦m ¨¦ poss¨ªvel baixar os dados, ou na descri??o da atividade no Canvas.
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>A m¨¦trica de avalia??o desta competi??o ¨¦ a <a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/wiki/MeanFScore""> M¨¦dia do F1-Score</a>. 
O F1 score ¨¦ comumente utilizado em recupera??o da informa??o, medindo acur¨¢cia atrav¨¦s da precis?o p e do recall r. Precis?o ¨¦ a raz?o entre os verdadeiros positivos e todas as amostras preditas positivas (tp + fp). Recall ¨¦ a raz?o entre os verdadeiros positivos para todos os verdadeiros positivos (tp, fn). Assim, o F1 ¨¦ dado por:</p>
<p>\[ F1 = 2\frac{p \cdot r}{p+r}\ \ \mathrm{where}\ \ p = \frac{tp}{tp+fp},\ \ r = \frac{tp}{tp+fn} \]</p>
<p>A m¨¦trica F1 pesa recall e precis?o de forma igualit¨¢ria, e ¨¦ um bom m¨¦todo de recupera??o, pois maximiza os dois simultaneamente, e uma boa performance em ambos gera um melhor resultado que um ¨®timo resultado em um e um baixo resultado no outro.</p>
<h2>Formato de Submiss?o</h2>
<p><strong>Para cada m¨²sica no conjunto de testes</strong>, o arquivo de submiss?o deve conter duas colunas: a id, presente no conjunto de teste, e a label predita pelo seu modelo. Um exemplo claro disso est¨¢ no arquivo Sample Submission, presente na aba Data.</p>","# Dataset Description

Os dados para esta tarefa s?o reais e foram extra¨ªdos de faixas de ¨¢udio. Para cada m¨²sica presente na base de dados foram extra¨ªdas as seguintes caracter¨ªsticas:

* Id: Identificador da m¨²sica;
* length: Dura??o do audio, em milissegundos;
* tempo: O tempo ¨¦ uma medida do passo da m¨²sica, sua velocidade. ¨¦ medido em batidas por minuto (BPM);
* label: O g¨ºnero musical. ¨¦ o atributo alvo.

Os atributos a seguir foram calculadas ao longo de toda a faixa de ¨¢udio, e para cada m¨¦trica extra¨ªda existem dois atributos: a m¨¦dia e a variancia. Al¨¦m disso, em alguns deles podemos ver a sigla STFT, Short Time Fourier Transform, uma t¨¦cnica que pode ser aplicada para a extra??o de m¨¦tricas em sinais anal¨®gicos cont¨ªnuos. S?o eles:

* Chroma STFT: Se refere ao tom da m¨²sica, em forma anal¨®gica;
* RMS: Sigla que significa Root Mean Squared, mas que no contexto de ¨¢udio se refere a m¨¦dia da volumosidade da m¨²sica;
* Spectral Centroid: O centroide espectral ¨¦ um ponto balanceado do espectro de ¨¢udio, e um atributo perceptual importante na caracteriza??o do timbre musical de instrumentos. ¨¦ usado tamb¨¦m para diferenciar os instrumentos presentes na m¨²sica: um baixo gera um baixo centroide espectral, enquanto um trompete gera um valor alto;
* Spectral Bandwidth: A largura espectral indica a largura da frequ¨ºncia ao longo do ¨¢udio. ¨¦ usado para distinguir sons agudos e graves;
* Roloff: Indica a frequ¨ºncia que cont¨¦m 99% da energia do espectro de ¨¢udio;
* Zero Crossing Rate: Taxas de Cruzamento Zero indicam a frequ¨ºncia que o espectro toca o ¡°zero¡±. ¨¦ usado para distinguir sons percussivos (devido a parada entre um pico e outro) e sons constantes;
* Harmony: A harmonia ¨¦ outra medida de entendimento do tom da m¨²sica;
* Mel-Frequency Cepstral Coefficients: S?o coeficientes da frequ¨ºncia na escala Mel, uma escala criada para auxiliar o entendimento humano dos tons de m¨²sica. Al¨¦m disso, os coeficientes cepstrais s?o usados para auxiliar a detec??o de voz. Nos dados, existem 20 atributos, referente a 20 diferentes tons na escala Mel, de mfcc1 a mfcc20.",True,True
