4266,analyticsclubproject,"# Description

## Loan Interest Rate Prediction
Data Science has recently found a very wide use case in the Banking sector and most companies leverage Data Science to make the most out of their data. One such task is to predict the Rate of Interest which should be levied on a person for a loan that they take. 

In this Task, you are asked to predict the category of the interest rate that should be levied on a person. For more details head on to the Evaluation and Data Tab.

Team Formation is not allowed and you will be required to submit the code which you used. 

### Leaderboard is not the only metric for judging. Another equally important part of the task which will be used to evaluate your submission is making visuals with the data and generating insights from it

For any more doubts feel free to reach out to any of the admins on the project whatsapp groups!!

HAPPY SOLVING!!!
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Evaluation
The metric that will be used for the competition is [Accuracy Score](https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course/classification/accuracy). Yes the words ""Accuracy Score"" is a link. Check it out!!
<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>For every Loan_ID in the dataset</strong>, submission files should contain two columns: Loan_ID and Interest_Rate. For more details look at the Submission File in the Data Tab","# Dataset Description

Below you will find all the files needed for solving the task

- train.csv: Contains the train set for the competition
- test.csv: Contains the test set for which you have to make predictions
- sample_submission.csv: Contains a sample submission which you could use to figure out the structure of the final submission that's expected
- train_data_dict.csv: Contains details about what each column means",True,True
4267,109-2-ntut-dl-app-hw2,"# Description

In Homework 2 we are going to train models that can recommend hashtags based on the content of an image. We will use the dataset ""HARRISON"". Please refer to the paper (https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.05054) for more details about the dataset.

The original data of HARRISON can be downloaded here: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1B9NZf42J_GpslRNlTTAxvM5c9WRVl_1Z/view?usp=sharing. 

You can download the images and take a look, but this is not mandatory. We already extracted the image features, compressed them as ""harrison_features.npz"", and upload to Kaggle:
https://www.kaggle.com/kuantinglai/harrison-dataset


The training process is split into two stages: hashtag2vec training and image-to-word2vec training. Please refer to the notebook of this competition. The steps are
1. Run https://www.kaggle.com/kuantinglai/train-htag2vec-tf1
2. Download ""tag\_list\_word2vec\_64.npz"" (The number 64 may be changed, it depends on your vector dimension)
3. Run https://www.kaggle.com/kuantinglai/train-devise-w-ur-htag2vec, upload your  ""tag\_list\_word2vec\_64.npz""
4. Download ""harrison\_test\_predict.csv"" and submit

To evaluate the model performance, we use the mean Average Precision (mAP) @ 10. Enjoy the homework and Have fun!
----------------------
# Evaluation

We use mean Average Precision (mAP) to evaluate the performance. Please refer to 
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evaluation_measures_(information_retrieval)#Average_precision
Or 
https://darren1231.pixnet.net/blog/post/347752732-machine-learning-map%28mean-average-precision%29-%E8%A9%B3%E7%B4%B0%E8%A7%A3%E8%AA%AA

for detailed explanation of Average Precision.",# Dataset Description,True,True
