4276,sentiment-analysis-of-covid-19-related-tweets,"# Description

<h2>Task description</h2>

<p>This competition is for sentiment analysis of Tweets related to the Covid-19
pandemic, which is a multi-label text classification task. Since the outbreak of coronavirus, it
has affected more than 180 countries where massive losses in the economy and jobs globally
and confining about 58% of the global population are caused. The research on people¡¯s feelings
is essential for keeping mental health and informed about Covid-19.</p>

<p>In this competition, the released training data contains 5000 labeled tweets while the released validation data have 2500 pieces of unlabeled tweets. The training data have 3 columns, containing Tweet ID, Tweet text, and labels. Note that the orders are shown as Optimistic (0), Thankful (1), Empathetic (2), Pessimistic (3), Anxious (4), Sad (5), Annoyed (6), Denial (7), Surprise (8), Official report (9), Joking (10). For example, if the labels are 3 and 6, it means that this piece of the tweet is labeled as Pessimistic and Annoyed.</p>

<p>The public ranking of the competition will be based on the prediction on the validation dataset. The final ranking will be based on a private testing dataset that has the same distribution as the training and validation dataset.</p>

<h2 style=""color: red"">Report Submission</h2>
Please submit your *****FINAL REPORT***** to <a href=""https://www.dropbox.com/request/zFuhaPrf7nFfaYH4Y0O3""> the dropbox folder</a>.

<h2>Important Notes:</h2> 
1) Follow carefully the instructions on this page and the evaluation page.
2) The deadline for this completion is ***29th June 2021 (11:59 PM UTC)***. Any further deadline extension will be announced on the event website.
3) Winners will be announced in September / October 2021.
----------------------
# Evaluation

<h2>Scoring Metric&lt;\h2&gt;
</h2>
The evaluation metric for this competition is Macro F1-Score.

<h2>Evaluation Strategy</h2>
The evaluation will be done in two stages:
<ol>
<li>The first stage is based on the evaluation on the validation set, which is available on the competition web page.
&lt;\li&gt;

</li><li>The second stage is based on the evaluation of a private testing set which has the same distribution as the validation set. We will invite the top-ranked participants to submit or share their codes with the organizers for the final evaluation.
</li>
</ol>


<h2>Submission Format</h2>

<p><strong>For every team </strong>, you should submit your solution of the validation set in a CSV file with exactly 2.5K entries plus a header row.&lt;\p&gt;

</p><p>Submission files should contain 2 columns: Tweet_id and the predicted labels including
Optimistic, Thankful, Empathetic, Pessimistic, Anxious, Sad, Annoyed, Denial, Official report, Surprise, Joking. Please use the exact required column names. Both columns should follow the format of the corresponding columns in the training data. Additionally, make sure that the predicted sentiments are mapped with their indexes ranging from 0 to 10. </p>

<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:
</p><ul>
<li>Tweet ID, Labels
&lt;\li&gt;
</li><li>
1221884257490042887, 5 6
&lt;\li&gt;
</li>
<li>1221883443467952128, 0 9
</li>
<li>...
&lt;\li&gt;
&lt;\ul&gt;
</li></ul>","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>training.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>validation.csv</strong> - the validation set</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Tweet ID</strong> - an anonymous id for each tweet</li>
<li><strong>Tweet text</strong> - the text content of a tweet</li>
<li><strong>Labels</strong> - the labels of a tweet, indicated by the label index from 0 to 10, which are
Optimistic (0), Thankful (1), Empathetic (2), Pessimistic (3), Anxious (4), Sad (5), Annoyed (6), Denial (7), Surprise (8), Official report (9), Joking (10).
</ul>",True,True
