4284,unextbnb-price-prediction,"# Description

We have train data for 10,000 homestay listing Amsterdam. The data dictionary is as follows:

SL no : Serial number of the homestay

price : Price of the homestay per night (the target variable)

host _listings _count : Number of listings by the host/homestay owner

accommodates : Number of persons who can be accommodated in the homestay

bathrooms : Number of bathrooms

bedrooms : Number of bedrooms

guests _included : Number of guests who are currently staying in the homestay

minimum _nights : Minimum number of nights for booking

number _of _reviews : Number of reviews of the homestay

calculated _host _listings _count : Number of listings by the host/homestay owner, excluding multiple adverts of the same homestay

latitude : latitude of the homestay

longitude : longitude of the homestay

room _type : options are Shared room, Private room, or Entire home/apt

instant _bookable : f = false; t= true -- may the rooms be booked instantly or do you need the host/homestay owner to confirm and the confirmation may take some time

d _centre : Distance of the homestay from the centre of the city

The test data has 957 entries with all the variables except for the target variable (""price"")
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metrics is RSME or root-mean-square error

In the submission file, we expect only 2 columns- ""SL no"" and ""price""
Price is the target variable. Upload must be in csv format only","# Dataset Description

