<h2>Training Data</h2>
The training data consists of 277,327 images, from 176 different sorghum species grown in 349 unique plots. Metadata for the training dataset can be found in the train\_dataset\_by\_image.csv file, which contains the following information:
- path: the path to the image in the data directory
- plot: an identifier for the plot that each image comes from
- cultivar: the species of sorghum shown in the particular image
- date_captured: the date on which the image was captured
- days\_after\_planting: the number of days after the seed was planted
- accumulated\_heat\_units: the amount of sunlight accumulated at the field site by this point in the growing cycle
- camera\_height\_off\_ground: the height in meters of the camera off of the ground (the camera moves upwards over the course of the season)
- end\_of\_season\_dry\_biomass: the weight of the plants cut down in the particular plot of interest

The TERRA-REF field consisted of multiple plots for each cultivar (the same species was grown in multiple different locations in the field). The training data is organized by plot, with all of the images from the same plot being stored inside of the same folder, in the following structure:

* data
    * train
