<h2>Testing Data</h2>
The testing data consists of 19,442 images from 110 unique plots. The plots are from unknown cultivars (although there is no overlap between the training and testing cultivars).

1/3 of the plots include images from early in the growing cycle, 1/3 from mid-growing season, and 1/3 from late in the growing season. Metadata for the testing imagery is included in the test\_dataset.csv file, with the following columns:

- path: the path to the image in the data directory
- plot_id: an identifier for the plot that each image comes from
- phase: whether this plot and its images come from early, mid or late season
- date_captured: the date on which the image was captured
- days\_after\_planting: the number of days after the seed was planted
- accumulated\_heat\_units: the amount of sunlight accumulated at the field site by this point in the growing cycle
- camera\_height\_off\_ground: the height in meters of the camera off of the ground (the camera moves upwards over the course of the season)

The test data is organized by phase and then by plot, in the following structure:

