4373,ais-winter-competition,"# Description

<p>This is the first AIS competition this year, and it's open to all TAMS students. You are challenged with predicting the star type of stars based on their characteristics. Try your best, stick to the rules, and have fun!</p>

<p>P.S. Detailed step-by-step instructions can be found here: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1FozW4kB3NeW3QN27UYJAj7LSeX1cuAfudeIJCImsWKA/edit#slide=id.gd80c872767_1_0

Message the group chat or one of the execs if you have any questions!</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>Evaluation will be done with the F1-Score metric.</p>

<p>The submission csv file should be called ""[Last Name]_[First Name]_Fall21.csv"" and it should be formatted like sample_submission.csv, which is in the Data tab. You will be turning this in on the competition site on Kaggle.</p>

<p>The submission code file should be a zip file called ""[Last Name]_[First Name]_Fall21_code.zip"" and should include all code files you used. You will be turning this in via email to tamsaisociety@gmail.com with the subject line formatted as ""[Last Name] [First Name] Fall21 code"". asijdkcja bsbh jal</p>","# Dataset Description

<p>Given the star types corresponding to sets of star characteristics, your goal is to make a prediction of the star types given their characteristics of some new stars.</p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>sample_submission.csv</strong> - Sample formatted csv file of submission</li>
<li><strong>stars_competitor_test.csv</strong> - 96 sets of star characteristics for which you will make predictions of star type</li>
<li><strong>stars_train.csv</strong> - 144 sets of star characteristics and corresponding star types that you will use as training data</li>
<li><strong>metadata.csv</strong> - Supplemental information about the data</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields (available in metadata.csv)</h2>
<table>
<tr>
<th><b>Column Name</b></th>
<th><b>Description</b></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Temperature</b></td>
<td><b>Star surface temperature in Kelvin</b></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>L</b></td>
<td><b>Relative Luminosity</b></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>R</b></td>
<td><b>Relative Radius</b></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>A_M</b></td>
<td><b>Absolute Magnitude</b></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Color</b></td>
<td><b>Star Color</b></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Spectral_Class</b></td>
<td><b>Spectral Class of star</b></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><b>Type</b></td>
<td><b>Purposely ambiguous star type</b></td>
</tr>
</table>",True,True
