4380,kirey-gimme5-unipo-2021,"# Description

<h2>Kirey Group Gimme5 Challenge </h2>
<p></p><li><strong>About the data<p> Data relates to the use of Gimme5 application. Information relating to users, contracts and targets built from December 2014 to November 2019 is reported.</p><br>
</strong></li><li><strong><strong>Goal<p>The goal of the challenge is to find out if reaching the target looks possible or not at the moment of the creation. STATUS variable shows if the target has been reached or not. It could be set as CLOSE, WON or ACTIVE. Close status means that the target hasn't been reached and has been handled as over. Won status regards targets that reached the goal import. Active status refers to targets still open that need to be investigated in the real status.</p><br>
</strong></strong></li><li><strong><strong><strong>Strategy<p> You are free to choose your favourite programming language. You can join and use all the datasets provided or just part of them. </p><br>
</strong></strong></strong></li><li><strong><strong><strong><strong>Teams<p> You are free to work in team or as single scientist. Teams must be formed by a maximum of two people. No exceptions will be handled.</p></strong></strong></strong></strong></li><p></p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>KC_TRANSACTION.csv</strong> - Information about all the operation for contract and/or target</li>
<li><strong>KC_USER_CONTRACT.csv</strong> - Information about the user and the contract</li>
<li><strong>KC_TARGET_ENCODED_train.csv</strong> - Training set - information about targets</li>
<li><strong>KC_TARGET_ENCODED_unknown_test.csv</strong> - Test set - Unknown records to be predicted and submitted in order to test your model</li>
<li><strong>submission_sample.csv</strong> - Sample to show the submission template</li>
</ul>
<h2>Submissions</h2>
<p>In order to join the challenge, you need to submit the test predictions before the deadline. Submissions return the metric score reached by a sample of the test and update the partial ranking. You can try to submit many times and your best performance will be evaluated. You can submit maximum twice daily. </p>
<p> Remember that in order to avoid cheats, the final ranking will be evaluated to a hidden part of the test. In this way, we discourage to overfit the evaluated test set with recursive submissions. </p>
<p> Deadline: 13.06.2020 - 23.59 UTC+2 Rome (09.59 PM UTC)</p>
<h2>Awards</h2>
<ul>
<p>During the award day two submissions are going to be presented as Winners of the following categories:  </p>
<li><strong>Technical Prize</strong> - highest metric score in the hidden test </li>
<li><strong>Creative Prize</strong> - best notebook for creative or innovator problem approach</li>
</ul>
----------------------
# Contacts

<h2>Contacts</h2>
<p><strong>Claudio Bottari</strong> - Chief Innovation Officer - Kirey Group<br>
<em>claudio.bottari@kireygroup.com</em></p>
<p><strong>Fabio Loche</strong> - Data Scientist - Kirey Group<br>
<em>fabio.loche@kireygroup.com</em></p>
<p><strong>Giuseppe Codazzi</strong> - Data Scientist - AcomeA<br>
<em>giuseppe.codazzi@acomea.it</em></p>
<p><strong>Valentina Sortino</strong> - Recruiting - Kirey Group<br>
<em>valentina.sortino@kireygroup.com</em></p>","# Dataset Description

<h1>Kirey Group Gimme5 Challenge </h1>

<p></p><li><strong>About the data<p> Data relates to the use of Gimme5 application. Information relating to users, contracts and targets built from December 2014 to November 2019 is reported.</p>
</strong></li><li><strong><strong>Goal<p>The goal of the challenge is to find out if reaching the target looks possible or not at the moment of the creation. STATUS variable explain if a target has been reached. It could be set as CLOSE, WON or ACTIVE. Close status means that the target hasn't been reached. Won status means that the target is been positive closed and reached. Active status is referred to open targets that need to be handled. </p><p></p>

<h2>File descriptions</h2>

</strong></strong><ul><strong><strong>
<li><strong>KC_TRANSACTION.csv</strong> - Information about all the operation for contract and/or target</li>
<li><strong>KC_USER_CONTRACT.csv</strong> - Information about the user and the contract</li>
<li><strong>KC_TARGET_ENCODED_train.csv</strong> - Training set - information about targets</li>
</strong><li><strong>KC_TARGET_ENCODED_unknown_test.csv</strong> - Test set - Unknown records to be predicted and submitted in order to test your model</li>
</strong><li><strong>submission_sample.csv</strong> - Sample to show the submission template with a casual prediction</li>
</ul></li>",True,True
4381,fcis-asu-autism-disorder-classification,"# Description

<h1> Introduction </h1>
Welcome to the competition. This competition is for CS students in Neural Network and Deep Learning course at FCIS. The goal of the competition is to build deep learning models that can diagnose autism disorder in the children from their face. Let's help the community with useful things!

<h1> Medical Background </h1>
<p>
Children with autism have a broader upper face, including wider eyes. Children with autism have a shorter middle region of the face, including the cheeks and nose. Children with autism have a broader or wider mouth and philtrum -- the divot below the nose, above the top lip.
</p>


----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>You have to submit a file in CSV format named as 'submit.csv'.</p>
<hr>
<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is the overall accuracy </p><p> 

</p><h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong> The file contains 2 column, the first column is ID, which is the name of the test image. The second column is label, which is your predicted label for the image </strong> </p>
<p>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</p>
<pre>id,label<br>1.jpg,1<br></pre>","# Dataset Description

<h1> Dataset description </h1>
<p>
The dataset is organized into 2 folders (train and test) and contains subfolders for the train category (autistic children and non-autistic children). There are 2,536 children faces training images, 1,268 autistic children faces and 1,268 non-autistic children faces.
The testing set contains 400 images for children and you have to classify each of them.

<h2>Files description</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.rar</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.rar</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>Submit.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in the correct format</li>
<li><strong>Names.csv</strong> this file contains the IDs of the two classes</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Image</strong> - the name of child face image </li>
<li><strong>Label</strong> - the predicted class</li>
</ul>",True,True
4382,predict-the-famous-cryptocurrencies,"# Description

Here are the top 5 cryptocurrencies along with their prices and valuations!

Why is there a sudden surge in the interest in recent days?

This will help understand the other factors related to Bitcoin price and also help one make future predictions in a better way than just using the historical price.

Acknowledgements
This data is taken from coinmarketcap and it is free to use the data.

Some of the questions which could be inferred from this dataset are:

How did the historical prices / market capitalizations of various currencies change over time?
Predicting the future price of the currencies
Which currencies are more volatile and which ones are more stable?
How does the price fluctuations of currencies correlate with each other?
Seasonal trend in the price fluctuations

This is a regression problem. the Evaluation Metrics is RMSE

The prediction file (submission.csv) should follow the following format with 290 predictions.

Submission Format
<p>The submission file should contain a header with two columns and have the following format:</p>

<pre>id, Close</pre>","# Dataset Description

Content
<p>
Price history is available on a daily basis from April 28, 2013. This dataset has the historical price information of some of the top crypto currencies by market capitalization.
</p>
<ul><li>
Date : date of observation
</li><li>
Open : Opening price on the given day
</li><li>
High : Highest price on the given day
</li><li>
Low : Lowest price on the given day
</li><li>
Close : Closing price on the given day [Target]
</li><li>
Volume : Volume of transactions on the given day
</li><li>
Market Cap : Market capitalization in USD
</li></ul>",True,True
