<p><b>2. Get to Work</b></p>

<p>Download the data, build models on it locally or on Kaggle Kernels (our no-setup, customizable Jupyter Notebooks environment with free GPUs) and generate a prediction file.</p>
<p></p>
<p></p>

<p><b>3. Make a Submission</b></p>
<p>Upload your prediction as a submission on Kaggle and receive an accuracy score.</p>
<p></p>
<p></p>

<p><b>4. Check the Leaderboard</b></p>
<p>See how your model ranks against other Kagglers on our leaderboard. </p>
<p></p>
<p></p>

<p><b>5. Improve Your Score</b></p>
<p>Check out the <a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/c/x2022/discussion"">discussion forum</a> to find lots of tutorials and insights from other competitors.</p>
<p></p>
<p></p>

