4471,evisioncompetation,"# Description

<h2>Introduction</h2>
<p>Welcome to the competition. This competition is for EVC trainees in Neural Network. The goal of the competition is to build deep learning models that can distinguish between indoor scenes. This dataset contains great training and testing sets for forming models that can distinguish the scenes.</p>

<h2>Content</h2>
<p>
This dataset contains 3,910 images of 10 classes of Indoor scenes. The data is split into 3,138 training images and 772 testing images, where each class has been split roughly in an 80-20 split.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>You have to submit a file in CSV format named as 'submit.csv'.</p>

<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is the overall accuracy</p>

<h2>Submission Format</h2>

<p>The file contains 2 columns, the first column is ID, which is the name of the test image. The second column is label, which is your predicted label for the image </p>

<h3>The file should contain a header and have the following format:</h3>

> id,label
0070.jpg,1","# Dataset Description

<h2>File descriptions</h2>
- train.rar - the training set
- test.rar - the test set
- Submit.csv - a sample submission file in the correct format

<h2>Data fields</h2>
- ID - the name of the photo
- Label - the predicted class for that ID

<h2>Labels</h2>
[Classes indexes](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d3Ijx2jka9hOD3cdSkQSrUgyMamR8LL_/)

![Classes](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d3Ijx2jka9hOD3cdSkQSrUgyMamR8LL_/view)",True,True
4472,anomaly-detection,"# Description

<p>Let us assume that, we have a company called ""Splash"", and you are a newly joined Machine Learning Engineer at our company, held at 30 LPA CTC. So, the below thing describes our company and the task in hand.</p>

<p>Currently we at Splash, help retailers with pricing intelligence and business monitoring.</p>

<p>One of our main challenges comprise of monitoring and analyzing our client's business metrics in real time for instant detection of the incidents that may impact their revenue.</p>

<p>One subpart of this challenge is Anomaly Detection which generates alerts on our client's business metrics.</p>

<p>The Problem Statement presented below highlights the problem which we are tackling right now</p>

<h2>Column Description</h2>
<p>The description of the column are as follows:</p>
<p>timestamp [ float ] : is provided as a Unix epoch in seconds.</p>
<p>value [ int ] : is a real value measurement of some metric at the timestamp.</p>
<p>is_anomaly [ boolean ] : is a boolean value which is True if the corresponding value is
identified as an anomaly. </p>
<p>predicted [ float ] : is a real value prediction coming from a black box forecasting
model for that timestamp. This black box forecasting model is assumed to be aware of
only the true data distribution.</p>

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p> The CSV format should contain two column, timestamp, is_anomaly score</p>

<h2>Scoring Criteria</h2>
<p>The scoring will be determined with the help of the Mean-F-Score, because the prediction of the anomaly is the important part, merely just making all the values to be False, would result in maybe 95% accuracy, which is not the desired thing for the client, because he is concerned more about the anomaly rather than the non anomaly data.</p>","# Dataset Description

<h2>Column Description</h2>
<p>The description of the column are as follows:</p>
<p>timestamp [ float ] : is provided as a Unix epoch in seconds.</p>
<p>value [ int ] : is a real value measurement of some metric at the timestamp.</p>
<p>is_anomaly [ boolean ] : is a boolean value which is True if the corresponding value is
identified as an anomaly. </p>
<p>predicted [ float ] : is a real value prediction coming from a black box forecasting
model for that timestamp. This black box forecasting model is assumed to be aware of
only the true data distribution.</p>

<h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p> The CSV format should contain two column, timestamp, is_anomaly score</p>",True,True
4473,dataminingc2021,"# Description

Bu Wiji, seorang peneliti baru tertarik untuk meneliti penyakit hati. Menggunakan data pasien yang tersedia, Bu Wiji cukup kesulitan dalam menentukan apakah pasien tersebut terindikasi penyakit hati atau tidak. Kamu sebagai teman Bu Wiji yang baik hati dan senang membantu diharapkan dapat membantu beliau. Maka dari itu, kamu diminta untuk membuat model yang dapat menentukan apakah pasien terkena penyakit hati atau tidak. Dari model yang didapat, kemudian diterapkan pada data test untuk memprediksi pasien.
Selamat mengerjakan ?? 
