4487,sasviyaforlearners2021,"# Description

## Introduction

The SAS Viya for Learners Challenge hosted online through Kaggle InClass is geared towards students who are looking to get into and engage with machine learning problems. Students will walk through the data science process and learn how to build machine learning models on a simulated business problem, with a chance to prove their skills on the live leader board.

SAS Viya for Learners is a full suite of cloud-based software that supports the entire analytics life cycle ¨C from data, to discovery, to deployment ¨C and it also lets you code in SAS, Python or R. Machine learning is about using a combination of programming for model building, as well as visual, interactive interfaces to be able to explore data and test assumptions quickly.

### To Enter The Challenge:

* In order to to participate in the challenge, you need to register for access to the SAS Viya for Learners environment
* Please click on the Rules tab and accept the competition rules in order to participate.

## Table of Contents
1. The Challenge Problem
2. Challenge Structure & Getting Started
3. SAS Viya Resources
4. Contact & Acknowledgements

## The Challenge Problem

The PVA dataset is an analytics table produced from the historical donor behaviour for donations to retired veterans in the United States. The data contained within has been aggregated to a number of key relevant features around the donor bases behaviour patterns, including recency, frequency and value of their donations. This data will be key in the organisations initiative to prioritise contacting those donors who are most likely to donate, to improve the efficiency of the call center, and improve the overall donor customer experience by optimizing the frequency of interactions based on their individual behavior.

## Challenge Structure
### Getting Started and Entering
To start developing the ML models for this challenge on SAS Viya for Learners, all participants need access to the environment. If you came here from the landing page, you should have an email with a provided credentials for you to access the environment. If you are signing up through Kaggle, please refer to the __SAS Viya For Learners Registration section__ on the left for more details.

Once you have access to the environment, please refer to the [Data](https://www.kaggle.com/c/sasviyaforlearners2021/data) section to understand and walk-through the data that will be used for the challenge.

### Rules

Please refer to the Evaluation and the Submission Requirements sections for more details.

## SAS Viya Resources 

To get you started, please refer to the Notebooks section of the Kaggle Competition page. In this Notebook section, are two programming templates in Python and R that walk-through a machine learning pipeline and build a simple model to get you started with the challenge.

For resources on how to use the SAS Viya graphical user interfaces, please refer to the __SAS Viya for Learners Resources Portal__.

## Contact &amp; Acknowledgements
- Please use the Discussion and Notebooks section for discussion on the challenge 
- Feel free to reach out to the SAS Academic team for any further questions (Academic@oz.sas.com)

Thanks for playing!
----------------------
# Evaluation & Submission Requirements

# Submission to Kaggle

## Submission Requirements

All submissions require the following components to be eligible:

- A CSV containing your model predictions on the test set labelled as submission.csv. This submission.csv is entered through the Kaggle competition page.

- Model code of your SAS model (built using SAS code, or the Python/R APIs). This is your model score code (.sas or .sas + ASTORE) and must be emailed to Academic@oz.sas.com

- Please also link your training notebook as part of your submission!

## Submission CSV Evaluation
All entries are evaluated on a final submission CSV file that contains two columns, ID and Predicted. ID represents the unique ID of the testing set and Predicted is the predicted value of the customers donation (continuous variable).

**Note: You may need to rename the column containing the predicted value to match with this structure.**

```
id, Predicted
3932693,	12.35
3932880,	15.47

```

The scoring metric for the Submission CSV is the RMSE.

## SAS Model Code
Along with your submission CSV, you must submit and provide accompanying model files so your submission can be replicated and you demonstrated that you used the SAS Viya procedures to build your model.

The model score code, which is either a .sas file or a combination of .sas &amp; ASTORE. These are scored representations of the model used to score new data.

These files can be emailed to Academic@oz.sas.com with an email titled ""SAS Viya for Learners Submission ###"" where ### is your Kaggle user or your team-name. 
----------------------
# Timeline

## Competition Timeline & Dates

- 8AM 19th July, 2021 - Challenge begins. The test dataset will be revealed on the Kaggle page and activated on the environment. Participants can then submit to the Leaderboard. Notebook and modelling templates will also be shared to help get participants started.

- 6PM 26th July, 2021 - Competition ends and submission deadline.

All deadlines will be AEST (UTC+10) based unless otherwise noted.
----------------------
# Prizes

## Prizes

Participants get a chance to hone their skills and receive a SAS Badge for their resume that can also be displayed on LinkedIn. These are digital badges through Acclaim and help not only display your skills, but link you to prospective employers looking for SAS skills.

There will be two badges offered:
 
A Participants for entering the challenge and making a submission.
![Participants Badge](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F1570418%2F2e74bf1c45d23b8ede6da5f9c5998d28%2FParticipantBadge.png?generation=1593741499565967&alt=media)


A Winner's Badge for the final Top 3 participants or team on the Leaderboard at the end of the challenge.
![Winner's Badge](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F1570418%2Fc14af378f7d501afe09cf97fda8550e6%2FWinnerBadge.png?generation=1593741514430259&alt=media)


An email will be sent to the Top 3 Winners on the Leaderboard from the SAS Academic Team (Academic@oz.sas.com) on Tuesday 27th July. If entering as a Team, all members will receive a Winner's Badge. Note to be eligible, the participant(s) must have registered their Kaggle account with an Australian university student email. Please refer to the Rules for more detail.
----------------------
# SAS Viya For Learners Registration

## Registration 

In order to  to participate in the challenge, you need to register for access to the SAS Viya for Learners environment. This environment is a 24/7, cloud-based environment where you will have access to the SAS Viya analytics platform in order to build models for the challenge.

To register, please visit the following link and sign-up for access:
https://www.sas.com/en_au/events/2021/sas-viya-for-learners-challenge.html

After applying, you should receive an email notice. Please follow the instructions specified in the email notice to navigate into the SAS Viya for Learners environment.
----------------------
# SAS Viya For Learners Resources Portal

## Resources

For the SAS Viya for Learners Challenge, we have created a customised learning portal containing resources to learn how to use the SAS Viya platform. 

To access the portal:
1.	Go to [support.sas.com/myelearn](https://support.sas.com/edu/viewmyelearn.html) and log in to your profile. If you do not currently have a profile, please create one using a link provided on support.sas.com/myelearn.
2.	Once you've logged in to your My Training page, locate the ""To Activate a New Product"" box on the right side of the screen.
3.	Enter the activation code, __*FS00188916252*__ and click Submit.
4.	Review and accept the license agreement.
5.	You should now see the training in your list of active courses
6.	Click on the portal link to access the SAS Viya for Learners resources.

Once you have performed this initial activation, visit [support.sas.com/myelearn](https://support.sas.com/edu/viewmyelearn.html) or select My Training from any page on the SAS training web site and log in to your profile to access the portal.

## Kaggle Introduction

Follow the ""Step-by-Step Guide to Using Viya for Learners for 2021 Kaggle Challenge"" to familiarise yourself with using the Viya platform.","# Dataset Description

## Introduction 

The data set which is to be used in this challenge contains individual records which tracks certain historical donation behaviour as well as certain demographic factors associated with donors. This data set is to be used to train a model which can be used to prioritise which donors in the database are most willing to donate, and therefore of the highest priority to call. 

## Data Overview 

The data contains the following fields:


**DemAge** - Donor's Age
 
**DemCluster** - Donor's Demographic Cluster
 
**DemGender** - Donor's Gender
 
**DemHomeOwner** - Flag indicating if donor owns their primary place of residence
 
**DemMedHomeValue** - Median value of homes in the donor's region
 
**DemMedIncome** - Median income of people living in the donor's region
 
**DemPctVeterans** - Percent of the population in the donor's region who are Military Veterans 
 
**GiftAvg36** - Average donation value from donations in the past 36 months 
 
**GiftAvgAll** - Average donation value from donations across all time
 
**GiftAvgCard36** - Gift Amount Average Card 36 Months
 
**GiftAvgLast** - Donation value from the donors most recent donation
 
**GiftCnt36** - Count of donations made in the last 36 Months
 
**GiftCntAll** - Count of all donations 
 
**GiftCntCard36** - Count of all donations made through mailout cards in the past 36 months
 
**GiftCntCardAll** - Count of all donations made through mailout cards
 
**GiftTimeFirst** - Time Since First Gift
 
**GiftTimeLast** - Time Since Last Gift
 
**ID** - Donor Id
 
**PromCnt12** - Count of promotional materials received in the past 12 Months
 
**PromCnt36** - Count of promotional materials received in the past 36 Months
 
**PromCntAll** - Count of promotional materials received 
 
**PromCntCard12** - Count of promotional cards received in the past 12 Months
 
**PromCntCard36** - Count of promotional cards received in the past 36 Months
 
**PromCntCardAll** - Count of promotional cards received 
 
**StatusCat96NK** - Donor Status Category 
 
**StatusCatStarAll** - Donor Status Category All Months
 
**TARGET_B** - Flag to indicate whether a donation was recieved **Do not use this variable as target or as input. You will not be able to score it, and that entry will be invalid**
 
**TARGET_D** - Value of donation received (no donation set as missing) **Do not use this variable as target or as input. You will not be able to score it, and that entry will be invalid**
 
**TARGET_D_with0** - Value of donation received (no donation set as zero) **This is the target variable to be trained upon**

## Instructions for the Challenge

### Access the Training Data using SAS Viya for Learners Interface

Since the training data is already loaded into the environment, once you have registered into SAS Viya for Learners, you can access the data within the KAGGLE Caslib through the availabile interfaces on Viya For Learners (SAS Studio, Jupiter Notebook, or the visual data science applications available).

### Coding ML models on training data using SAS/Python/R

Using SAS through SAS Studio or Python/R with the SWAT package in JupyterLab, a connection to CAS must first be established. From there you can access the PVA_TRAIN data set and begin training your model. See the Notebooks section for more snippets to get started.

### Generating Submission CSV on Evaluation Data

Kaggle expects the submission CSV to have the ID column to a specific order, when you evaluate your model you need to follow the below steps to generate your submission CSV.

1. After you have trained your model, you must score it on the test data and generate your prediction column, Expected_Donation. Once this column is generated, output the column as a CSV and save it.

2. Download the __submissionId.csv__ file. This is a CSV containing the TODO in the test set in the specified order. 

3. Append your prediction column to the __submissionId.csv__ and save as a new CSV - your predictions should be ready to submit. To see what this file should look like, please refer to the __submissionExample.csv__ file. 

## File Descriptions

* PVA_TRAIN - Training data, already loaded into the KAGGLE Caslib on the environment.

* PVA_SCORE - Test data, already loaded into the KAGGLE Caslib on the environment.

* __submissionExample.csv__ - Example submission 

* __submissionId.csv__ - Submission Id columns required to make the submission",True,True
4488,sliced-s01e05-WXx7h8,"# Description

In this episode of SLICED, contestants are challenged to predict the price of Airbnb listings in NYC.

<p>The&nbsp;evaluation metric for this competition is <a href=""https://www.kaggle.com/wiki/RootMeanSquaredLogarithmicError"">Root Mean Squared Logarithmic Error</a>.</p>
<p>$$<br>\epsilon = \sqrt{\frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n (\log(p_i + 1) - \log(a_i+1))^2 }<br>$$</p>
<p>Using natural log.</p>


<div class=""note"">
<strong>Audience Participation and Prize!</strong><br>
Audience members can follow along, too, during the live show. If you participate, DO NOT CHEAT, e.g., use exploits in the data, use public data. The top audience participant at the end of the show will get a free Kaggle swag and a code to redeem a free NVIDIA Deep Learning Institute training course!
</div>


## How to participate

1. Log in or create a Kaggle account
2. Accept the competition's rules
3. Download the data (click on the ""Data"" tab) or create a notebook directly on Kaggle (click on the ""Code"" tab)
4. Train a model on `train.csv` predicting on `test.csv`
5. Generate a `submission.csv` file in the same format as the `sample_submission.csv`
6. Upload your `submission.csv` file on ""My Submissions""

**You get TEN SUBMISSIONS during the episode. They must be submitted before the end of the two-hour live coding is up.** You can hand select a submission from the ""My Submissions"" tab, otherwise the submission with the best public score (on 1% of the test data) will be taken and scored on the private leader board (on 99% of the test data).

## About SLICED
[SLICED](https://www.notion.so/SLICED-Show-c7bd26356e3a42279e2dfbafb0480073) is like the TV Show Chopped but for data science. Competitors get a never-before-seen dataset and two-hours to code a solution to a prediction challenge. Contestants get points for the best model plus bonus points for data visualization, votes from the audience, and more.

SLICED is possible thanks to support from:

* RStudio
* Streamlit
* NVIDIA
* Kaggle

SLICED is streaming on Twitch Tuesdays at 8:30PM ET for twelve weeks starting June 1st: https://www.twitch.tv/nickwan_datasci. 

## About SLICED Season 1, Episode 5

- **Date**: June 28 at 8:30PM on https://www.twitch.tv/nickwan_datasci
- **Contestants**: Canzhi, Josh, Michael, Craig
- **Winner**: Michael & Josh (TIE!)
- **Audience winner**: Datalab
