4521,sliced-s01e06-2ld97c,"# Description

In this episode of SLICED, contestants are challenged to predict the rank of the top 200 games streamed on Twitch during May 2021.

The evaluation metric for this competition is accuracy. 

NOTE: IN THE EVENT OF A TIE the TIE BREAKER, the EARLIER entry will be considered the ""better"" entry

<div class=""note"">
<strong>Audience Participation and Prize!</strong><br>
Audience members can follow along, too, during the live show. If you participate, DO NOT CHEAT, e.g., use exploits in the data, use public data. The top audience participant at the end of the show will get a free Kaggle swag and a code to redeem a free NVIDIA Deep Learning Institute training course!
</div>


## How to participate

1. Log in or create a Kaggle account
2. Accept the competition's rules
3. Download the data (click on the ""Data"" tab) or create a notebook directly on Kaggle (click on the ""Code"" tab)
4. Train a model on `train.csv` predicting on `test.csv`
5. Generate a `submission.csv` file in the same format as the `sample_submission.csv`
6. Upload your `submission.csv` file on ""My Submissions""

**You get TEN SUBMISSIONS during the episode. They must be submitted before the end of the two-hour live coding is up.** You can hand select a submission from the ""My Submissions"" tab, otherwise the submission with the best public score (on 1% of the test data) will be taken and scored on the private leader board (on 99% of the test data).

## About SLICED
[SLICED](https://www.notion.so/SLICED-Show-c7bd26356e3a42279e2dfbafb0480073) is like the TV Show Chopped but for data science. Competitors get a never-before-seen dataset and two-hours to code a solution to a prediction challenge. Contestants get points for the best model plus bonus points for data visualization, votes from the audience, and more.

SLICED is possible thanks to support from:

* RStudio
* Streamlit
* NVIDIA
* Kaggle

SLICED is streaming on Twitch Tuesdays at 8:30PM ET for twelve weeks starting June 1st: https://www.twitch.tv/nickwan_datasci. 

## About SLICED Season 1, Episode 6

- **Date**: July 6th at 8:30PM on https://www.twitch.tv/nickwan_datasci  
- **Contestants**: Jordan Wilheim, Kyle Ligon, Jesse Mostipak, and Adrian Cadena Medina  
- **Winner**: Jesse
- **Audience winner**: tidyqn
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Submission format

Your submission should contain two columns: `Game` and `Rank`. See `sample_submission.csv` on the ""Data"" tab for an example of what your file should look like. Make a submission by clicking on ""My Submissions"" and uploading your submission file. The evaluation algorithm is accuracy.

**You only get TEN SUBMISSIONS during the episode. They must be submitted before the end of the two-hour live coding is up.** Select your preferred final submission on the ""My Submissions"" tab.","# Dataset Description

In this dataset you can find the top 200 games on Twitch on each month from 2016 to May 2021. 

# File descriptions 
* train.csv - the training set
* test.csv - the test set
* sample_submission.csv - a sample submission file in the correct format

The test set (test.csv) is May 2021. 

# Data dictionary  
**`Rank`**: The rank of a `Game` for the given `Month` and `Year` (ranges from 1 to 200). `Rank` is determined by  `Hours_watched`, where the most `Hours_watched` is `Rank` 1 for the given month + year  

**`Game`**: Name of the game streamed on Twitch. This also contains categories (i.e. ""Just Chatting"")

**`Month`**: Month, numeric 

**`Year`**: Year, numeric 

**`Hours_watched`**: Number of total hours people have watched a given game in the month + year  

**`Hours_Streamed`**: Number of total hours streamers have streamed a given game in the month + year  

**`Peak_viewers`**: Max amount of viewers watching a given game in the month + year  

**`Peak_channels`**: Max amount of channels streaming a given game in the month + year  

**`Streamers`**: Number of streamers who streamed a given game in the month + year  

**`Avg_viewer_ratio`**: The average viewers watching a given game divided by the average channels streaming a given game, both in the same month + year",True,True
