4593,CiVilium,"# Description

<p>
For the longest time in the history of TechX, a mystical cryptocurrency, CiVilium (CiV), has been circulating amongst the Academic Leads. Although its price fluctuates wildly, we hope to discover an underlying pattern in its price change. </p>

Your task is to develop a machine learning model that predicts Civilium's future price trends, thus giving you the power to manipulate CiVilium's market. Whoever gains a monopoly shall rule XAcademy.

<h2>Dataset</h2>
The train.csv file given to you contains the weighted price and traded volume of CiVilium at ~730000 time stamps. You will be tested on test.csv which contains ~310000 data points 

<h2>Recommended libraries</h2>
sklearn
matplotlib

<h2>If you have completely no idea where to start, please see our starter notebook</h2>
----------------------
# Evaluation

# RMSE loss:

Root-Mean-Square-Error or RMSE is one of the most popular measures to estimate the accuracy of our forecasting model¡¯s predicted values versus the actual or observed values while training the regression models or time series models.

It measures the error in our predicted values when the target or response variable is a continuous number. For example, when using regression models to predict a quantity like income, sales value/volumes, demand volumes, scores, height or weight etc.

![](https://miro.medium.com/max/548/0*IN6VnDGeafpUioDN)
