4625,ml4einductions,"# Description

#Hello ML enthusiasts,
##### Through this competition we will be shortlisting candidates for the ML4E induction interview round. For many of you, this might be the first competition that you will be taking part in. The details about the dataset have been mentioned in the Data section. Kindly go through all the details. The evaluation metric for the completion will be the AUC score. All the best !!!

###May the force be with you !!!!
----------------------
# Evaluation

### The evaluation metric will be the ROC-AUC score.
##### You can read more about it from the sklearn documentation here
https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/classes.html#module-sklearn.metrics

## Submission File

The submission file should contain the 'ID' column from the test data set and the corresponding prediction in 'y' column. 

For reference, please take a look at the provided sample_submission.csv file.","# Dataset Description

## The data is related to a banking institution. The target column 'y' has two attributes yes - '1' or no - '0', which tell us if the customer chooses to opt for the product/services offered by the bank
## Input variables:
### 1 - age - numeric
### 2 - job : type of job - categorical: 'admin.','blue-collar','entrepreneur','housemaid','management','retired','self-employed','services','student','technician','unemployed','unknown'
### 3 - Padhai-Contains details about the educational background-categorical: 'basic.4y','basic.6y','basic.9y','high.school','illiterate','professional.course','university.degree','unknown'
### 4 - default: has credit in default? - categorical: 'no','yes','unknown'
### 5- $$$ paisa-bank balance
### 6 - housing: has a housing loan? - categorical: 'no','yes','unknown'
### 7 - loan: has a personal loan? - categorical: 'no','yes','unknown'
### 8 - month: last contact month of year -categorical: 'jan', 'feb', 'mar', ..., 'nov', 'dec'
### 9 - day_of_week: last contact day of the week - categorical: 'mon','tue','wed','thu','fri'
### 10 - duration: last contact duration, in seconds - numeric
### 11 - campaign: number of contacts performed
### 12 - pdays: number of days that passed by after the client was last contacted from a previous campaign - numeric; 999 means client was not previously contacted
### 13 - previous: number of contacts performed before this campaign and for this client - numeric
### 14 - poutcome: outcome of the previous marketing campaign - categorical: 'failure','nonexistent','success'
### 15- ID Column",True,True
