4630,fit5215-s2-2021-animal-classification,"# Description

This is the home page of the competition. This competition is organized for the FIT5215: Deep Learning unit at Monash University. The students who are interested can join in this competition.

If you are in the top 10, you will be awarded *5 points*, while if you are in the top 3, you will be awarded *10 points*. Especially, if you are the winner (i.e., top 1), you will be awarded a *free ML and DL book* (<150 AUDs) of your choice from the teaching team.


Please note that if you are in the top 10, you need to submit a brief document to describe your network and the pre-trained model that obtains the final results leading you to a position in the top 10 leader board.

Hope that you enjoy this competition. Have funs!!
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p></p><h2>Evaluation Metric</h2>
<p>The evaluation metric for this competition is the accuracy </p><p>
</p><h2>Submission Format</h2>
<p><strong>Please follow the file my_solution.csv in the tab Data to submit your result.</strong></p>","# Dataset Description

This page contains the datasets and their information for the FIT5215 animal classification competition. There are three zip and one CSV file as follows:

- **train_dataset**: the labeled training set with 5000 images and ten classes.

- **test_dataset**: the unlabeled testing dataset of images of the size (64, 64, 3).

- **guideline_code**: the template for the CSV  submission file and the code to load and process the testing set together with the code to create a  submitted  CSV file from the model predictions.

- **my_solution.csv**: the template for a submitted file.",True,True
