4642,iiitd-abuse-detection-challenge,"# Description

<p>IEEE BigMM is hosting a grand data challenge to bring together interdisciplinary novel research focused on improving the social space for the members of the community. The focus area for this year is improving abusive comment identification on social media in low-resource Indic languages.</p>

All details [here](https://sharechat.com/events/abuse-detection-challenge).

**NOTE: Teams must register at [this form](https://forms.gle/yTj5RhPQiGwSCyMy5) to be eligible for prizes.**

<p>Moj Multilingual Abusive Comment Identification - Challenge
An innovative new challenge towards combating abusive comments on Moj, one of India's largest short-video apps in multiple regional languages. We invite submissions to a grand challenge, where the goal is to develop AI solutions for predicting abusive comments posted on the Moj app in 10+ languages given natural language data along with contextual user data. Key novelties around this dataset include:</p>

- Massive &amp; Multilungual - 10+ low-resource Indic languages
- human annotated
- Metadata based explicit feedback like #likes, #reports on each comment


<h2>Acknowledgements</h2>
